window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0065", [{"word":"stabilization","ipa_uk":"/ˌsteɪbɪlaɪˈzeɪʃən/","ipa_us":"/ˌsteɪbələˈzeɪʃən/","definition_zh":"稳定；稳定化；使趋于平稳的过程；（经济、政治）稳定措施","definition_en":"the process of making something firm, steady, or unlikely to move, change or fail","core_image":"一名工人把晃动的三脚架逐条腿拧紧，直到水平仪的气泡停在中央","scene":"The central bank's stabilization program slowed inflation within a year.","sceneCN":"这里 stabilization 是「稳定化」（第 2 个义项：用政策手段让价格、货币或经济趋于平稳）；句意：中央银行的稳定化计划在一年内让通胀放缓。图中可辨识物件：三脚架、水平仪气泡、拧紧的旋钮、趋于水平的平台。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"稳定；稳定化；（经济、政治）稳定措施（指过程时多不可数，指多项措施时可用复数 stabilizations）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"price stabilization","zh":"价格稳定"},{"phrase":"economic stabilization","zh":"经济稳定"},{"phrase":"stabilization program","zh":"稳定化计划"},{"phrase":"stabilization fund","zh":"稳定基金"},{"phrase":"macroeconomic stabilization","zh":"宏观经济稳定"},{"phrase":"image stabilization","zh":"图像防抖"},{"phrase":"population stabilization","zh":"人口数量趋于稳定"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多项稳定措施）","form":"stabilizations"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"stabilize（使稳定；稳定下来）"},{"label":"形容词形式","form":"stable（稳定的；牢固的）"},{"label":"名词（性质）","form":"stability（稳定性）"},{"label":"名词（装置或药剂）","form":"stabilizer（稳定器；稳定剂）"},{"label":"反义动词","form":"destabilize（使不稳定；动摇）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"stabilize","pos":"v.","zh":"使稳定；使趋于平稳"},{"word":"stability","pos":"n.","zh":"稳定性；稳固"},{"word":"stabilizer","pos":"n.","zh":"稳定器；稳定剂"},{"word":"destabilize","pos":"v.","zh":"使不稳定；动摇"},{"word":"instability","pos":"n.","zh":"不稳定；不稳固"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The act of making something steady","titleCN":"稳定化：使某物趋于稳固的过程","definition":"the process of making something firm, steady, or less likely to move, change or fail","definitionCN":"使某物变得稳固、平稳、不易移动、变化或失败的过程","example":"The stabilization of the scaffolding took two hours before the painters climbed up.","exampleCN":"为了让油漆工登上去，脚手架的加固稳定花了两个小时。","why":"Latin stabilis meant 'firm, steadfast', and the noun ending -ation names the action of producing that state, so the word begins with the picture of something wobbling and being held still.","whyCN":"拉丁 stabilis 意为「稳固的、坚定的」，名词词尾 -ation 命名制造这种状态的动作，因此词义起点是「某物在晃、被扶稳」的画面。"},{"no":"02","title":"Policy action that steadies an economy","titleCN":"经济稳定化：用政策稳住价格与货币","definition":"the use of official policy, such as interest rates or fiscal measures, to keep prices, currency or output from swinging sharply","definitionCN":"运用利率、财政措施等官方政策，使价格、货币或产出不出现剧烈波动的做法","example":"The stabilization program combined tight spending with a fixed exchange rate.","exampleCN":"这项稳定化计划把紧缩开支与固定汇率结合在一起。","why":"In the twentieth century governments and international lenders turned the general idea of steadying into a named policy package, so stabilization came to mean the measures themselves, especially after wartime inflation.","whyCN":"二十世纪，各国政府与国际贷款机构把「稳住」这一一般概念变成有名称的政策组合，于是 stabilization 开始指这些措施本身，尤其在战时通胀之后。"},{"no":"03","title":"Restoring order to a government or region","titleCN":"政治稳定化：恢复政权或地区的秩序","definition":"the process of bringing a government, region or institution back to order after unrest, conflict or collapse","definitionCN":"在动荡、冲突或崩溃之后，使政府、地区或机构恢复秩序的过程","example":"The peace mission focused on political stabilization rather than reconstruction.","exampleCN":"这支和平使团把重点放在政治稳定，而不是重建。","why":"Because a state can wobble like a structure, the same noun was extended from physical steadiness to the steadiness of public order, a use that became common in diplomacy.","whyCN":"国家也会像结构物一样摇晃，于是同一个名词从物理上的稳固扩展到公共秩序的稳固，这一用法在外交领域变得常见。"},{"no":"04","title":"Reinforcing a building, slope or bridge","titleCN":"结构加固：让建筑、坡体或桥梁不再失稳","definition":"engineering work that makes a structure or a mass of ground able to stand without shifting or collapsing","definitionCN":"使建筑物或土体能够站住、不位移、不坍塌的工程处理","example":"Slope stabilization with concrete anchors prevented a landslide above the road.","exampleCN":"用混凝土锚杆进行的坡体加固防止了公路上方的滑坡。","why":"This is the oldest physical sense applied to large objects: the thing is given the firmness that Latin stabilis named, and the noun describes the work that produces it.","whyCN":"这是最古老的物理义项在大尺度物体上的应用：对象被赋予拉丁 stabilis 所指的稳固，名词则描述产生这种稳固的工程。"},{"no":"05","title":"Bringing a patient to a safe condition","titleCN":"医疗稳定：把病人的生命体征拉到安全范围","definition":"the medical process of bringing a patient's breathing, blood pressure and heart rate to a level that is safe enough for further treatment","definitionCN":"把病人的呼吸、血压与心率调整到足以接受后续治疗的安全水平的医疗过程","example":"The paramedics achieved stabilization before moving the injured climber.","exampleCN":"急救人员在搬运受伤的登山者之前先完成了生命体征稳定。","why":"A body in crisis is described as unstable, so the act of holding its vital signs within safe limits takes the same noun; the metaphor treats physiology as a system that can be propped up.","whyCN":"处于危机的身体被称为不稳定，因此把生命体征维持在安全范围内的动作沿用同一个名词；这一比喻把生理状态看作可以被支撑住的系统。"},{"no":"06","title":"Treating a substance so it does not change","titleCN":"化学稳定：处理物质使其不易变质或反应","definition":"the treatment of a chemical or material so that it resists decay, separation or unwanted reaction","definitionCN":"对化学品或材料进行处理，使其不易腐败、分离或发生不需要的反应","example":"The stabilization of the vaccine required a strict cold chain.","exampleCN":"疫苗的稳定化处理需要严格的冷链。","why":"Chemists borrowed the word because a compound that decomposes is literally not standing firm; adding a stabilizer makes its bonds hold, and the process is called stabilization.","whyCN":"化学家借用这个词，是因为会分解的化合物字面上就「站不稳」；加入稳定剂让化学键保持住，这一过程便称为稳定化。"},{"no":"07","title":"Removing jitter from an image or signal","titleCN":"图像或信号防抖：消除抖动与漂移","definition":"the reduction of unwanted shake or drift in a camera image, a recording or a stream of data","definitionCN":"减少相机画面、录音或数据流中不需要的抖动或漂移","example":"Optical stabilization keeps handheld video smooth at long focal lengths.","exampleCN":"光学防抖让长焦段的手持视频保持平稳。","why":"This technical sense keeps the core image almost literally: a shaking frame is steadied, and the noun names the mechanism or the correction, not the physical support.","whyCN":"这一技术义项几乎字面保留核心意象：晃动的画面被稳住，名词指机制或校正，而不是物理支撑。"},{"no":"08","title":"A population that stops growing","titleCN":"人口稳定：数量停止增长并保持水平","definition":"the point at which births and deaths balance so that a population stops rising and holds roughly level","definitionCN":"出生与死亡达到平衡、人口停止上升并大致保持水平的状态","example":"Demographers expect global population stabilization later this century.","exampleCN":"人口学家预计全球人口将在本世纪后期趋于稳定。","why":"Here the thing being held level is a number rather than an object, an extension of the same idea of stopping a movement, common in demography and ecology.","whyCN":"这里被保持在水平线上的是数字而不是物体，仍是「止住某种移动」这一思路的延伸，常见于人口学与生态学。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Stabilization is an English noun of action built on the verb stabilize, whose base is Latin stabilis 'firm', from stare 'to stand'. The dates below are approximate.","cn":"stabilization 是英语动作名词，建立在动词 stabilize 之上；其词基为拉丁 stabilis「稳固的」，出自 stare「站立」。以下年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN STABILIS","en":"Latin stabilis meant 'firm, steadfast, able to stand'. It is an adjective in -bilis built on stare 'to stand', a root shared by status, station and constant.","cn":"拉丁 stabilis 意为「稳固的、坚定的、站得住的」，是加 -bilis 的形容词，建立在 stare「站立」之上；status、station、constant 共享这个词根。"},{"era":"LATIN STABILIRE","en":"The verb stabilire 'to make firm, establish' is attested in Latin and supplies the action behind the English verb. Its past participle stabilis is the source of the adjective.","cn":"动词 stabilire「使稳固、确立」在拉丁文献中有记录，为英语动词提供动作基础；其分词形式与形容词 stabilis 同源。"},{"era":"FRENCH AND ENGLISH VERB","en":"French stabiliser and English stabilize appear in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries, built on the adjective with the verb suffix -ize.","cn":"法语 stabiliser 与英语 stabilize 分别出现在十八、十九世纪，由形容词加动词词尾 -ize 构成。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ACTION NOUN","en":"Stabilization adds -ation, the noun-of-action ending that reached English through French. It names the act of stabilizing rather than the state, which is stability.","cn":"stabilization 加上了经法语进入英语的动作名词词尾 -ation，命名「使稳定」的动作，而不是状态；状态由 stability 表示。"},{"era":"TWENTIETH-CENTURY POLICY","en":"The economic and political senses became fixed in the twentieth century through phrases such as stabilization fund, stabilization program and macroeconomic stabilization.","cn":"经济与政治义项在二十世纪通过 stabilization fund、stabilization program、macroeconomic stabilization 等短语固定下来。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"The exact first English citation of stabilization is uncertain. The deeper root of stare is reconstructed as Indo-European *sta-, so the form is a reconstruction rather than a recorded word.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：stabilization 的英语最早书证年代不明。stare 的更深词根被重构为印欧语 *sta-，属重构形式，而非有记录的真实词形。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates members of the same Latin family that differ in part of speech; the second gives near-synonyms for the result or the process.","cn":"第一组区分同一拉丁词族中词性不同的成员；第二组给出表示结果或过程的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"stability","ipa":"/stəˈbɪləti/","tag":"noun of state","definition":"The state of being steady. You can measure the stability of a bridge, but stabilization is the work done to produce it.","definitionCN":"指稳固的状态：可以测量桥的稳定性，而 stabilization 是产生这种稳定性所做的工作。"},{"word":"stabilize","ipa":"/ˈsteɪbəlaɪz/","tag":"verb","definition":"The verb meaning to make or become steady; stabilization is the corresponding action noun.","definitionCN":"动词，意为使稳定或变得稳定；stabilization 是相应的动作名词。"},{"word":"stable","ipa":"/ˈsteɪbəl/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Describes a thing that stands firm; it is the quality word, not the process word.","definitionCN":"形容词，描述站得稳的事物；它是性质词，不是过程词。"},{"word":"stabilizer","ipa":"/ˈsteɪbəlaɪzə/","tag":"device or additive","definition":"The object that produces steadiness, such as a camera stabilizer or a chemical additive; stabilization is the process, not the object.","definitionCN":"指产生稳定效果的物件，如相机稳定器或化学稳定剂；stabilization 是过程，不是物件。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"consolidation","ipa":"/kənˌsɒlɪˈdeɪʃən/","tag":"making solid or unified","definition":"The act of combining parts into one solid whole. Stabilization keeps something from moving; consolidation makes it one body.","definitionCN":"把各部分合并成一个坚固整体的动作：stabilization 让某物不再移动，consolidation 让它成为一个整体。"},{"word":"equilibrium","ipa":"/ˌiːkwɪˈlɪbriəm/","tag":"balanced state","definition":"A state in which opposing forces cancel. It is a condition that can exist without any action, while stabilization implies an effort to reach it.","definitionCN":"指相反力量相互抵消的状态；这种状态可以自然存在，而 stabilization 隐含达到它的努力。"},{"word":"security","ipa":"/sɪˈkjʊərəti/","tag":"freedom from danger","definition":"Protection from threat, especially military or financial. It is broader and more subjective than the technical steadiness of stabilization.","definitionCN":"指免受威胁，尤指军事或金融方面；它比 stabilization 的技术性「平稳」更宽泛、更主观。"},{"word":"steadiness","ipa":"/ˈstedinəs/","tag":"plain quality","definition":"The everyday quality of not shaking or changing. It is close to stability but lacks the technical and policy senses of stabilization.","definitionCN":"日常意义上的「不晃、不变」，接近 stability，但没有 stabilization 的技术与政策义项。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"stable + -ize + -ation: first make steady, then name the making.","cn":"stable + -ize + -ation：先使稳固，再为「使稳固」这一动作命名。"},{"en":"The family runs stable, stability, stabilize, stabilizer, instability, destabilize.","cn":"同族词包括 stable、stability、stabilize、stabilizer、instability、destabilize。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the policy sense: stabilization program, stabilization fund, price stabilization, macroeconomic stabilization.","cn":"固定搭配标出政策义项：稳定化计划、稳定基金、价格稳定、宏观经济稳定。"},{"en":"A camera lens advertises image stabilization; a central bank advertises price stabilization.","cn":"相机镜头宣传图像防抖，中央银行宣传价格稳定，二者用的是同一个词。"},{"en":"Stability is the state; stabilization is the work; a stabilizer is the tool.","cn":"stability 是状态，stabilization 是工作过程，stabilizer 是工具。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a tower of blocks wobbling and a hand pressing the top flat.","cn":"想象一堆积木在摇晃，一只手把顶部压平。"},{"en":"Picture a climbing line on a chart that suddenly turns into a horizontal rule.","cn":"想象图表上一条攀升的线突然变成水平直线。"},{"en":"Picture a ship's gyroscope holding the deck level while the sea moves.","cn":"想象船用陀螺仪在波涛中让甲板保持水平。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The stabilization of the currency required both higher interest rates and spending cuts.","cn":"货币的稳定化既需要提高利率，也需要削减开支。"},{"en":"Engineers completed the slope stabilization before the rainy season began.","cn":"工程师在雨季开始前完成了坡体加固。"},{"en":"Optical stabilization lets a handheld camera take sharp pictures in dim light.","cn":"光学防抖让手持相机在弱光下也能拍出清晰照片。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「stable（稳的）+ ization」——把晃动的东西扶稳 → stabilization 稳定化","word":"stabilization"},"root":"拉丁 stabilis「稳固的」（出自 stare「站立」）→ 拉丁 stabilire「使稳固」→ 法语 stabiliser → 英语 stabilize + -ation。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one idea at different scales: a tripod steadied, a currency held level, a region restored to order, a slope anchored, a patient kept alive, a compound kept from decaying, a frame kept from shaking, and a population that stops growing.","cn":"八个义项是同一思路在不同尺度上的展开：扶稳三脚架、稳住货币、恢复地区秩序、锚固坡体、维持病人生命、防止化合物变质、让画面不抖，以及人口停止增长。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a wobbling object is caught and held level.","cn":"核心意象：晃动的物体被抓住并保持在水平线上。"},"chain":["WOBBLE","GRIP IT","ANCHOR THE FRAME","KEEP A NUMBER LEVEL","RESTORE PUBLIC ORDER","HOLD A CONDITION STEADY"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1","en":"PLAIN ACTION: any effort that turns a shaky thing into a firm one.","cn":"一般动作：任何把摇晃之物变为稳固之物的努力。"},{"senses":"S2 · S8","en":"HOLDING A QUANTITY FLAT: prices, currency and population stop swinging or rising.","cn":"把数量压平：价格、货币与人口停止波动或上升。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"ORDER IN A STATE: public authority is restored after unrest.","cn":"国家秩序：动荡之后恢复公共权威。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"PHYSICAL SUPPORT: ground, bridges and buildings are anchored so they cannot fail.","cn":"物理支撑：土体、桥梁与建筑被锚固，因而不致失稳。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6 · S7","en":"FRAGILE SYSTEMS: vital signs, chemical bonds and image frames are kept from failing or drifting.","cn":"脆弱系统：生命体征、化学键与画面帧被维持住，不致崩溃或漂移。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Stabilization is layered: a Latin adjective of standing firm, a Latin verb of making firm, an English verb in -ize, and the action-noun ending -ation.","cn":"stabilization 是分层构成的：表示「站得稳」的拉丁形容词，表示「使稳固」的拉丁动词，加 -ize 的英语动词，以及动作名词词尾 -ation。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin stabilis and stabilire come from stare 'to stand', the root behind stable, stability, constant, status and station; the noun ending -atio reached English as -ation through French.","cn":"拉丁 stabilis 与 stabilire 出自 stare「站立」，这一词根也见于 stable、stability、constant、status、station；名词词尾 -atio 经法语进入英语作 -ation。"},"items":[{"word":"stabilization","structure":"stabilize + -ation (action noun)","meaning":"the act of making steady","meaningCN":"使趋于稳固的动作","example":"Currency stabilization was the first goal of the new government.","exampleCN":"货币稳定是新政府的首要目标。"},{"word":"stabilize","structure":"stable + -ize (to make)","meaning":"to make or become steady","meaningCN":"使稳定；稳定下来","example":"Doctors worked to stabilize the patient's breathing.","exampleCN":"医生努力稳定病人的呼吸。"},{"word":"stable","structure":"Latin stabilis (firm)","meaning":"firm and unlikely to move","meaningCN":"稳固的；不易移动的","example":"The table felt stable once the fourth leg was fitted.","exampleCN":"装上第四条腿后，桌子就稳了。"},{"word":"stability","structure":"stable + -ity (quality noun)","meaning":"the quality of being steady","meaningCN":"稳固的性质","example":"Political stability encouraged foreign investment.","exampleCN":"政治稳定吸引了外国投资。"},{"word":"stabilizer","structure":"stabilize + -er (agent noun)","meaning":"a device or substance that keeps something steady","meaningCN":"保持稳定的装置或物质","example":"A stabilizer in the fuel prevents it from separating.","exampleCN":"燃料中的稳定剂防止其分层。"},{"word":"instability","structure":"in- (not) + stability","meaning":"lack of steadiness","meaningCN":"不稳定的状态","example":"Currency instability made long-term planning difficult.","exampleCN":"货币不稳定使长期规划变得困难。"},{"word":"destabilize","structure":"de- (reverse) + stabilize","meaning":"to make unsteady or undermine","meaningCN":"使不稳定；动摇","example":"Rumors can destabilize a fragile government.","exampleCN":"谣言能动摇一个脆弱的政府。"},{"word":"destabilization","structure":"destabilize + -ation","meaning":"the act of making something unsteady","meaningCN":"使不稳定的行为","example":"The report warned of regional destabilization.","exampleCN":"报告警告了地区动荡的风险。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"stabilis","structure":"stabilis, stabile (adjective, third declension)","meaning":"firm, steadfast, standing fast","meaningCN":"稳固的；坚定的；站得住的"},{"word":"stabilire","structure":"stabilis + -ire (verb of making)","meaning":"to make firm, establish","meaningCN":"使稳固；确立"},{"word":"-atio","structure":"-atio, -ationis (f., action noun)","meaning":"suffix naming an action or its result","meaningCN":"命名动作或其结果的词尾"}]}},{"word":"standardized","ipa_uk":"/ˈstændədaɪzd/","ipa_us":"/ˈstændɚdaɪzd/","definition_zh":"标准化的；按统一标准制作或检验的；规范化的；（贬义）千篇一律的","definition_en":"made to conform to an agreed standard, or measured and judged against one","core_image":"一排原本长短不一的螺丝被同一把卡尺逐个量过，最后整齐地落进同一个量规","scene":"All the parts were standardized so that any replacement would fit.","sceneCN":"这里 standardized 是「按统一标准制作的」（第 1 个义项：零件遵循同一规格而可互换）；句意：所有零件都已标准化，任何替换件都能装上。图中可辨识物件：卡尺、量规、同一规格的螺丝、装件盒。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"标准化的；按统一标准制作或检验的；规范化的；（贬义）千篇一律的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"standardized test","zh":"标准化考试"},{"phrase":"standardized score","zh":"标准化分数"},{"phrase":"standardized procedure","zh":"标准化程序"},{"phrase":"standardized measurement","zh":"标准化测量"},{"phrase":"standardized parts","zh":"标准化零件"},{"phrase":"standardized format","zh":"标准化格式"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more standardized（更标准化的）"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most standardized（最标准化的）"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"standardize（使标准化；统一规格）"},{"label":"名词（过程）","form":"standardization（标准化）"},{"label":"名词兼形容词","form":"standard（标准；标准的）"},{"label":"否定形式","form":"nonstandard（非标准的）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"standardize","pos":"v.","zh":"使标准化；统一规格"},{"word":"standardization","pos":"n.","zh":"标准化；规格统一"},{"word":"standard","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"标准；标准的"},{"word":"substandard","pos":"adj.","zh":"低于标准的；不合格的"},{"word":"nonstandard","pos":"adj.","zh":"非标准的；不规范的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Made to one agreed specification","titleCN":"按统一规格制作","definition":"made to a common size, design or specification so that one item can replace another","definitionCN":"按共同的尺寸、设计或规格制作，使一件物品可以替换另一件","example":"Standardized containers cut the cost of loading ships.","exampleCN":"标准化集装箱降低了装船成本。","why":"Standard first named a fixed rallying point and later an authorized model; adding -ize turns that model into a verb, and the past participle describes whatever has been made to match it.","whyCN":"standard 最初指固定的集结点，后指权威认定的范型；加 -ize 把这个范型变成动词，过去分词则描述已被做成与之一致的事物。"},{"no":"02","title":"Scored against a fixed test standard","titleCN":"按固定标准评分：标准化考试","definition":"of a test or score, designed, administered and graded in the same way for every candidate so that results can be compared","definitionCN":"指测试或分数按同一方式设计、实施与评分，使不同考生的结果可以比较","example":"The university accepts either the national standardized test or its own exam.","exampleCN":"这所大学接受全国标准化考试，也接受本校自设考试。","why":"Comparability is the point: if every candidate meets the same procedure and the same scoring key, the differences in score reflect differences in performance rather than differences in the test.","whyCN":"关键在于可比性：如果每位考生面对同一程序与同一评分标准，分数的差异就反映表现差异，而不是测试本身的差异。"},{"no":"03","title":"Calibrated against a reference","titleCN":"依基准标定：校准过的仪器或量值","definition":"of an instrument or measurement, checked against a known reference so that its readings can be trusted","definitionCN":"指仪器或测量已对照已知基准进行校验，因而读数可信","example":"Only standardized thermometers were used in the temperature trial.","exampleCN":"温度试验中只使用了经过标定的温度计。","why":"Metrology treats the standard as the authority; a standardized instrument is one whose readings have been tied to that authority, which is a narrower, technical version of sense one.","whyCN":"计量学把标准视为权威；standardized 仪器就是读数已与该权威挂钩的仪器，这是第 1 个义项在计量领域的更窄用法。"},{"no":"04","title":"Brought into a common format","titleCN":"统一格式：数据与记录规范化","definition":"of data, records or documents, converted into a common layout and set of fields so that they can be merged or compared","definitionCN":"指数据、记录或文件被转换为共同的版式与字段，以便合并或比较","example":"The clinics standardized their forms before linking the databases.","exampleCN":"各家诊所在连接数据库之前统一了表格格式。","why":"The metaphor moves from physical parts to information: a form that follows one standard can be read by the same machine or clerk as any other form.","whyCN":"这一比喻从实体零件转向信息：按同一标准制作的表格，能和其他表格一样被同一台机器或同一位职员读取。"},{"no":"05","title":"Following a fixed procedure","titleCN":"按固定程序执行","definition":"of a procedure or protocol, written down and followed in the same order every time so that results are reproducible","definitionCN":"指程序或规程被写下来，每次按同样顺序执行，使结果可以复现","example":"The lab adopted a standardized procedure for storing samples.","exampleCN":"实验室采用了标准化的样本保存程序。","why":"A procedure becomes a standard when it stops depending on individual habit; the participle marks the state of having been brought under that rule.","whyCN":"当程序不再依赖个人习惯时，它就成为标准；过去分词标记「已被纳入该规则」的状态。"},{"no":"06","title":"Made uniform in spelling or usage","titleCN":"写法或用法统一","definition":"of spelling, terminology or usage, reduced to one accepted form where several variants once existed","definitionCN":"指拼写、术语或用法在曾有多种变体的情况下被归并为一种被接受的形式","example":"Standardized spelling made the dictionary usable across regions.","exampleCN":"统一的拼写让这部词典在各地区都能使用。","why":"Printing and schooling needed one form per word; the same authority that fixes a measure can fix a spelling, so the participle extends to language.","whyCN":"印刷与学校教育需要每个词只有一种写法；能确定度量标准的权威也能确定拼写，于是过去分词扩展到语言领域。"},{"no":"07","title":"Made routine and interchangeable","titleCN":"流程化、可互换","definition":"of work, services or systems, organized into identical repeatable units so that people and parts can be swapped in and out","definitionCN":"指工作、服务或系统被组织成相同的可重复单元，使人与零件可以随时替换","example":"Standardized shifts allowed nurses to move between wards.","exampleCN":"标准化班次让护士可以在不同病区之间调动。","why":"Standardization removes local variation on purpose; what remains is a unit that fits anywhere, which is efficient and also the source of the pejorative sense that follows.","whyCN":"标准化有意消除地方差异，剩下的是随处可用的单元；这带来效率，也正是随后贬义义的来源。"},{"no":"08","title":"Uniform to the point of blandness","titleCN":"千篇一律：失去个性的统一","definition":"used with disapproval, describing housing, schooling or products that are so uniform that individuality and local character are lost","definitionCN":"带贬义，描述住房、教育或产品过于统一，以致个性与地方特色消失","example":"Critics called the new district standardized and soulless.","exampleCN":"批评者称这个新城区千篇一律、没有灵魂。","why":"Once the word spreads from parts to people's lives, the virtue of fitting in becomes the vice of being indistinguishable, and the participle acquires this critical tone.","whyCN":"当这个词从零件扩展到人的生活，「适配」的优点就变成「难以区分」的缺点，过去分词由此带上批评语气。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Standardized is an English formation: the noun standard, the verb suffix -ize and the past-participle ending -ed. Standard itself is not Latin but came through Old French, and its deeper origin is disputed.","cn":"standardized 是英语内部构成：名词 standard、动词词尾 -ize 与过去分词词尾 -ed。standard 本身并非源自拉丁，而是经古法语进入英语，其更深来源有争议。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD FRENCH ESTANDART","en":"Old French estandart named a rallying flag or banner, the sign around which troops gathered. English borrowed the word in the thirteenth century.","cn":"古法语 estandart 指集结用的旗帜或军旗，即部队聚拢所围绕的标志。英语在十三世纪借入该词。"},{"era":"FRANKISH RECONSTRUCTION","en":"The Old French form is generally believed to come from a Frankish compound reconstructed as *standhard, 'stand firm', from *standan 'to stand' and *hard 'hard, firm'. The starred form is a reconstruction, not a recorded word.","cn":"一般认为古法语形式来自法兰克语复合词，被重构为 *standhard「站稳」，由 *standan「站立」与 *hard「坚硬、牢固」构成。带星号的形式是重构，并非有记录的真实词形。"},{"era":"SENSE SHIFT TO MEASURE","en":"By the eighteenth century standard meant an authorized rule or model against which things are judged, a sense that developed from the fixed rallying point. The precise path and date are uncertain.","cn":"到十八世纪，standard 已指权威规则或范型，用来评判事物；这一义项由固定的集结点发展而来，但确切路径与年代不确定。"},{"era":"VERB STANDARDIZE","en":"Standardize is an English verb of the nineteenth century, formed from standard plus -ize. It first described making weights, measures and parts conform to one model.","cn":"standardize 是十九世纪的英语动词，由 standard 加 -ize 构成，最初描述让度量衡与零件符合同一范型。"},{"era":"PAST PARTICIPLE AS ADJECTIVE","en":"The participle standardized spread in the twentieth century with mass production, national testing and digital records, and it took on the critical sense of 'made blandly uniform'.","cn":"过去分词 standardized 随大规模生产、全国性考试与数字记录在二十世纪流行，并获得「被弄得千篇一律」的批评义。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertainty (root): the deeper origin of standard is undecided, and Frankish *standhard is a reconstructed form. First-attestation uncertainty: no exact year is known for the earliest English use of standardize or standardized. No Latin source can be confirmed, so latinEntries is left empty.","cn":"来源不确定（词根）：standard 的更深词源没有定论，法兰克语 *standhard 属重构形式。首见年代存疑：standardize 与 standardized 的英语最早书证均无确定年份。本词无法确证拉丁来源，故拉丁词条留空。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the standard family by part of speech and level; the second gives near-synonyms for uniformity.","cn":"第一组按词性与层级区分 standard 词族；第二组给出表示「统一」的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"standard","ipa":"/ˈstændəd/","tag":"noun or adjective","definition":"The rule or model itself, or an adjective meaning 'normal and accepted'. Standardized describes something that has been made to match the standard.","definitionCN":"指规则或范型本身，也可作形容词表示「通常被接受的」；standardized 描述已被做成符合该标准的事物。"},{"word":"standardize","ipa":"/ˈstændədaɪz/","tag":"verb","definition":"The act of bringing things to one standard; standardized is the resulting state.","definitionCN":"把事物统一到某一标准的动作；standardized 是由此形成的状态。"},{"word":"standardization","ipa":"/ˌstændədaɪˈzeɪʃən/","tag":"process noun","definition":"The process itself. Standardized is the adjective for what has undergone that process.","definitionCN":"指过程本身；standardized 是经历了该过程之后的形容词。"},{"word":"substandard","ipa":"/ˌsʌbˈstændəd/","tag":"below the standard","definition":"Falling short of the required standard. It judges quality, while standardized only says which standard was applied.","definitionCN":"指低于要求的标准，评判的是质量；standardized 只说明采用了哪一标准。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"uniform","ipa":"/ˈjuːnɪfɔːm/","tag":"all the same","definition":"The same in form throughout. It describes the sameness itself, not the act of imposing a standard.","definitionCN":"指整体形式相同，描述的是相同性本身，而不是施加标准的动作。"},{"word":"consistent","ipa":"/kənˈsɪstənt/","tag":"not varying","definition":"Behaving or appearing the same from one case to the next. It stresses reliability over a series, not conformity to a written rule.","definitionCN":"指一个个案例之间表现一致，强调跨系列的可靠性，而非符合书面规则。"},{"word":"normalized","ipa":"/ˈnɔːməlaɪzd/","tag":"scaled to a common base","definition":"Adjusted to a common scale or baseline, especially in data and diplomacy. It is a technical cousin of standardized.","definitionCN":"指调整到共同尺度或基线，尤其用于数据与外交；它是 standardized 的技术性近亲。"},{"word":"interchangeable","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈtʃeɪndʒəbəl/","tag":"fit for swapping","definition":"Able to be put in place of one another. It states the practical result of standardization, not the act.","definitionCN":"指可以互相替换，说明标准化带来的实际结果，而不是动作。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"standard + -ize + -ed: first set the model, then make things match it.","cn":"standard + -ize + -ed：先立范型，再让事物与之一致。"},{"en":"The family runs standard, standardize, standardization, substandard, nonstandard.","cn":"同族词包括 standard、standardize、standardization、substandard、nonstandard。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the range: standardized test, standardized score, standardized procedure, standardized parts.","cn":"固定搭配标出范围：标准化考试、标准化分数、标准化程序、标准化零件。"},{"en":"A standard is a flag troops rally around; standardized parts all snap into the same slot.","cn":"standard 原指部队聚拢的旗帜；standardized 零件则都能卡进同一个槽位。"},{"en":"The word improves parts and can belittle places: standardized bolts are good, standardized suburbs are dull.","cn":"这个词既能夸零件，也能贬地方：标准化螺栓很好，标准化郊区很乏味。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a row of screws measured by one caliper and dropped into one gauge.","cn":"想象一排螺丝被同一把卡尺量过，落进同一个量规。"},{"en":"Picture many different doors cut to one keyhole size.","cn":"想象许多不同的门都被改成同一个锁孔尺寸。"},{"en":"Picture a town where every street sign uses the same font and the same grey wall.","cn":"想象一座小镇，所有路牌用同一字体，所有墙是同一种灰色。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Standardized shipping containers changed world trade more than any single ship design.","cn":"标准化集装箱对世界贸易的改变超过任何单一船型的设计。"},{"en":"The researchers used a standardized questionnaire to compare the two groups.","cn":"研究人员使用标准化问卷来比较两组人群。"},{"en":"Residents complained that the new housing was standardized and had lost all local character.","cn":"居民抱怨新住房千篇一律，失去了所有地方特色。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「standard（标准）+ ized」——被同一把尺子量过一遍 → standardized 标准化的","word":"standardized"},"root":"英语 standard（源出古法语 estandart「军旗、集结点」，一般认为来自法兰克语重构形式 *standhard「站稳」）+ -ize + -ed；非拉丁来源，latinEntries 留空。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses move from physical parts to testing, instruments, data, procedures, spelling, work routines and finally to the critical sense of a life made too uniform.","cn":"八个义项从实体零件依次扩展到考试、仪器、数据、程序、拼写、工作班次，最后落到「生活被弄得过于统一」的批评义。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: many uneven pieces are measured against one gauge until they match.","cn":"核心意象：许多不齐的零件被同一个量规量到彼此一致。"},"chain":["FIX THE MODEL","MEASURE EACH PIECE","MAKE THEM FIT","SHARE ONE FORMAT","REPEAT THE PROCEDURE","LOSE LOCAL VARIATION"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S3","en":"PHYSICAL CONFORMITY: parts and instruments are matched or calibrated to one reference.","cn":"物理一致：零件与仪器被做成或校准到同一基准。"},{"senses":"S2","en":"FAIR COMPARISON: one test procedure lets different candidates be ranked on the same scale.","cn":"公平比较：同一考试程序让不同考生在同一尺度上排序。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"INSTITUTIONAL ROUTINE: forms and protocols follow one layout and one order.","cn":"制度常规：表格与规程遵循同一版式、同一顺序。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"ONE ACCEPTED FORM: spelling and terminology are reduced to a single variant.","cn":"唯一被接受的形式：拼写与术语被归并为一种变体。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"SWAPPABLE UNITS AND THEIR COST: work becomes interchangeable, and places lose character.","cn":"可互换单元及其代价：工作变得可互换，地方则失去特色。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Standardized is standard plus the verb suffix -ize plus the past-participle ending -ed, which here works as an adjective ending meaning 'having been made so'.","cn":"standardized 由 standard 加动词词尾 -ize、再加过去分词词尾 -ed 构成；此处 -ed 作形容词词尾，意为「已被做成那样」。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Standard has no confirmed Latin source: it came through Old French from a Frankish form reconstructed as *standhard. Because the Latin line cannot be confirmed, no latinEntries are listed.","cn":"standard 没有可确证的拉丁来源：它经古法语来自被重构为 *standhard 的法兰克语形式。由于无法确证拉丁来源，本词条不列拉丁词条。"},"items":[{"word":"standardized","structure":"standardize + -ed (past participle adjective)","meaning":"made to conform to a standard","meaningCN":"已被做成符合某一标准的","example":"The clinic uses standardized intake forms.","exampleCN":"该诊所使用标准化的接诊表格。"},{"word":"standardize","structure":"standard + -ize (to make)","meaning":"to bring things to one standard","meaningCN":"使事物统一到某一标准","example":"The alliance agreed to standardize radio frequencies.","exampleCN":"联盟同意统一无线电频率。"},{"word":"standardization","structure":"standardize + -ation (action noun)","meaning":"the process of making uniform","meaningCN":"使统一的过程","example":"Standardization of the bolts lowered repair costs.","exampleCN":"螺栓的标准化降低了维修成本。"},{"word":"standard","structure":"Old French estandart (banner, rallying point)","meaning":"an accepted rule or model","meaningCN":"被接受的规则或范型","example":"The agency sets the standard for drinking water.","exampleCN":"该机构制定饮用水标准。"},{"word":"substandard","structure":"sub- (below) + standard","meaning":"below the required standard","meaningCN":"低于规定标准的","example":"Substandard wiring caused the fire.","exampleCN":"不合格的电线引发了火灾。"},{"word":"nonstandard","structure":"non- (not) + standard","meaning":"not conforming to the standard","meaningCN":"不符合标准的","example":"Nonstandard dialects are still fully grammatical.","exampleCN":"非标准方言同样完全合乎语法。"},{"word":"standardizer","structure":"standardize + -er (agent noun)","meaning":"a person or body that standardizes","meaningCN":"推行标准化的人或机构","example":"The standardizer must consult the workers who use the tools.","exampleCN":"标准化推行者必须咨询实际使用工具的人。"},{"word":"standard-bearer","structure":"standard (banner) + bearer","meaning":"one who carries the flag, or a leading representative","meaningCN":"旗手；某一事业的代表者","example":"She became the standard-bearer of the reform movement.","exampleCN":"她成为这场改革运动的旗手。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"statistical","ipa_uk":"/stəˈtɪstɪkəl/","ipa_us":"/stəˈtɪstɪkəl/","definition_zh":"统计的；统计学的；以统计数据为依据的","definition_en":"relating to statistics, or based on numerical data gathered from many cases rather than on single examples","core_image":"一张巨大的表格被折成柱状图，成百上千的个人点数收拢成几根高低不同的柱子","scene":"The report offered statistical evidence that the policy had cut waiting times.","sceneCN":"这里 statistical 是「统计的、以数据为依据的」（第 2 个义项：用汇总数字而非个案来说明问题）；句意：报告给出了政策缩短等待时间的统计证据。图中可辨识物件：表格、柱状图、样本点、误差线。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"统计的；统计学的；以统计数据为依据的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"statistical analysis","zh":"统计分析"},{"phrase":"statistical significance","zh":"统计显著性"},{"phrase":"statistical method","zh":"统计方法"},{"phrase":"statistical data","zh":"统计数据"},{"phrase":"statistical inference","zh":"统计推断"},{"phrase":"statistical error","zh":"统计误差"},{"phrase":"statistical population","zh":"统计总体"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more statistical（更具统计性质的）"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most statistical（最具统计性质的）"},{"label":"副词形式","form":"statistically（在统计上；从统计角度看）"},{"label":"名词（学科）","form":"statistics（统计学；统计数据）"},{"label":"名词（单个数值）","form":"statistic（统计量；一项数据）"},{"label":"名词（从业者）","form":"statistician（统计学家；统计员）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"statistics","pos":"n.","zh":"统计学；统计数据"},{"word":"statistic","pos":"n.","zh":"统计量；一项统计数据"},{"word":"statistician","pos":"n.","zh":"统计学家；统计员"},{"word":"statistically","pos":"adv.","zh":"在统计上；从统计角度"},{"word":"biostatistics","pos":"n.","zh":"生物统计学"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Belonging to the discipline of statistics","titleCN":"属于统计学这一学科","definition":"relating to statistics as a branch of mathematics that collects, summarizes and analyses data","definitionCN":"与作为数学分支的统计学有关，该学科收集、汇总并分析数据","example":"Her statistical training let her detect a flaw in the sampling design.","exampleCN":"她的统计学训练使她发现了抽样设计中的缺陷。","why":"The adjective simply marks membership in the field: anything taught in a statistics course, from distributions to estimators, can be called statistical.","whyCN":"这个形容词只是标记「属于该领域」：统计学课程里讲授的内容，从分布到估计量，都可以称为 statistical。"},{"no":"02","title":"Based on aggregated numbers","titleCN":"以汇总数据为依据","definition":"resting on numbers collected from many cases and summarized, rather than on one person's experience","definitionCN":"建立在从许多案例收集并汇总的数字之上，而不是依据某个人的经历","example":"Statistical evidence linked seat-belt laws to fewer road deaths.","exampleCN":"统计数据把安全带立法与道路死亡人数下降联系起来。","why":"Statistics began as the science of the state's numbers; the adjective therefore signals evidence at the level of a population, where individual stories become counts.","whyCN":"statistics 最初是研究「国家数据」的学问，因此这个形容词标示的是人口层面的证据，个人的故事在这里变成计数。"},{"no":"03","title":"Unlikely to be due to chance","titleCN":"达到统计显著性：不太可能出于偶然","definition":"of a result, large enough relative to random variation that it is unlikely to have arisen by chance alone","definitionCN":"指结果相对于随机波动足够大，单靠偶然出现的可能性很低","example":"The difference was statistical at the five percent level.","exampleCN":"这一差异在百分之五的水平上具有统计显著性。","why":"Statisticians compare an observed difference with the spread that chance would produce; when the gap is large against that spread, the result earns the label statistical in this evaluative sense.","whyCN":"统计学家把观察到的差异与偶然会造成的变化幅度相比较；当差距相对于该幅度足够大时，结果就在这种评价意义上获得 statistical 的标签。"},{"no":"04","title":"Estimating from a sample","titleCN":"由样本推断总体","definition":"of inference or probability, concerned with drawing conclusions about a whole from a limited sample","definitionCN":"指推断或概率，关注如何从有限样本对整个总体得出结论","example":"Statistical inference turned the survey of two thousand voters into a forecast.","exampleCN":"统计推断把两千名选民调查变成了预测。","why":"Because we rarely measure everyone, statistical reasoning works by assigning probabilities to claims about the unmeasured remainder; the adjective names that bridge from part to whole.","whyCN":"因为我们很少能测量所有人，统计推理就通过给关于未测部分的判断分配概率来工作；这个形容词命名的正是「由部分到整体」的桥梁。"},{"no":"05","title":"Averaged over countless particles","titleCN":"物理学中的统计方法：对大量粒子取平均","definition":"of mechanics or thermodynamics, describing the behaviour of a system through averages over very many particles rather than through each one","definitionCN":"指力学或热力学，通过大量粒子的平均行为而不是逐个粒子来描述系统","example":"Statistical mechanics explains why a gas fills its container.","exampleCN":"统计力学解释了气体为何会充满容器。","why":"Physics borrowed the word because tracking every molecule is impossible; temperature and pressure are statistical facts, meaningful only as averages.","whyCN":"物理学借用这个词，因为追踪每一个分子是不可能的；温度与压强都是统计性事实，只有作为平均值才有意义。"},{"no":"06","title":"The group being measured","titleCN":"被测量的总体或样本","definition":"of a population or sample, referring to the complete set or the subset from which data are drawn","definitionCN":"指总体或样本，即数据所取自的完整集合或其中的子集","example":"The statistical population included every adult in the county.","exampleCN":"统计总体包括该县每一位成年人。","why":"Before any number can be computed, the statistician must define the group; the adjective marks that group as the object of measurement rather than as everyday 'people'.","whyCN":"在计算任何数字之前，统计学家必须先界定群体；这个形容词把该群体标记为测量对象，而不是日常意义上的「人们」。"},{"no":"07","title":"Random variation, not a mistake","titleCN":"统计误差：随机波动，而非操作错误","definition":"of error, the unavoidable scatter produced by sampling and randomness, as opposed to a blunder in measurement","definitionCN":"指误差，即抽样与随机性造成的不可避免的离散，而不是测量中的操作失误","example":"Statistical error in the poll was plus or minus three points.","exampleCN":"民调的统计误差为正负三个百分点。","why":"This sense corrects a common confusion: statistical error is a property of the method, whereas a mistake is a failure of the person, so the adjective separates noise from fault.","whyCN":"这一义项纠正常见混淆：统计误差是方法本身的属性，而错误是人的失误；形容词由此把「噪声」与「过错」区分开。"},{"no":"08","title":"Odds attached to one case","titleCN":"个案身上的统计概率","definition":"describing the probability that a particular person or event falls into a risk category, as calculated from group data","definitionCN":"指依据群体数据计算出的、某个具体人或事件落入某一风险类别的概率","example":"Insurers price policies by the statistical risk of each age group.","exampleCN":"保险公司按各年龄组的统计风险为保单定价。","why":"Group data can be applied back to individuals as odds; this sense is where statistical language enters insurance, medicine and everyday risk talk.","whyCN":"群体数据可以被反过来作为概率用于个人；正是在这一义项上，统计语言进入保险、医学与日常的风险讨论。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Statistical is the adjective of statistics, a word coined in eighteenth-century German academia from New Latin statisticum and Latin status 'state, condition'. The adjective marks 'of state data' before it marks 'of mathematical methods'.","cn":"statistical 是 statistics 的形容词；statistics 由十八世纪德国学界用新拉丁 statisticum 与拉丁 status「国家、状态」造出。这个形容词先表示「关于国家数据的」，后表示「关于数学方法的」。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN STATUS","en":"Latin status meant 'condition, position, state', from stare 'to stand'. It supplied the word for the commonwealth, the state, and also for the standing of affairs that officials wished to count.","cn":"拉丁 status 意为「状况、地位、国家」，出自 stare「站立」。它既提供「国家」一词，也指官员想要统计的「事务状况」。"},{"era":"NEW LATIN STATISTICUM","en":"In seventeenth- and eighteenth-century German universities, statisticum collegium named a course on the affairs of the state, gathering facts about population, trade and territory.","cn":"在十七、十八世纪的德国大学里，statisticum collegium 指讲授国家事务的课程，收集人口、贸易与领土方面的事实。"},{"era":"GERMAN STATISTIK","en":"Achenwall's lectures of 1749 fixed Statistik as the name of this descriptive science of state facts, which is generally credited with launching the modern word.","cn":"阿亨瓦尔 1749 年的讲座把 Statistik 固定为这门描述国家事实的学问之名，一般认为现代这个词由此发端。"},{"era":"ENGLISH STATISTICS","en":"English adopted statistics in the late eighteenth century, at first for state facts and only later for the mathematical treatment of numerical data.","cn":"英语在十八世纪末借入 statistics，最初指国家事实，后来才指对数值数据的数学处理。"},{"era":"STATISTICAL","en":"The adjective statistical was formed on statistics and broadened in the nineteenth and twentieth centuries to cover probability, sampling and physics.","cn":"形容词 statistical 由 statistics 构成，并在十九、二十世纪扩展到概率、抽样与物理学。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"The exact first English citation of statistical is uncertain. The Latin root status is clear, but the deeper Indo-European form *sta- is a reconstruction rather than a recorded word.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：statistical 的英语最早书证年代不确定。拉丁词根 status 清楚，但更深的印欧语形式 *sta- 是重构形式，并非有记录的真实词形。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the statistics family by part of speech; the second gives near-synonyms for data-based reasoning.","cn":"第一组按词性区分 statistics 词族；第二组给出表示「以数据为依据」的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"statistics","ipa":"/stəˈtɪstɪks/","tag":"noun, the field","definition":"The discipline, or the body of data. Statistical is the adjective describing what belongs to it.","definitionCN":"指学科或数据整体；statistical 是描述「属于它」的形容词。"},{"word":"statistic","ipa":"/stəˈtɪstɪk/","tag":"single number","definition":"One computed value such as a mean. The singular is countable; statistics as a subject is not.","definitionCN":"指一个计算出来的数值，如平均数；单数可数，而作为学科的 statistics 不可数。"},{"word":"statistician","ipa":"/ˌstætɪˈstɪʃən/","tag":"person","definition":"The person who analyses data. The adjective statistical describes the work, not the worker.","definitionCN":"指分析数据的人；形容词 statistical 描述工作，而非工作者。"},{"word":"statistically","ipa":"/stəˈtɪstɪkli/","tag":"adverb","definition":"The adverb answering 'in what terms?' or 'by what measure?'. Statistical modifies a noun; statistically modifies a verb or adjective.","definitionCN":"副词，回答「从什么角度」「用什么度量」；statistical 修饰名词，statistically 修饰动词或形容词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"numerical","ipa":"/njuːˈmerɪkəl/","tag":"expressed in numbers","definition":"Given in numbers rather than words. It does not imply that the numbers were sampled or tested.","definitionCN":"指用数字而非文字表达，并不隐含这些数字经过抽样或检验。"},{"word":"quantitative","ipa":"/ˈkwɒntɪtətɪv/","tag":"measured by amount","definition":"Concerned with quantities rather than qualities. It is broader than statistical, which specifically involves inference from data.","definitionCN":"指关注数量而非性质，比 statistical 更宽泛，后者具体涉及由数据作出推断。"},{"word":"probabilistic","ipa":"/ˌprɒbəbɪˈlɪstɪk/","tag":"in terms of probability","definition":"Expressed as a likelihood. Statistical results are often probabilistic, but probabilistic models need not use measured samples.","definitionCN":"指以可能性来表达；统计结果常是概率性的，但概率模型并不一定使用实测样本。"},{"word":"actuarial","ipa":"/ˌæktʃuˈeəriəl/","tag":"insurance mathematics","definition":"Relating to the risk tables of insurers. It is a specialised application of statistical method to life and property risk.","definitionCN":"指与保险公司的风险表有关，是统计方法在人身与财产风险上的专门应用。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"statistics + -al: of the discipline that turns cases into counts.","cn":"statistics + -al：属于那门把个案变成计数的学科。"},{"en":"The family runs statistic, statistics, statistician, statistically, biostatistics.","cn":"同族词包括 statistic、statistics、statistician、statistically、biostatistics。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases show the range: statistical analysis, statistical significance, statistical inference, statistical error.","cn":"固定搭配展示范围：统计分析、统计显著性、统计推断、统计误差。"},{"en":"A single case is an anecdote; a thousand cases become a statistic, and the method becomes statistical.","cn":"一个个案是轶事，上千个个案成为统计量，方法也就成为 statistical。"},{"en":"Statistical error is noise, not a blunder; keep the two apart.","cn":"统计误差是噪声而不是失误，要把两者分开。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a crowd of faces collapsing into a few coloured bars.","cn":"想象一群面孔收拢成几根彩色柱子。"},{"en":"Picture a net thrown over a river: it catches a sample, not the whole river.","cn":"想象一张网撒向河流：它捕到的是样本，不是整条河。"},{"en":"Picture a bell-shaped hill with two small tails marked 'unlikely'.","cn":"想象一座钟形山丘，两端各有一条标着「不太可能」的小尾巴。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The paper's statistical analysis controlled for age and income.","cn":"这篇论文的统计分析对年龄与收入作了控制。"},{"en":"No statistical method can rescue a badly designed sample.","cn":"再好的统计方法也救不了一个设计糟糕的样本。"},{"en":"Statistical mechanics treats heat as the average motion of huge numbers of molecules.","cn":"统计力学把热视为大量分子运动的平均值。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「statistics（统计）+ al」——看汇总数字而不是看个人 → statistical 统计的","word":"statistical"},"root":"拉丁 status「国家、状态」（出自 stare「站立」）→ 新拉丁 statisticum「国家事务讲座」→ 德语 Statistik → 英语 statistics + -al。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses range from the discipline itself to aggregated evidence, significance testing, sampling, physics, the measured population, random error and personal odds.","cn":"八个义项从学科本身，延伸到汇总证据、显著性检验、抽样、物理学、被测量的总体、随机误差与个人风险概率。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: many individual points are folded into a few summarizing bars.","cn":"核心意象：许多个别的数据点被折成少数几根概括性的柱子。"},"chain":["COUNT THE STATE","SUM THE CASES","COMPARE WITH CHANCE","INFER THE WHOLE","AVERAGE THE PARTICLES","PRICE ONE CASE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1","en":"THE DISCIPLINE: the whole toolkit of collecting, summarizing and testing data.","cn":"学科整体：收集、汇总与检验数据的整套工具。"},{"senses":"S2 · S6","en":"THE MEASURED GROUP: evidence and the defined population from which it comes.","cn":"被测量的群体：证据本身，以及证据所来自的被界定总体。"},{"senses":"S3 · S7","en":"CHANCE AND NOISE: results are judged against random scatter, and scatter is not blamed on the researcher.","cn":"偶然与噪声：结果要对照随机离散来评判，而离散不应归咎于研究者。"},{"senses":"S4 · S8","en":"FROM SAMPLE TO CASE: conclusions about a whole, then odds applied back to one person.","cn":"从样本到个案：先对整体下结论，再把概率反用于某个人。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"MANY-PARTICLE LIMIT: temperature and pressure exist only as averages over enormous numbers.","cn":"多粒子极限：温度与压强只作为极大量粒子的平均值而存在。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Statistical is statistics plus the adjective ending -al. The base statistics is a German academic coinage resting on New Latin statisticum, itself built on Latin status.","cn":"statistical 是 statistics 加形容词词尾 -al。词基 statistics 是德国学界的造词，建立在新拉丁 statisticum 之上，后者又由拉丁 status 构成。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin line runs status 'state, condition' from stare 'to stand', then New Latin statisticum 'of state affairs', then German Statistik and English statistics.","cn":"拉丁线索是 status「国家、状态」（出自 stare「站立」）→ 新拉丁 statisticum「与国家事务有关的」→ 德语 Statistik → 英语 statistics。"},"items":[{"word":"statistical","structure":"statistics + -al (relating to)","meaning":"relating to statistics","meaningCN":"与统计学有关的","example":"The journal requires a statistical review of every trial.","exampleCN":"该期刊要求对每项试验进行统计审查。"},{"word":"statistics","structure":"German Statistik, from New Latin statisticum","meaning":"the science of data, or a body of data","meaningCN":"数据科学；一批数据","example":"The statistics show a steady rise in enrolment.","exampleCN":"统计数据显示入学人数稳步上升。"},{"word":"statistic","structure":"back-formation from statistics","meaning":"a single computed value","meaningCN":"一个计算出的数值","example":"The mean is the simplest statistic in the table.","exampleCN":"平均数是表中最简单的统计量。"},{"word":"statistician","structure":"statistics + -ian (person)","meaning":"one who works with statistics","meaningCN":"从事统计工作的人","example":"A statistician checked the sampling plan.","exampleCN":"一位统计学家检查了抽样方案。"},{"word":"statistically","structure":"statistical + -ly (manner adverb)","meaning":"in statistical terms","meaningCN":"从统计角度；在统计上","example":"The two groups were statistically equivalent at the start.","exampleCN":"两组在开始时统计上相当。"},{"word":"stats","structure":"informal clipping of statistics","meaning":"figures used in casual speech","meaningCN":"口语中的统计数字","example":"Check the player's stats before the match.","exampleCN":"赛前先看看这名球员的数据。"},{"word":"biostatistics","structure":"bio- (life) + statistics","meaning":"statistics applied to living things","meaningCN":"应用于生物的统计学","example":"Biostatistics guides the design of clinical trials.","exampleCN":"生物统计学指导临床试验的设计。"},{"word":"vital statistics","structure":"fixed phrase: vital (of life) + statistics","meaning":"official figures on births, deaths and marriages","meaningCN":"关于出生、死亡与婚姻的官方数据","example":"Vital statistics recorded a falling birth rate.","exampleCN":"生命统计记录了出生率下降。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"status","structure":"status, status (m., fourth declension)","meaning":"condition, position, state","meaningCN":"状况；地位；国家"},{"word":"statisticum","structure":"New Latin, from status","meaning":"of state affairs","meaningCN":"与国家事务有关的"},{"word":"-alis","structure":"-alis, -ale (adjective suffix)","meaning":"suffix meaning 'belonging to'","meaningCN":"表示「属于……」的形容词词尾"}]}},{"word":"statistically","ipa_uk":"/stəˈtɪstɪkli/","ipa_us":"/stəˈtɪstɪkli/","definition_zh":"统计上；从统计角度看；在统计意义下","definition_en":"in terms of statistics, or by the methods and standards of statistical analysis","core_image":"两支几乎重合的曲线落在同一条误差带里，标尺显示两者的差距不足以判定不同","scene":"Statistically, the two treatments performed the same.","sceneCN":"这里 statistically 是「从统计角度看」（第 1 个义项：依据统计方法判断，而非凭印象）；句意：从统计上看，两种疗法的效果相同。图中可辨识物件：误差带、重叠区间、标尺、两条几乎重合的曲线。","pos":[{"tag":"adv.","zh":"统计上；从统计角度看；在统计意义下"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"statistically significant","zh":"统计上显著的"},{"phrase":"statistically indistinguishable","zh":"统计上无法区分的"},{"phrase":"statistically representative","zh":"在统计上具有代表性的"},{"phrase":"statistically speaking","zh":"从统计角度来说"},{"phrase":"statistically likely","zh":"统计上很可能的"},{"phrase":"statistically negligible","zh":"统计上可忽略的"},{"phrase":"statistically valid","zh":"统计上有效的"}],"forms":[{"label":"形容词形式","form":"statistical（统计的）"},{"label":"名词（学科）","form":"statistics（统计学）"},{"label":"名词（数值）","form":"statistic（统计量）"},{"label":"名词（从业者）","form":"statistician（统计学家）"},{"label":"比较级","form":"more statistically（更从统计角度地）"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most statistically（最从统计角度地）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"statistical","pos":"adj.","zh":"统计的；统计学的"},{"word":"statistics","pos":"n.","zh":"统计学；统计数据"},{"word":"statistician","pos":"n.","zh":"统计学家"},{"word":"statistic","pos":"n.","zh":"统计量；一项数据"},{"word":"biostatistics","pos":"n.","zh":"生物统计学"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"By statistical methods","titleCN":"以统计方法判断","definition":"in a way that uses statistical methods or rests on summarized numerical evidence","definitionCN":"以使用统计方法或依据汇总数值证据的方式","example":"Statistically, the survey is the best evidence we have.","exampleCN":"从统计上看，这次调查是我们手上最好的证据。","why":"The adverb -ly turns the adjective into a standpoint: the speaker asks the listener to judge the claim by counting and probability rather than by impression.","whyCN":"副词词尾 -ly 把形容词变成一种立场：说话人要求听者用计数与概率而不是凭印象来判断这一说法。"},{"no":"02","title":"At the threshold of significance","titleCN":"达到统计显著：差距大到不像偶然","definition":"used with significant, meaning that the observed difference is large enough relative to random variation to be unlikely by chance","definitionCN":"与 significant 连用，表示观察到的差异相对于随机波动足够大，不太可能出于偶然","example":"The new drug lowered blood pressure statistically significantly.","exampleCN":"新药在统计上显著降低了血压。","why":"This is the most common use in research writing: the adverb tells the reader that the result passed a pre-set probability test, not that the effect was large in daily life.","whyCN":"这是研究写作中最常见的用法：副词告诉读者结果通过了预设的概率检验，并不表示效果在日常生活中很大。"},{"no":"03","title":"In terms of calculated probability","titleCN":"从计算出的概率看","definition":"used to state how likely something is according to probability calculated from data","definitionCN":"用于说明依据数据计算出的概率，某事有多大的可能性","example":"Statistically, a passenger is safer in a bus than in a car.","exampleCN":"从统计概率看，乘客坐公交车比坐小汽车更安全。","why":"Here the adverb shifts the frame from one journey to many journeys, so that risk is read off a distribution rather than off a single event.","whyCN":"这里副词把视角从一次行程移到许多次行程，于是风险是从分布上读出的，而不是从单一事件读出的。"},{"no":"04","title":"With no detectable difference","titleCN":"统计上无法区分","definition":"used with words such as indistinguishable or equivalent, meaning that the data show no difference large enough to detect","definitionCN":"与 indistinguishable、equivalent 等词连用，表示数据显示不出足够大的差异","example":"The two samples were statistically indistinguishable.","exampleCN":"这两个样本在统计上无法区分。","why":"Statistically here marks a limit of evidence, not a proof of sameness: the method cannot separate the cases, which is a different claim from saying they are identical.","whyCN":"这里的 statistically 标记证据的极限，而不是证明相同：方法无法把两者分开，这与「它们完全相同」是不同的主张。"},{"no":"05","title":"As a representative sample","titleCN":"在统计上具有代表性","definition":"used of a sample, meaning that its composition matches the larger population closely enough for inference","definitionCN":"用于样本，表示其构成与更大总体足够接近，可以进行推断","example":"The panel was statistically representative of the electorate.","exampleCN":"这个小组在统计上代表了全体选民。","why":"Representativeness is a statistical property, not a moral one; the adverb says the sample was checked against known proportions of the population.","whyCN":"代表性是一种统计属性，而不是道德属性；副词说明该样本已对照总体的已知比例作过检验。"},{"no":"06","title":"As a way of framing a claim","titleCN":"从统计角度来说（话语标记）","definition":"used as a discourse marker to announce that the following statement is a statistical generalization rather than a personal observation","definitionCN":"作话语标记，提示接下来的陈述是统计概括，而不是个人观察","example":"Statistically speaking, most errors happen in the first week.","exampleCN":"从统计角度来说，大多数错误发生在第一周。","why":"The phrase softens and frames: it warns the listener that exceptions exist, while asserting that the pattern holds across the counted cases.","whyCN":"这个短语起缓冲与框定作用：它提醒听者存在例外，同时断言这一模式在被计数的案例中成立。"},{"no":"07","title":"On average, in the typical case","titleCN":"按平均值、在典型情况下","definition":"in the average case, as opposed to an extreme or atypical one","definitionCN":"在平均值情形下，而不是在极端或非典型情形下","example":"Statistically, the average household spends a fifth of its income on housing.","exampleCN":"从统计平均看，普通家庭把五分之一的收入花在住房上。","why":"Averages hide variation, and the adverb signals that the statement is about the middle of a distribution, where no single family need actually sit.","whyCN":"平均值会掩盖差异，这个副词提示该陈述针对分布的中间位置，而未必有任何一个家庭真的处在那里。"},{"no":"08","title":"Too small to matter in practice","titleCN":"统计上可忽略：效应小到无实际意义","definition":"used of an effect or risk, meaning that it is measurably present but so small that it can be disregarded in practice","definitionCN":"用于效应或风险，表示它在测量上确实存在，但小到在实际中可忽略","example":"The added risk was statistically negligible.","exampleCN":"增加的风险在统计上可忽略不计。","why":"This sense separates statistical existence from practical importance: a difference can be real in the data and still be too small to act on.","whyCN":"这一义项把「统计上存在」与「实际重要」分开：差异在数据中可能真实存在，却仍小到不值得采取行动。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Statistically is statistical plus the native adverb ending -ly, whose Old English ancestor -lice marked manner. Statistical itself rests on statistics, a German academic coinage from New Latin statisticum and Latin status.","cn":"statistically 是 statistical 加本族副词词尾 -ly，其古英语前身 -lice 标记方式。statistical 又建立在 statistics 之上，后者是德国学界由新拉丁 statisticum 与拉丁 status 构成的造词。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN STATUS","en":"Latin status 'condition, state' comes from stare 'to stand' and gives the whole family its base.","cn":"拉丁 status「状况、国家」出自 stare「站立」，为整个词族提供词基。"},{"era":"GERMAN STATISTIK","en":"Statistik was fixed in 1749 as the name of the descriptive science of state facts; English statistics followed late in the century.","cn":"Statistik 在 1749 年被固定为描述国家事实的学问之名；英语 statistics 在该世纪后期跟进。"},{"era":"STATISTICAL","en":"The adjective statistical was formed on statistics and later applied to probability and sampling.","cn":"形容词 statistical 由 statistics 构成，后来应用于概率与抽样。"},{"era":"ADVERB SUFFIX","en":"The Old English suffix -lice, later -ly, formed manner adverbs from adjectives; English applied it freely to statistical once the adjective existed.","cn":"古英语后缀 -lice（后为 -ly）由形容词构成方式副词；statistical 一旦存在，英语便自由地加上这一词尾。"},{"era":"RESEARCH USAGE","en":"In the twentieth century statistically fixed its collocations in research writing, above all statistically significant, and later statistically indistinguishable and statistically negligible.","cn":"二十世纪，statistically 在研究写作中固定了搭配，最重要的是 statistically significant，后来又出现 statistically indistinguishable 与 statistically negligible。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"The exact first English citation of statistically is uncertain. The deeper root of stare is reconstructed as Indo-European *sta-, a reconstruction rather than a recorded form.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：statistically 的英语最早书证年代不确定。stare 的更深词根被重构为印欧语 *sta-，属重构形式，并非有记录的真实词形。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the statistics family by part of speech; the second gives near-synonyms for the standpoint the adverb marks.","cn":"第一组按词性区分 statistics 词族；第二组给出与该副词所标立场相近的说法。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"statistical","ipa":"/stəˈtɪstɪkəl/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Describes a noun, such as a method or a result. Statistically describes how a verb is done or how a claim is framed.","definitionCN":"修饰名词，如方法或结果；statistically 描述动作怎样完成或主张如何被框定。"},{"word":"statistics","ipa":"/stəˈtɪstɪks/","tag":"noun","definition":"The field or the data. It cannot stand where the adverb stands.","definitionCN":"指学科或数据，不能出现在副词的位置上。"},{"word":"statistic","ipa":"/stəˈtɪstɪk/","tag":"single value","definition":"One computed number. The adverb never names a number; it names a way of judging.","definitionCN":"指一个计算出的数值；副词从不命名数字，而是命名判断方式。"},{"word":"statistician","ipa":"/ˌstætɪˈstɪʃən/","tag":"person","definition":"The analyst. Statistically refers to the method the analyst uses, not the analyst.","definitionCN":"指分析者；statistically 指分析者所用的方法，而不是分析者本人。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"numerically","ipa":"/njuːˈmerɪkli/","tag":"in numbers","definition":"Expressed as figures. It does not say whether the figures were sampled or tested.","definitionCN":"指以数字表达，并不说明这些数字是否经过抽样或检验。"},{"word":"quantitatively","ipa":"/ˈkwɒntɪtətɪvli/","tag":"by amount","definition":"In terms of quantity rather than quality. It is broader and less technical than statistically.","definitionCN":"指从数量而非性质角度，比 statistically 更宽泛、更不技术化。"},{"word":"probabilistically","ipa":"/ˌprɒbəbɪˈlɪstɪkli/","tag":"by likelihood","definition":"In terms of probability. A model can be probabilistic without using measured data, so the words are not interchangeable.","definitionCN":"指从概率角度；模型可以是概率性的而不使用实测数据，因此两者不能随意互换。"},{"word":"on average","ipa":"/ɒn ˈævərɪdʒ/","tag":"typical case","definition":"The everyday phrase for the middle of a distribution; it matches the 'typical case' sense but not the significance sense.","definitionCN":"指分布中间的日常说法；它对应「典型情况」义项，但不对应显著性义项。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"statistical + -ly: judge the claim by the numbers.","cn":"statistical + -ly：用数字来判断这一说法。"},{"en":"The family runs statistics, statistic, statistician, statistical, biostatistics.","cn":"同族词包括 statistics、statistic、statistician、statistical、biostatistics。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases carry the sense: statistically significant, statistically indistinguishable, statistically speaking.","cn":"固定搭配承载词义：统计显著、统计上无法区分、从统计角度来说。"},{"en":"A result can be statistically real and still too small to matter.","cn":"结果可以在统计上真实存在，却仍小到不重要。"},{"en":"Statistically answers 'by what measure?', not 'how much?'","cn":"statistically 回答「用什么度量判断」，而不是「有多少」。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture two curves lying inside the same error band.","cn":"想象两条曲线落在同一条误差带里。"},{"en":"Picture a coin flipped a thousand times instead of once.","cn":"想象一枚硬币被掷一千次，而不是一次。"},{"en":"Picture a ruler whose smallest mark is labelled 'not enough evidence'.","cn":"想象一把尺子，最小的刻度标着「证据不足」。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Statistically, the two schools differ by less than one point.","cn":"从统计上看，两所学校的差距不到一分。"},{"en":"The treatment worked statistically, though few patients noticed a change.","cn":"该疗法在统计上有效，尽管很少有病人感到变化。"},{"en":"Statistically speaking, the risk rises sharply after the age of sixty.","cn":"从统计角度来说，风险在六十岁之后急剧上升。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「statistical（统计的）+ ly」——拿数字说话 → statistically 从统计上看","word":"statistically"},"root":"拉丁 status「国家、状态」（出自 stare「站立」）→ 新拉丁 statisticum → 德语 Statistik → 英语 statistics → statistical + -ly。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses cover the plain standpoint, the significance threshold, calculated odds, undetectable difference, representative sampling, discourse framing, the average case and practical negligibility.","cn":"八个义项覆盖：一般统计立场、显著性门槛、计算出的概率、无法检出的差异、代表性抽样、话语框定、平均情形，以及实际可忽略性。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two results sit inside one error band, and the ruler decides whether they differ.","cn":"核心意象：两个结果落在同一条误差带里，由标尺决定它们是否不同。"},"chain":["COUNT CASES","SUMMARIZE","TEST AGAINST CHANCE","FRAME THE CLAIM","READ THE AVERAGE","DISMISS THE TINY EFFECT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1","en":"THE STANDPOINT: judge by data and method rather than by impression.","cn":"立场：用数据与方法判断，而不是凭印象。"},{"senses":"S2","en":"THE SIGNIFICANCE LINE: the difference passes a pre-set chance test.","cn":"显著性界线：差异通过了预设的偶然性检验。"},{"senses":"S3 · S5","en":"ODDS AND REPRESENTATION: probability read from a distribution, and a sample that mirrors it.","cn":"概率与代表性：从分布读出的概率，以及与之相称的样本。"},{"senses":"S4 · S6","en":"LIMITS OF EVIDENCE: no detectable difference, and a framing phrase that admits exceptions.","cn":"证据的限度：检不出差异，以及承认例外的框定说法。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"THE MIDDLE VERSUS THE TRIVIAL: the average case, and an effect too small to act on.","cn":"中间情形与微不足道：平均情形，以及小到无需行动的效应。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Statistically is a three-layer English word: statistics from German and New Latin, the adjective ending -al, and the native manner-adverb ending -ly.","cn":"statistically 是三层构成的英语词：来自德语与新拉丁的 statistics，形容词词尾 -al，以及本族方式副词词尾 -ly。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin element is status 'state, condition', from stare 'to stand', carried into New Latin statisticum and then into German and English.","cn":"其中的拉丁成分是 status「国家、状况」，出自 stare「站立」，经新拉丁 statisticum 进入德语与英语。"},"items":[{"word":"statistically","structure":"statistical + -ly (manner adverb)","meaning":"in statistical terms","meaningCN":"从统计角度；在统计上","example":"The groups did not differ statistically.","exampleCN":"各组在统计上没有差异。"},{"word":"statistical","structure":"statistics + -al (relating to)","meaning":"relating to statistics","meaningCN":"与统计有关的","example":"The survey has a statistical appendix.","exampleCN":"该调查附有统计附录。"},{"word":"statistics","structure":"German Statistik, from New Latin statisticum","meaning":"the data science","meaningCN":"数据科学；统计学","example":"Statistics is required for the degree.","exampleCN":"该学位要求修统计学。"},{"word":"statistic","structure":"back-formation from statistics","meaning":"one computed value","meaningCN":"一个统计数值","example":"Goals per game is a useful statistic.","exampleCN":"每场进球数是一项有用的统计量。"},{"word":"statistician","structure":"statistics + -ian (person)","meaning":"a statistics specialist","meaningCN":"统计专业人员","example":"The statistician questioned the sample size.","exampleCN":"统计学家质疑样本量。"},{"word":"stats","structure":"informal clipping","meaning":"figures in casual speech","meaningCN":"口语中的统计数字","example":"The coach checked the stats at halftime.","exampleCN":"教练在半场时查看了数据。"},{"word":"biostatistics","structure":"bio- (life) + statistics","meaning":"statistics for living systems","meaningCN":"用于生命系统的统计学","example":"Biostatistics sets the rules for trial analysis.","exampleCN":"生物统计学为试验分析设定规则。"},{"word":"statistical significance","structure":"fixed phrase: statistical + significance","meaning":"the probability threshold for a result","meaningCN":"结果所通过的概率门槛","example":"The finding reached statistical significance.","exampleCN":"该发现达到统计显著。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"status","structure":"status, status (m., fourth declension)","meaning":"condition, state, position","meaningCN":"状况；状态；地位"},{"word":"statisticum","structure":"New Latin, from status","meaning":"of state affairs","meaningCN":"与国家事务有关的"},{"word":"-alis","structure":"-alis, -ale (adjective suffix)","meaning":"belonging to","meaningCN":"属于……的"}]}},{"word":"stimulation","ipa_uk":"/ˌstɪmjʊˈleɪʃən/","ipa_us":"/ˌstɪmjəˈleɪʃən/","definition_zh":"刺激；激发；兴奋作用；（经济）刺激措施","definition_en":"the act of arousing, exciting or increasing the activity of something","core_image":"一根细针轻触马腹，马向前迈步；同一画面旁边是一只被点亮的灯泡","scene":"Gentle electrical stimulation helped the injured nerve recover.","sceneCN":"这里 stimulation 是「对神经的电刺激」（第 4 个义项：用电流等方式激发神经或肌肉活动）；句意：温和的电刺激帮助受伤神经恢复。图中可辨识物件：电极、神经示意线、脉冲波形、恢复中的肌肉。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"刺激；激发；兴奋作用；（经济）刺激措施（指过程时多不可数，指多种刺激时可用复数 stimulations）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"electrical stimulation","zh":"电刺激"},{"phrase":"sensory stimulation","zh":"感官刺激"},{"phrase":"economic stimulation","zh":"经济刺激"},{"phrase":"nerve stimulation","zh":"神经刺激"},{"phrase":"brain stimulation","zh":"脑刺激"},{"phrase":"stimulation of growth","zh":"对生长的促进"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多种刺激）","form":"stimulations"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"stimulate（刺激；激发）"},{"label":"名词（刺激物）","form":"stimulus（刺激物；刺激因素；复数 stimuli）"},{"label":"形容词（令人兴奋的）","form":"stimulating（令人振奋的；起刺激作用的）"},{"label":"名词（兴奋剂）","form":"stimulant（兴奋剂；刺激物）"},{"label":"形容词（刺激性的）","form":"stimulatory（起刺激作用的）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"stimulate","pos":"v.","zh":"刺激；激发；促进"},{"word":"stimulus","pos":"n.","zh":"刺激物；刺激因素（复数 stimuli）"},{"word":"stimulating","pos":"adj.","zh":"令人振奋的；起刺激作用的"},{"word":"stimulant","pos":"n.","zh":"兴奋剂；刺激物"},{"word":"stimulatory","pos":"adj.","zh":"起刺激作用的；促进性的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The act of arousing activity","titleCN":"刺激：唤起或增强活动","definition":"the act of making something more active, alert or responsive than it was","definitionCN":"使某物比原来更活跃、更警觉或更有反应的动作","example":"The stimulation of the audience began with a surprising question.","exampleCN":"对听众的激发从一个出人意料的问题开始。","why":"Latin stimulus was a goad used to move an animal forward, so the noun starts from a prod that produces motion and then widens to any increase in activity.","whyCN":"拉丁 stimulus 是驱赶动物前进的刺棒，因此这个名词的起点是一个产生动作的「戳」，再扩展为任何活动的增强。"},{"no":"02","title":"Policy that prods an economy","titleCN":"经济刺激：推动需求与增长","definition":"government spending, tax cuts or rate cuts intended to increase demand and activity in an economy","definitionCN":"旨在增加经济中的需求与活动的政府支出、减税或降息","example":"Fiscal stimulation lifted construction employment within two quarters.","exampleCN":"财政刺激在两个季度内提升了建筑业就业。","why":"Economists borrowed the physiological word for a deliberate push: the economy is treated as a body that responds to a stimulus, and the measures are the prod.","whyCN":"经济学家借用了生理学词汇来表示有意的推动：经济被当作会对刺激作出反应的身体，而政策措施就是那根刺棒。"},{"no":"03","title":"Input to the senses","titleCN":"感官刺激：作用于视觉、听觉、触觉的输入","definition":"light, sound, texture or other input that the senses register and that keeps attention and perception active","definitionCN":"视觉、听觉、触觉等感官接收并使其保持活跃的输入","example":"Young children need varied sensory stimulation, not only screens.","exampleCN":"幼儿需要多样的感官刺激，而不只是屏幕。","why":"In psychology a stimulus is any event that produces a response; stimulation is the supplying of such events, which is why the word often appears with sensory.","whyCN":"心理学中，stimulus 是任何引起反应的事件；stimulation 则是提供这类事件，因此这个词常与 sensory 搭配。"},{"no":"04","title":"Electrical activation of nerve or muscle","titleCN":"电刺激：激活神经或肌肉","definition":"the use of small electrical currents to activate nerves or muscles for therapy, diagnosis or research","definitionCN":"使用微弱电流激活神经或肌肉，用于治疗、诊断或研究","example":"Deep brain stimulation can reduce tremor in Parkinson's disease.","exampleCN":"脑深部电刺激可以减轻帕金森病中的震颤。","why":"This medical sense is the most literal modern descendant of the goad: an electrode delivers a controlled pulse, and the tissue responds as if prodded.","whyCN":"这一医学义项是「刺棒」最字面的现代后裔：电极发出受控脉冲，组织就像被戳了一下那样作出反应。"},{"no":"05","title":"Triggering a gland or hormone","titleCN":"腺体或激素刺激：促使分泌","definition":"the process by which a hormone, nerve signal or drug causes a gland to release its secretion","definitionCN":"激素、神经信号或药物促使腺体释放分泌物的过程","example":"Thyroid stimulation raised the patient's hormone levels.","exampleCN":"甲状腺刺激提高了病人的激素水平。","why":"Endocrinology uses the word because a gland that is not secreting must be prodded into action; the noun names that trigger rather than the secretion itself.","whyCN":"内分泌学使用这个词，因为不分泌的腺体需要被「催动」；名词命名的是这一触发，而不是分泌物本身。"},{"no":"06","title":"Something that sparks thought or creativity","titleCN":"智识或创作上的激发","definition":"an idea, conversation or environment that makes thinking, learning or creative work more active","definitionCN":"使思考、学习或创作更加活跃的想法、对话或环境","example":"The seminar gave her the intellectual stimulation she had missed.","exampleCN":"这次研讨给了她久缺的智识激发。","why":"The metaphor of the goad is applied to the mind: a question or a problem prods thought into motion, and the resulting activity is called stimulation.","whyCN":"「刺棒」的比喻被用于心智：一个问题或难题把思考推入运动，由此产生的活跃状态便称为 stimulation。"},{"no":"07","title":"Promoting growth in living things","titleCN":"生物生长刺激：促进发育","definition":"the encouragement of growth, division or development in cells, plants or organisms by nutrients, hormones or light","definitionCN":"通过养分、激素或光照促进细胞、植物或生物体的生长、分裂或发育","example":"Light stimulation triggers flowering in many plants.","exampleCN":"光照刺激会触发许多植物开花。","why":"Growth can be dormant, and a signal can start it; biology names that starting signal stimulation, keeping the core idea of awakening an inactive system.","whyCN":"生长可以处于休眠状态，而某个信号可以启动它；生物学把这一启动信号称为 stimulation，保留「唤醒不活跃系统」的核心意思。"},{"no":"08","title":"Too much input at once","titleCN":"过度刺激：输入过量","definition":"an excessive amount of sensory, mental or social input that overwhelms rather than helps","definitionCN":"过量到令人不堪承受、而非有益的感官、心智或社交输入","example":"The classroom's constant stimulation left the children exhausted.","exampleCN":"教室里持续不断的刺激让孩子们筋疲力尽。","why":"The same noun covers excess because a goad applied without pause stops being a spur and becomes a burden; the word itself does not mark the limit, context does.","whyCN":"同一个名词也涵盖过量，因为不停施加的刺棒不再是激励而成为负担；词本身不标示界限，语境才标示。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Stimulation comes from Latin stimulatio, an action noun from stimulare 'to goad, prick', built on stimulus 'goad, spur'. The family is Latin, but the deeper origin of stimulus is not established.","cn":"stimulation 出自拉丁 stimulatio，是由 stimulare「刺、驱赶」构成的行动名词，词基为 stimulus「刺棒、马刺」。该词族源自拉丁，但 stimulus 的更深来源并无定论。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN STIMULUS","en":"Latin stimulus named a goad for driving animals and also the sting of an insect. Its deeper origin is uncertain; no reliable Indo-European root has been established.","cn":"拉丁 stimulus 指驱赶牲畜的刺棒，也指昆虫的螫针。其更深来源不确定，尚未确立可靠的印欧语词根。"},{"era":"LATIN STIMULARE","en":"The verb stimulare meant 'to prick, goad, urge on', used both for animals and for inciting a person.","cn":"动词 stimulare 意为「刺、用刺棒驱赶、催促」，既用于牲畜，也用于鼓动人。"},{"era":"LATIN STIMULATIO","en":"Stimulatio is the action noun: a goading, a spurring on. It supplies the English noun almost unchanged.","cn":"stimulatio 是动作名词，意为「用刺棒驱赶、激励」。英语名词几乎原样继承了它。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ARRIVAL","en":"Stimulation enters English in the early modern period, first in learned and medical prose about arousing bodily or mental activity.","cn":"stimulation 在近代早期进入英语，最早见于讨论唤起身体或心智活动的学术与医学文献。"},{"era":"PHYSIOLOGY AND PSYCHOLOGY","en":"In the nineteenth and twentieth centuries stimulation became a technical term for nerve, muscle and hormone activation, and for sensory input in psychology.","cn":"在十九、二十世纪，stimulation 成为神经、肌肉与激素激活的技术术语，也在心理学中指感官输入。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertainty (deeper root): the Indo-European origin of stimulus is undecided. First-attestation uncertainty: the earliest English citation of stimulation is unknown, and the date of Latin stimulatio itself is not precisely established.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词根）：stimulus 的印欧语来源没有定论。首见年代存疑：stimulation 的英语最早书证年代不确定，拉丁 stimulatio 本身的书证年代也非精确已知。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the stimulus family by part of speech and role; the second gives near-synonyms for the act of arousing.","cn":"第一组按词性与角色区分 stimulus 词族；第二组给出表示「唤起」的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"stimulus","ipa":"/ˈstɪmjələs/","tag":"noun, the trigger","definition":"The event or substance that produces a response. Stimulation is the act of supplying it, or the resulting activity.","definitionCN":"指产生反应的事件或物质；stimulation 是提供它的动作，或由此产生的活动。"},{"word":"stimulate","ipa":"/ˈstɪmjəleɪt/","tag":"verb","definition":"To produce stimulation; the verb names the action that the noun also names.","definitionCN":"指施加刺激；动词与名词都命名这一动作。"},{"word":"stimulant","ipa":"/ˈstɪmjələnt/","tag":"noun, a substance","definition":"A drug or drink that raises activity, such as caffeine. A stimulant is a thing; stimulation is a process.","definitionCN":"指提高活动水平的药物或饮品，如咖啡因；stimulant 是东西，stimulation 是过程。"},{"word":"stimulating","ipa":"/ˈstɪmjəleɪtɪŋ/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Descriptive of something that arouses interest; it is the quality, not the act.","definitionCN":"描述能引起兴趣的事物，是性质词，不是动作词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"excitation","ipa":"/ˌeksaɪˈteɪʃən/","tag":"physical or nervous","definition":"A technical raising of energy, especially in physics or physiology. It is narrower and more physical than stimulation.","definitionCN":"指能量提高的技术性说法，尤其用于物理或生理学；比 stimulation 更窄、更偏物理。"},{"word":"arousal","ipa":"/əˈraʊzəl/","tag":"waking up a state","definition":"The act of waking or awakening a response, often bodily or emotional. It stresses the transition from rest.","definitionCN":"指唤醒或引起反应，常指身体或情绪方面；更强调从静止到被唤醒的转变。"},{"word":"encouragement","ipa":"/ɪnˈkʌrɪdʒmənt/","tag":"social support","definition":"Words or support that give someone confidence. It works through meaning, while stimulation can be purely physical.","definitionCN":"指给人信心的话语或支持，通过意义起作用；stimulation 可以纯粹是物理的。"},{"word":"impetus","ipa":"/ˈɪmpɪtəs/","tag":"driving force","definition":"A force that makes something move faster or start. It is usually a single push, while stimulation can be sustained input.","definitionCN":"指使某物加速或启动的力量，通常是单次推动；stimulation 可以是持续的输入。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"stimulus + -ation: the goad, then the act of goading.","cn":"stimulus + -ation：先是刺棒，再是用刺棒驱赶的动作。"},{"en":"The family runs stimulate, stimulus, stimulant, stimulating, stimulatory.","cn":"同族词包括 stimulate、stimulus、stimulant、stimulating、stimulatory。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the senses: electrical stimulation, sensory stimulation, economic stimulation, brain stimulation.","cn":"固定搭配标出义项：电刺激、感官刺激、经济刺激、脑刺激。"},{"en":"A stimulus is the prod; stimulation is the prodding; a stimulant is the substance.","cn":"stimulus 是那根刺棒，stimulation 是刺的动作，stimulant 是刺激物。"},{"en":"Too much of it is overstimulation, not more benefit.","cn":"过多就是过度刺激，而不是更多益处。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a needle touching a horse's flank and the horse stepping forward.","cn":"想象一根细针碰到马腹，马向前迈步。"},{"en":"Picture a dark room where one switch lights a row of bulbs.","cn":"想象一间暗室，一个开关点亮一排灯泡。"},{"en":"Picture a quiet pond and a single stone setting rings moving outward.","cn":"想象平静的池塘，一块石头激起一圈圈向外扩散的波纹。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The therapist used electrical stimulation to restore movement in the hand.","cn":"治疗师用电刺激恢复手部活动。"},{"en":"Tax cuts were sold as stimulation for a slowing economy.","cn":"减税被宣传为对放缓经济的刺激。"},{"en":"Constant stimulation from screens can leave children too tired to play.","cn":"屏幕带来的持续刺激会让孩子累得不想玩。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「stimulate（刺激）+ ion」——用刺棒轻轻一戳，让人动起来 → stimulation 刺激","word":"stimulation"},"root":"拉丁 stimulus「刺棒、马刺」→ stimulare「刺、驱赶」→ stimulatio「激励」→ 英语 stimulation。更深词根来源不确定。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow the goad image outward: general arousal, economic stimulus, sensory input, nerve activation, gland secretion, mental spark, growth promotion and finally overload.","cn":"八个义项沿着「刺棒」意象向外展开：一般唤起、经济刺激、感官输入、神经激活、腺体分泌、心智激发、促进生长，最后是输入过量。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a light prod makes a resting system move.","cn":"核心意象：轻轻一戳，让静止的系统动起来。"},"chain":["RESTING STATE","PROD","RESPOND","INCREASE ACTIVITY","TRIGGER SECRETION","OVERLOAD"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S6","en":"AROUSAL OF MIND OR BODY: interest, attention and thought are set in motion.","cn":"心智或身体的唤起：兴趣、注意与思考被推动起来。"},{"senses":"S2","en":"DEMAND SIDE PUSH: public spending acts as the goad for an economy.","cn":"需求侧推动：公共支出充当经济的刺棒。"},{"senses":"S3 · S7","en":"INPUT THAT STARTS A PROCESS: sensory signals and growth signals wake a system.","cn":"启动过程的输入：感官信号与生长信号唤醒系统。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"MEDICAL TRIGGERING: currents activate nerves, hormones trigger glands.","cn":"医学触发：电流激活神经，激素触发腺体。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"THE LIMIT: the same prod, repeated without pause, becomes a burden.","cn":"限度：同一根刺棒若不停施加，便成为负担。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Stimulation is a Latin action noun: the base stimulus 'goad', the verb stimulare 'to goad', and the ending -atio.","cn":"stimulation 是拉丁动作名词：词基 stimulus「刺棒」，动词 stimulare「驱赶」，以及词尾 -atio。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin stimulus and stimulare supply stimulate, stimulant, stimulating, stimulatory and stimulation; all keep the idea of a prod that produces a response.","cn":"拉丁 stimulus 与 stimulare 衍生出 stimulate、stimulant、stimulating、stimulatory 与 stimulation，都保留「一戳引起反应」的意思。"},"items":[{"word":"stimulation","structure":"stimulare + -atio (action noun)","meaning":"the act of goading or arousing","meaningCN":"刺激或唤起的动作","example":"Sensory stimulation is essential in early childhood.","exampleCN":"感官刺激在幼儿期至关重要。"},{"word":"stimulate","structure":"Latin stimulare (to goad)","meaning":"to arouse or increase activity","meaningCN":"刺激；使活跃","example":"The policy aimed to stimulate demand.","exampleCN":"该政策旨在刺激需求。"},{"word":"stimulus","structure":"Latin stimulus (goad)","meaning":"something that produces a response","meaningCN":"引起反应的事物","example":"The tax rebate was a stimulus for spending.","exampleCN":"退税是促进消费的刺激。"},{"word":"stimulant","structure":"stimulare + -ant (agent)","meaning":"a substance that raises activity","meaningCN":"提高活动水平的物质","example":"Caffeine is a mild stimulant.","exampleCN":"咖啡因是一种温和的兴奋剂。"},{"word":"stimulating","structure":"stimulate + -ing (adjective)","meaning":"arousing interest or activity","meaningCN":"令人兴奋的；启发性的","example":"It was a stimulating debate.","exampleCN":"那是一场令人振奋的辩论。"},{"word":"stimulatory","structure":"stimulate + -ory (tending to)","meaning":"having a stimulating effect","meaningCN":"具有刺激作用的","example":"The drug has a stimulatory effect on the heart.","exampleCN":"该药对心脏有刺激作用。"},{"word":"stimulator","structure":"stimulate + -or (device or agent)","meaning":"a device that delivers stimulation","meaningCN":"施加刺激的装置","example":"A nerve stimulator can block pain signals.","exampleCN":"神经刺激器可以阻断疼痛信号。"},{"word":"overstimulation","structure":"over- (too much) + stimulation","meaning":"excessive input","meaningCN":"过度刺激","example":"Overstimulation makes it hard to concentrate.","exampleCN":"过度刺激使人难以集中注意。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"stimulus","structure":"stimulus, stimuli (m., second declension)","meaning":"goad, spur; sting","meaningCN":"刺棒；马刺；螫针"},{"word":"stimulare","structure":"stimulus + -are (verb)","meaning":"to goad, prick, urge on","meaningCN":"用刺棒驱赶；刺；催促"},{"word":"-atio","structure":"-atio, -ationis (f., action noun)","meaning":"suffix naming an action","meaningCN":"命名动作的名词词尾"}]}},{"word":"structural","ipa_uk":"/strʌkˈtʃərəl/","ipa_us":"/strʌkˈtʃɚəl/","definition_zh":"结构的；结构性的；建筑承重构造的；系统深层的","definition_en":"relating to the structure or framework of something, especially to its load-bearing parts or its underlying organization","core_image":"一座桥的钢架剖面被抽掉一块，周围的梁柱仍把重量一步步传向地基","scene":"The survey found structural damage beneath the bridge deck.","sceneCN":"这里 structural 是「结构上的、承重构造的」（第 2 个义项：与建筑的梁柱和承重体系有关）；句意：检测发现桥面下方存在结构损伤。图中可辨识物件：钢梁、桥墩、裂缝、承重箭头。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"结构的；结构性的；建筑承重构造的；系统深层的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"structural damage","zh":"结构损伤"},{"phrase":"structural reform","zh":"结构性改革"},{"phrase":"structural adjustment","zh":"结构调整"},{"phrase":"structural change","zh":"结构性变化"},{"phrase":"structural engineer","zh":"结构工程师"},{"phrase":"structural inequality","zh":"结构性不平等"},{"phrase":"structural analysis","zh":"结构分析"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more structural（更具结构性的）"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most structural（最具结构性的）"},{"label":"副词形式","form":"structurally（在结构上）"},{"label":"名词（框架）","form":"structure（结构；构造）"},{"label":"名词（学说）","form":"structuralism（结构主义）"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"restructure（重组；重构）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"structure","pos":"n./v.","zh":"结构；构造；组织"},{"word":"structuralism","pos":"n.","zh":"结构主义"},{"word":"structuralist","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"结构主义者；结构主义的"},{"word":"restructure","pos":"v.","zh":"重组；重构"},{"word":"infrastructure","pos":"n.","zh":"基础设施"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Relating to a framework","titleCN":"与框架、构造有关","definition":"relating to the way the parts of something are arranged and connected to form a whole","definitionCN":"与某物各部分如何排列、连接成一个整体的方式有关","example":"The essay compares the structural features of the two novels.","exampleCN":"这篇文章比较了这两部小说的结构特征。","why":"Latin structura named a fitting together, from struere 'to build'; the adjective therefore points to arrangement rather than to surface appearance.","whyCN":"拉丁 structura 指「拼合、建造」，出自 struere「建造」；因此这个形容词指向排列方式，而不是表面外观。"},{"no":"02","title":"Load-bearing parts of a building","titleCN":"建筑承重结构","definition":"relating to the beams, columns, walls and foundations that carry weight and keep a building standing","definitionCN":"与承担重量、使建筑站立的梁、柱、墙与基础有关","example":"A structural engineer approved the plans before construction began.","exampleCN":"施工开始前，结构工程师批准了图纸。","why":"This engineering sense is the concrete core of the metaphor: the parts that bear load are literally the structure, and damage to them threatens the whole.","whyCN":"这一工程义项是比喻的具体核心：承重的部件就是字面意义上的结构，它们的损伤会威胁整体。"},{"no":"03","title":"Of a language as a system","titleCN":"语言学中的结构：把语言视为系统","definition":"in linguistics, describing language as a system of relations among sounds, words and sentences rather than as a list of items","definitionCN":"在语言学中，把语言描述为声音、词与句子之间的关系系统，而不是一份条目清单","example":"Structural analysis shows that the two dialects share the same sound system.","exampleCN":"结构分析显示，这两种方言共享同一套语音系统。","why":"Twentieth-century linguistics shifted attention from isolated words to the network that holds them together, and structural became the label for that viewpoint.","whyCN":"二十世纪语言学把关注点从孤立的词转向维系它们的网络，structural 成为这一视角的标签。"},{"no":"04","title":"Underlying causes in a system","titleCN":"系统性深层原因","definition":"describing a cause that lies in the organization of a system rather than in the choices of one person","definitionCN":"指某项原因存在于系统的组织方式中，而不是某个人的选择中","example":"Poverty in the region is structural, not a matter of individual effort.","exampleCN":"该地区的贫困是结构性的，与个人努力无关。","why":"If the arrangement of institutions produces the outcome, blaming individuals misses the mechanism; structural names that mechanism and is often opposed to personal or accidental.","whyCN":"如果制度安排产生了这一结果，归咎个人就错失了机制；structural 命名这一机制，常与「个人的」「偶然的」相对。"},{"no":"05","title":"Change that alters the framework","titleCN":"改变框架本身的结构性变革","definition":"describing reform or change that alters the basic organization of an economy, industry or institution rather than adjusting its surface","definitionCN":"指改变经济、产业或机构基本组织方式的改革，而不是表面调整","example":"The country undertook structural reforms in taxation and labour law.","exampleCN":"该国在税制与劳动法方面进行了结构性改革。","why":"Policy language distinguishes a structural reform from a temporary fix: the former changes the rules that generate outcomes, not just the outcomes themselves.","whyCN":"政策语言把结构性改革与临时补救区分开：前者改变产生结果的规则，而不只是结果本身。"},{"no":"06","title":"Arrangement of molecules or cells","titleCN":"分子或细胞层面的结构","definition":"in chemistry and biology, relating to the arrangement of atoms, molecules or tissues and how that arrangement determines function","definitionCN":"在化学与生物学中，与原子、分子或组织的排列方式以及该排列如何决定功能有关","example":"Structural biology revealed how the protein binds its target.","exampleCN":"结构生物学揭示了这种蛋白质如何结合靶点。","why":"Function follows form at the molecular scale: knowing how the parts are arranged explains what the molecule can do, which is why the adjective attaches to biology.","whyCN":"在分子尺度上功能随形式而来：了解各部分如何排列，就能解释分子能做什么，因此这个形容词常与生物学搭配。"},{"no":"07","title":"Inequality built into society","titleCN":"制度化的结构性不平等","definition":"describing disadvantage that is reproduced by the rules, norms and organization of a society rather than by individual prejudice alone","definitionCN":"指由社会的规则、规范与组织方式不断再生产出来的不利处境，而非仅由个人偏见造成","example":"The report documented structural inequality in housing and schooling.","exampleCN":"报告记录了指住房与教育方面的结构性不平等。","why":"This social sense extends the engineering image to institutions: the rules act as beams that distribute advantage unevenly, so the pattern persists even when individuals change.","whyCN":"这一社会义项把工程意象扩展到制度：规则像梁一样不均匀地分配优势，因此即使个人更替，模式仍然持续。"},{"no":"08","title":"Damage to the load-bearing frame","titleCN":"承重框架受损","definition":"describing physical damage that affects the frame or foundation of a building, vehicle or machine rather than its surface","definitionCN":"指影响建筑、车辆或机器框架或基础的物理损伤，而不是表面损伤","example":"The earthquake caused structural damage but no injuries.","exampleCN":"地震造成了结构损伤，但无人受伤。","why":"This sense returns to the literal core: cosmetic cracks can be repaired, but structural damage means the part that carries the load is compromised, so the whole is at risk.","whyCN":"这一义项回到字面核心：表面裂缝可以修补，而结构损伤意味着承重部件受损，整体因而处于风险中。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Structural is structure plus the adjective ending -al; structure comes from Latin structura 'a building, a fitting together', from struere 'to build, pile up'. The deeper root is reconstructed.","cn":"structural 是 structure 加形容词词尾 -al；structure 出自拉丁 structura「建筑、拼合」，源自 struere「建造、堆叠」。其更深词根为重构形式。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN STRUERE","en":"Latin struere meant 'to build, pile up, arrange', and its past participle structus supplied the notion of something already built. The deeper root is reconstructed as Indo-European *streu- 'to spread, pile up'.","cn":"拉丁 struere 意为「建造、堆叠、安排」，其过去分词 structus 提供「已建成之物」的概念。更深词根被重构为印欧语 *streu-「铺开、堆积」。"},{"era":"LATIN STRUCTURA","en":"Structura named the act of building and the building itself, hence 'a fitting together, an arrangement'. It is the direct source of English structure.","cn":"structura 指建造行为及建筑物本身，因而表示「拼合、安排」。它是英语 structure 的直接来源。"},{"era":"ENGLISH STRUCTURE","en":"English borrowed structure in the fifteenth century, first for buildings and later for the arrangement of any organized whole.","cn":"英语在十五世纪借入 structure，最初指建筑物，后来指任何有组织整体的排列方式。"},{"era":"STRUCTURAL","en":"The adjective structural appears later, formed on structure with -al, and spread in engineering, biology and grammar in the nineteenth century.","cn":"形容词 structural 出现较晚，由 structure 加 -al 构成，并在十九世纪扩展到工程、生物与语法领域。"},{"era":"STRUCTURALISM","en":"Twentieth-century linguistics and anthropology made structural a key term for systems of relations, giving the word its abstract, systemic sense.","cn":"二十世纪的语言学与人类学使 structural 成为「关系系统」的关键术语，赋予该词抽象的、系统性的义项。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"First-attestation uncertainty: the earliest English citation of structural is unknown. Reconstructed form: the Indo-European root of struere, *streu-, is a reconstruction rather than a recorded word, and its exact semantic range remains disputed.","cn":"首见年代存疑：structural 的英语最早书证年代不确定。重构形式：struere 的印欧语词根 *streu- 属重构，并非有记录的真实词形，其确切语义范围仍有争议。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the structure family by part of speech and use; the second gives near-synonyms for being fundamental to a system.","cn":"第一组按词性与用法区分 structure 词族；第二组给出表示「属于系统根本」的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"structure","ipa":"/ˈstrʌktʃə/","tag":"noun or verb","definition":"The arrangement itself, or the act of arranging. Structural is the adjective describing it.","definitionCN":"指排列本身，或安排的动作；structural 是描述它的形容词。"},{"word":"structured","ipa":"/ˈstrʌktʃəd/","tag":"adjective of arrangement","definition":"Having a definite plan or pattern. Structured describes a thing that was organized; structural describes what belongs to the frame.","definitionCN":"指具有明确计划或模式；structured 描述被组织好的事物，structural 描述属于框架的东西。"},{"word":"structuralism","ipa":"/ˈstrʌktʃərəlɪzəm/","tag":"the theory","definition":"The school of thought that analyses systems of relations. Structural is the adjective; structuralism is the doctrine.","definitionCN":"指分析关系系统的学派；structural 是形容词，structuralism 是学说。"},{"word":"structurally","ipa":"/ˈstrʌktʃərəli/","tag":"adverb","definition":"The adverb answering 'in what respect?'. Structural modifies a noun; structurally modifies a verb or adjective.","definitionCN":"副词，回答「在哪方面」；structural 修饰名词，structurally 修饰动词或形容词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"systemic","ipa":"/sɪˈstemɪk/","tag":"affecting the whole","definition":"Affecting the whole system rather than a part. It stresses spread through the system; structural stresses the framework that causes the spread.","definitionCN":"指影响整个系统而非局部；systemic 强调贯穿系统，structural 强调造成这种贯穿的框架。"},{"word":"architectural","ipa":"/ˌɑːkɪˈtektʃərəl/","tag":"of design of buildings","definition":"Relating to the art and design of buildings. Structural concerns whether they stand; architectural concerns how they are conceived.","definitionCN":"指建筑艺术与设计；structural 关心建筑能否站住，architectural 关心如何构思。"},{"word":"organizational","ipa":"/ˌɔːɡənaɪˈzeɪʃənəl/","tag":"of an institution","definition":"Relating to the way a group is arranged. It is the social counterpart of structural, which can also describe beams and molecules.","definitionCN":"指群体的安排方式，是 structural 在社会领域的对应词，而 structural 也能描述梁柱与分子。"},{"word":"foundational","ipa":"/faʊnˈdeɪʃənəl/","tag":"at the base","definition":"Serving as the base or basis. It points to what everything rests on, while structural points to how the parts are connected.","definitionCN":"指作为基础或依据，强调一切所依托之物；structural 强调部分如何连接。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"structure + -al: of the frame that holds the parts together.","cn":"structure + -al：属于把各部分撑在一起的框架。"},{"en":"The family runs structure, structured, structuralism, structuralist, restructure, infrastructure.","cn":"同族词包括 structure、structured、structuralism、structuralist、restructure、infrastructure。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases show the range: structural damage, structural reform, structural adjustment, structural engineer.","cn":"固定搭配展示范围：结构损伤、结构性改革、结构调整、结构工程师。"},{"en":"A structure carries load; a structural problem is one in the load-bearing part.","cn":"结构承担荷载；结构性问题就出在承重部分。"},{"en":"Structural causes outlast individual choices.","cn":"结构性原因比个人选择更持久。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a bridge cut open so the beams and the arrows of load are visible.","cn":"想象一座桥被剖开，梁柱与荷载箭头都可见。"},{"en":"Picture a building whose walls are rules rather than bricks.","cn":"想象一座建筑，墙体是规则而不是砖块。"},{"en":"Picture a skeleton inside a body, holding up everything that looks soft.","cn":"想象身体里的一副骨架，撑起所有看似柔软的部分。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The inspection found structural cracks in three of the columns.","cn":"检查发现其中三根柱子有结构裂缝。"},{"en":"High youth unemployment is a structural problem, not a seasonal one.","cn":"青年高失业率是结构性问题，而不是季节性问题。"},{"en":"Structural biology maps the shape of proteins to explain their function.","cn":"结构生物学绘制蛋白质的形状，以解释其功能。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「structure（结构）+ al」——看骨架，不看表皮 → structural 结构的","word":"structural"},"root":"拉丁 struere「建造、堆叠」→ 过去分词 structus → 拉丁 structura「建筑、拼合」→ 英语 structure + -al。更深词根为重构形式 *streu-。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses move from arrangement in general to load-bearing frames, language systems, underlying causes, framework-changing reform, molecular shape, social inequality and literal structural damage.","cn":"八个义项从一般排列方式，扩展到承重框架、语言系统、深层原因、改变框架的改革、分子形态、社会不平等，最后回到字面上的结构损伤。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a visible frame carries weight from the top down to the base.","cn":"核心意象：可见的框架把重量从顶部一路传到基座。"},"chain":["FIT TOGETHER","BEAR LOAD","HOLD RELATIONS","CAUSE FROM BELOW","CHANGE THE FRAME","ARRANGE MOLECULES"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1","en":"ARRANGEMENT AS SUCH: how the parts are put together to make a whole.","cn":"排列本身：各部分如何拼合成一个整体。"},{"senses":"S2 · S8","en":"LOAD PATH: beams and foundations carry weight, and damage there endangers the whole.","cn":"荷载路径：梁与基础承担重量，此处受损会危及整体。"},{"senses":"S3 · S6","en":"SYSTEMS OF RELATIONS: sounds in a language, atoms in a molecule, arranged so that form explains function.","cn":"关系系统：语言中的音、分子中的原子，其排列使形式解释功能。"},{"senses":"S4 · S7","en":"CAUSES BUILT INTO INSTITUTIONS: outcomes reproduced by rules rather than by individual choice.","cn":"制度内置的原因：结果由规则而非个人选择不断再生产。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"REFORM AT THE FRAME: change the rules that generate outcomes, not just the outcomes.","cn":"框架层面的改革：改变产生结果的规则，而不只是结果。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Structural is a Latin-derived base plus an adjective ending: struere 'to build' gives structura, English structure, and then structural with -al.","cn":"structural 是拉丁词基加形容词词尾：struere「建造」给出 structura，英语作 structure，再加 -al 成为 structural。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin struere and structura also underlie construct, destruction, instruct, obstruct and infrastructure, all built on the image of piling parts into a frame.","cn":"拉丁 struere 与 structura 也支撑 construct、destruction、instruct、obstruct、infrastructure，都建立在「把部件堆成框架」的意象上。"},"items":[{"word":"structural","structure":"structure + -al (relating to)","meaning":"relating to a framework","meaningCN":"与框架有关的","example":"The building has structural problems in the east wing.","exampleCN":"这座建筑东翼存在结构问题。"},{"word":"structure","structure":"Latin structura (building, arrangement)","meaning":"the arrangement of parts","meaningCN":"各部分的排列方式","example":"The structure of the argument is easy to follow.","exampleCN":"这一论证的结构很容易跟随。"},{"word":"structurally","structure":"structural + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in structural terms","meaningCN":"在结构上","example":"The two buildings are structurally similar.","exampleCN":"这两座建筑在结构上相似。"},{"word":"structuralism","structure":"structural + -ism (doctrine)","meaning":"the theory of relational systems","meaningCN":"研究关系系统的学说","example":"Structuralism treated language as a system of differences.","exampleCN":"结构主义把语言视为差异系统。"},{"word":"structuralist","structure":"structural + -ist (person or adjective)","meaning":"a follower of structuralism","meaningCN":"结构主义者；结构主义的","example":"The structuralist read the myth as a pattern of oppositions.","exampleCN":"这位结构主义者把神话读成对立模式。"},{"word":"restructure","structure":"re- (again) + structure","meaning":"to organize again in a new way","meaningCN":"重组；以新方式组织","example":"The firm restructured its debt last year.","exampleCN":"该公司去年重组了债务。"},{"word":"infrastructure","structure":"infra- (below) + structure","meaning":"the underlying systems a society needs","meaningCN":"社会所依赖的基础系统","example":"Roads and water pipes are infrastructure.","exampleCN":"道路与水管属于基础设施。"},{"word":"substructure","structure":"sub- (under) + structure","meaning":"the supporting part beneath a building","meaningCN":"建筑物下方的支撑部分","example":"The substructure was reinforced with steel piles.","exampleCN":"下部结构用钢桩加固。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"struere","structure":"struere, struxi, structum (third conjugation)","meaning":"to build, pile up, arrange","meaningCN":"建造；堆叠；安排"},{"word":"structura","structure":"structura, structurae (f., first declension)","meaning":"a building; a fitting together","meaningCN":"建筑物；拼合方式"},{"word":"-alis","structure":"-alis, -ale (adjective suffix)","meaning":"belonging to","meaningCN":"属于……的"}]}},{"word":"structurally","ipa_uk":"/ˈstrʌktʃərəli/","ipa_us":"/ˈstrʌktʃərəli/","definition_zh":"结构上；从结构上看；在构造方面；（建筑）承重上","definition_en":"in terms of structure, or with regard to the way something is built, arranged or organized","core_image":"一座桥的剖切图：钢梁与拱肋被高亮标出，荷载沿梁身一路传到桥台","scene":"Structurally, the old bridge is still sound, though its surface looks worn.","sceneCN":"这里 structurally 是「结构上」（第 1 个义项：从构造与受力体系判断，而不是只看外观）；句意：从结构上看，这座旧桥仍然牢固，尽管表面显得破旧。图中可辨识物件：桥的剖切面、钢梁、拱肋、桥台，以及沿梁身传向桥台的荷载箭头。","pos":[{"tag":"adv.","zh":"结构上；从结构上看；在构造方面；（建筑）承重上（常置于句首或动词前，也可与 sound、similar、different 等形容词连用）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"structurally sound","zh":"结构完好；结构牢固"},{"phrase":"structurally similar","zh":"结构相似"},{"phrase":"structurally different","zh":"结构不同"},{"phrase":"structurally impossible","zh":"结构上不可能的"},{"phrase":"structurally determined","zh":"由结构决定的"},{"phrase":"structurally unstable","zh":"结构不稳定的"}],"forms":[{"label":"形容词形式","form":"structural（结构的；结构性的）"},{"label":"名词（事物）","form":"structure（结构；构造；建筑物）"},{"label":"名词（学科视角）","form":"structuralism（结构主义）"},{"label":"名词（过程）","form":"structuration（结构化过程）"},{"label":"比较级","form":"more structurally（更从结构角度地）"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most structurally（最从结构角度地）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"structural","pos":"adj.","zh":"结构的；结构性的；承重的"},{"word":"structure","pos":"n.","zh":"结构；构造；建筑物"},{"word":"structured","pos":"adj.","zh":"有结构的；有组织的；有条理的"},{"word":"restructuring","pos":"n.","zh":"重组；结构调整"},{"word":"structuralism","pos":"n.","zh":"结构主义"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"In terms of construction or make-up","titleCN":"结构上：就构造与组成而言","definition":"with respect to the way the parts of something are put together","definitionCN":"就某物各部分的组合方式而言","example":"Structurally, the two languages are unrelated.","exampleCN":"从结构上看，这两种语言并无亲缘关系。","why":"The adverb -ly turns structural into a viewpoint: the speaker sets aside surface detail and asks how the parts are arranged and joined.","whyCN":"副词词尾 -ly 把 structural 变成一种视角：说话人撇开表面细节，追问各部分如何排列与连接。"},{"no":"02","title":"As regards load-bearing safety","titleCN":"承重上：就建筑受力安全而言","definition":"with respect to whether a building or frame can carry its loads without failing","definitionCN":"就建筑物或构架能否安全承受荷载、不致失效而言","example":"Structurally, the balcony cannot take the weight of a hot tub.","exampleCN":"从承重上看，这个阳台承受不了一个热水浴缸的重量。","why":"In engineering the structure is the load path, so structurally names the question of whether forces reach the ground safely.","whyCN":"在工程中，结构就是荷载路径，因此 structurally 指的是力能否安全传到地面这一问题。"},{"no":"03","title":"Compared by the way parts are arranged","titleCN":"结构相似或不同：从构造上比较","definition":"used with similar or different, meaning that the comparison concerns the arrangement of parts rather than their appearance or size","definitionCN":"与 similar 或 different 连用，表示比较的是各部分的排列方式，而不是外观或大小","example":"The two proteins are structurally similar but chemically distinct.","exampleCN":"这两种蛋白质在结构上相似，化学性质却不同。","why":"Once structure means arrangement, the adverb allows a comparison that holds apart from surface differences, a common move in biology and linguistics.","whyCN":"当 structure 指排列方式时，这个副词使比较得以脱离表面差异而成立，这在生物学与语言学中很常见。"},{"no":"04","title":"Determined by the structure","titleCN":"结构决定：由构造方式所决定","definition":"in a way that is fixed or caused by the arrangement of parts rather than by choice or surface features","definitionCN":"指由各部分的排列方式所固定或造成，而不是由选择或表面特征造成","example":"Structurally, the shortage is built into the system, not caused by bad managers.","exampleCN":"从结构上说，这种短缺是制度内在造成的，而不是坏管理者造成的。","why":"Here the adverb shifts from describing to explaining: the arrangement itself is presented as the cause, so structurally means by the logic of the structure.","whyCN":"这里副词从描述转为解释：排列方式本身被呈现为原因，因此 structurally 意为「按结构的逻辑」。"},{"no":"05","title":"Impossible by the nature of the structure","titleCN":"结构上不可能：构造本身不允许","definition":"used with impossible, meaning that no rearrangement of the existing parts could make something happen","definitionCN":"与 impossible 连用，表示无论怎样重新排列现有部分都无法使之发生","example":"Structurally, a two-wheeled cart cannot stand still without a support.","exampleCN":"从结构上说，两轮车没有支撑就无法静止站立。","why":"This sense draws the line between a practical difficulty and a limit set by the arrangement itself, which no effort can remove.","whyCN":"这一义项划出「实际困难」与「构造本身设定的限制」之间的界线，后者再努力也无法消除。"},{"no":"06","title":"At the level of molecules or crystals","titleCN":"分子或晶体层面：原子怎样排布","definition":"at the level of the arrangement of atoms or molecules in a substance","definitionCN":"指物质中原子或分子排布的层面","example":"The alloy is structurally stable up to six hundred degrees.","exampleCN":"这种合金在六百度以内结构稳定。","why":"Materials science reads structure as the lattice, so the adverb points to atomic arrangement rather than to visible shape.","whyCN":"材料科学把结构理解为晶格，因此这个副词指向原子排布，而不是可见外形。"},{"no":"07","title":"At the level of institutions or society","titleCN":"制度层面：社会与经济的结构","definition":"with respect to the institutions and relations that organize a society or economy","definitionCN":"就组织社会或经济的制度与关系而言","example":"The report argues that the problem is structurally embedded in the labour market.","exampleCN":"报告认为，这一问题已结构性嵌入劳动力市场。","why":"Social scientists extended structure from buildings to institutions, and structurally now marks causes that lie in the system rather than in individuals.","whyCN":"社会科学家把 structure 从建筑扩展到制度，structurally 现在标记那些位于制度而非个人之中的原因。"},{"no":"08","title":"Sound in its structure","titleCN":"结构完好：构架足以承重","definition":"used with sound or unsound, meaning that the frame is strong enough to carry its intended loads","definitionCN":"与 sound 或 unsound 连用，表示构架足够坚固，能承受预定荷载","example":"The inspection found the roof structurally sound after the storm.","exampleCN":"检查发现，暴风雨过后屋顶结构完好。","why":"Sound here is the engineer's word for a structure that passes its load test, so the phrase is the standard verdict of an inspection.","whyCN":"这里的 sound 是工程师用来表示结构通过荷载检验的词，因此该短语是检查报告的标准结论。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Structurally is an English adverb built on structure, from Latin structura 'a building, a fitting together', from struere 'to build, pile up'. The dates below are approximate.","cn":"structurally 是英语副词，建立在 structure 之上；structure 出自拉丁 structura「建筑物、拼合」，而 structura 又出自 struere「建造、堆叠」。以下年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN STRUERE","en":"Latin struere meant 'to build, pile up, arrange in layers'. Its supine stem struct- supplies the participle structus 'built' and underlies the whole family.","cn":"拉丁 struere 意为「建造、堆叠、层层排列」，其目的分词词干 struct- 提供分词 structus「被建造的」，并支撑整个词族。"},{"era":"LATIN STRUCTURA","en":"structura 'a building, a fitting together' adds -ura to the supine stem and names both the act of building and its result.","cn":"structura「建筑物、拼合」在目的分词词干上加 -ura，既命名建造动作，也命名建造结果。"},{"era":"ENGLISH STRUCTURE","en":"English structure enters through Old French in the fourteenth century, first as the act of building and later as the arrangement of parts.","cn":"英语 structure 于十四世纪经古法语进入，先指建造动作，后指各部分的排列方式。"},{"era":"ADJECTIVE -AL","en":"The adjective structural adds -al, from Latin -alis 'belonging to', to structure; structurally then takes the native adverb ending.","cn":"形容词 structural 在 structure 上加 -al（出自拉丁 -alis「属于……的」）；structurally 再加本族副词词尾。"},{"era":"ADVERB -LY","en":"Old English -lice, the ancestor of -ly, formed manner adverbs from adjectives and survives as the regular English ending.","cn":"古英语 -lice 是 -ly 的前身，由形容词构成方式副词，并作为英语的常规词尾留存下来。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"The first English citation of structurally is uncertain. The deeper Indo-European root is reconstructed as *streu- 'to pile up, spread', a reconstruction and not a recorded word; handbooks also connect it with Latin strues 'heap'.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：structurally 的英语最早书证年代不明。更深的印欧词根被重构为 *streu-「堆起、铺开」，属重构形式而非有记录的真实词形；手册还把它与拉丁 strues「堆」相联系。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates members of the same Latin family by part of speech; the second gives near-synonyms for the viewpoints the adverb can mark.","cn":"第一组按词性区分同一拉丁词族的成员；第二组给出与该副词所标视角相近的说法。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"structural","ipa":"/strʌkˈtʃʊərəl/","tag":"adjective","definition":"The adjective that modifies a noun: a structural problem is a problem in the frame, while structurally tells how the frame is affected.","definitionCN":"修饰名词的形容词：structural problem 指构架本身的问题，而 structurally 说明从结构角度看受到怎样的影响。"},{"word":"structure","ipa":"/ˈstrʌktʃə/","tag":"noun","definition":"The frame or arrangement itself; it can be a subject or object, which the adverb cannot.","definitionCN":"指构架或排列方式本身；它可以作主语或宾语，而副词不能。"},{"word":"structured","ipa":"/ˈstrʌktʃəd/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Having a deliberate arrangement, often of time, data or activity; it describes a designed order rather than a viewpoint.","definitionCN":"指具有刻意安排的结构，常用于时间、数据或活动；它描述被设计出的秩序，而不是一种视角。"},{"word":"structuralism","ipa":"/strʌkˈtʃʊərəlɪzəm/","tag":"theory","definition":"The academic approach that studies systems of relations; it names a theory, not a way of speaking about one object.","definitionCN":"指研究关系系统的学术取向；它命名一种理论，而不是谈论某一对象的说法。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"architecturally","ipa":"/ˌɑːkɪˈtektʃərəli/","tag":"in building design","definition":"In terms of building design. It covers appearance and style, whereas structurally concerns the load-bearing frame.","definitionCN":"指从建筑设计角度看，涵盖外观与风格；而 structurally 关心的是承重构架。"},{"word":"anatomically","ipa":"/əˈnætəmɪkli/","tag":"in body structure","definition":"In terms of the parts of a body. It is the biological counterpart of sense 3, not a word for buildings.","definitionCN":"指从身体各部分的构造看；它是第 3 个义项在生物领域的对应说法，而不是用于建筑。"},{"word":"organizationally","ipa":"/ˌɔːɡənaɪˈzeɪʃənəli/","tag":"in institutional layout","definition":"In terms of how an institution is arranged; close to sense 7 but limited to management and hierarchy.","definitionCN":"指从机构的编排方式看；接近第 7 个义项，但限于管理与层级。"},{"word":"mechanically","ipa":"/məˈkænɪkli/","tag":"in working parts","definition":"In terms of working parts and forces; it overlaps with load-bearing but also covers function and machinery.","definitionCN":"指从运转部件与受力看；它与承重义项有重叠，但也涵盖功能与机械。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"struct- (build) + -ure (result) + -al (relating to) + -ly (in that way): in the way the thing is put together.","cn":"struct-（建造）+ -ure（结果）+ -al（与……有关）+ -ly（以……方式）：按事物被拼合的方式来看。"},{"en":"The family runs structure, structural, structured, restructuring, structuralism.","cn":"同族词包括 structure、structural、structured、restructuring、structuralism。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases carry the senses: structurally sound, structurally similar, structurally impossible, structurally embedded.","cn":"固定搭配承载词义：结构完好、结构相似、结构上不可能、结构性嵌入。"},{"en":"An engineer asks 'will it stand?'; a linguist asks 'how are the parts arranged?'; both answer structurally.","cn":"工程师问「它站得住吗」，语言学家问「各部分怎样排列」，两者都用 structurally 回答。"},{"en":"Structural is the adjective, structure the noun, structurally the standpoint.","cn":"structural 是形容词，structure 是名词，structurally 是一种视角。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a bridge cut in half so that beams and arches show.","cn":"想象一座桥被剖成两半，钢梁与拱肋都露出来。"},{"en":"Picture a shelf unit in which every shelf is the same distance apart.","cn":"想象一个书架，每层搁板之间的距离完全相同。"},{"en":"Picture a row of dominoes already leaning, so the fall is decided before it starts.","cn":"想象一排已经倾斜的多米诺骨牌，倒塌在开始之前就已被决定。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Structurally, the proposal is a copy of the plan rejected last year.","cn":"从结构上看，这项提案是去年被否决计划的翻版。"},{"en":"The old theatre is structurally unsound and will be closed for repairs.","cn":"这座旧剧院结构不牢固，将关闭维修。"},{"en":"The two sentences are structurally different although they mean the same.","cn":"这两个句子结构不同，尽管意思相同。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「structure（结构）+ ally（地）」——按结构来看 → structurally 从结构上","word":"structurally"},"root":"拉丁 struere「建造、堆叠」→ 拉丁 structura「建造；构造」→ 古法语 structure → 英语 structure + -al + -ly。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one idea, the arrangement of parts: the plain structural view, the load path of a building, a comparison of arrangements, a cause built into a system, a limit set by the frame, the lattice of a material, the institutions of a society, and the verdict that a frame is sound.","cn":"八个义项围绕同一思路「各部分的排列」展开：一般结构视角、建筑的荷载路径、构造比较、制度内在的原因、构架设定的限制、材料的晶格、社会的制度，以及构架完好的判定。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a frame of beams carries a load down to the ground.","cn":"核心意象：由梁构成的构架把荷载一路传到地面。"},"chain":["ARRANGE THE PARTS","JOIN INTO A FRAME","TRACE THE LOAD","COMPARE THE ARRANGEMENT","EXTEND TO INSTITUTIONS","JUDGE IT SOUND"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S3","en":"THE VIEW FROM STRUCTURE: how parts are arranged, and how two arrangements compare.","cn":"结构视角：各部分怎样排列，以及两种排列怎样比较。"},{"senses":"S2 · S8","en":"LOAD PATH: whether the frame can carry its weight and pass inspection.","cn":"荷载路径：构架能否承重并通过检验。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"WHAT THE FRAME DECIDES: causes fixed by arrangement, and limits no effort can lift.","cn":"构架所决定的事：由排列固定的原因，以及再努力也无法解除的限制。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"THE LATTICE: atoms and crystals arranged in a pattern.","cn":"晶格：原子与晶体按一定图样排布。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"THE INSTITUTIONAL FRAME: markets and offices organized by rules.","cn":"制度构架：市场与机构按规则组织起来。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Structurally is built in four layers: Latin struere 'to build', Latin structura, the adjective ending -al, and the native adverb ending -ly.","cn":"structurally 分四层构成：拉丁 struere「建造」，拉丁 structura，形容词词尾 -al，以及本族副词词尾 -ly。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin struere supplies the supine stem struct-, from which structura 'a building, a fitting together' is formed; -al comes from Latin -alis, while -ly is native English.","cn":"拉丁 struere 提供目的分词词干 struct-，由此构成 structura「建筑物、拼合」；-al 出自拉丁 -alis，而 -ly 是本族英语词尾。"},"items":[{"word":"structurally","structure":"structural + -ly (manner adverb)","meaning":"from the point of view of structure","meaningCN":"从结构的角度；在结构上","example":"The annex is structurally separate from the main house.","exampleCN":"这间附属房在结构上与主屋分开。"},{"word":"structural","structure":"structure + -al (relating to)","meaning":"relating to structure","meaningCN":"与结构有关的","example":"Structural repairs kept the bridge open.","exampleCN":"结构维修让这座桥得以继续开放。"},{"word":"structure","structure":"Latin structura (a building, arrangement)","meaning":"a frame or arrangement of parts","meaningCN":"构架；各部分的排列","example":"The structure of the essay is easy to follow.","exampleCN":"这篇文章的结构很容易跟上。"},{"word":"structured","structure":"structure + -ed (having)","meaning":"having a deliberate arrangement","meaningCN":"具有刻意安排的","example":"The course follows a structured timetable.","exampleCN":"这门课按一张安排好的时间表进行。"},{"word":"restructuring","structure":"re- (again) + structure + -ing","meaning":"the act of organizing again","meaningCN":"重新组织；结构调整","example":"The restructuring cut two layers of management.","exampleCN":"这次重组削减了两个管理层级。"},{"word":"infrastructure","structure":"infra- (below) + structure","meaning":"the underlying public system","meaningCN":"底层公共设施体系","example":"Roads and sewers are part of the infrastructure.","exampleCN":"道路与下水道属于基础设施。"},{"word":"obstruct","structure":"ob- (against) + struere (to build)","meaning":"to block by building against","meaningCN":"阻挡；妨碍","example":"Fallen trees obstructed the path.","exampleCN":"倒下的树挡住了小路。"},{"word":"construction","structure":"con- (together) + struere + -tion","meaning":"the act of building","meaningCN":"建造；施工","example":"Construction of the tunnel took four years.","exampleCN":"这条隧道的建造花了四年。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"struere","structure":"struere, struxi, structum (third conjugation)","meaning":"to build, pile up, arrange","meaningCN":"建造；堆叠；排列"},{"word":"structura","structure":"struct- (supine stem) + -ura (result noun)","meaning":"a building, a fitting together","meaningCN":"建筑物；拼合；构造"},{"word":"-alis","structure":"-alis, -ale (adjective suffix)","meaning":"belonging to, relating to","meaningCN":"属于……的；与……有关的"}]}},{"word":"substantially","ipa_uk":"/səbˈstænʃəli/","ipa_us":"/səbˈstænʃəli/","definition_zh":"在很大程度上；大体上；大幅地；实质上","definition_en":"to a large degree, or in essence rather than in appearance","core_image":"一架天平：一端是一块实心铁砝码，另一端堆着许多小砝码，横梁只轻微倾斜","scene":"The cost of the project rose substantially after the design was revised.","sceneCN":"这里 substantially 是「大幅地」（第 3 个义项：数量、价格或水平出现明显增减）；句意：设计修改后，项目成本大幅上升。图中可辨识物件：天平横梁、实心铁砝码、成堆的小砝码、刻度指针，以及几乎不动的平衡标记。","pos":[{"tag":"adv.","zh":"在很大程度上；大体上；大幅地；实质上（修饰动词或形容词，说明程度或本质）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"substantially increase","zh":"大幅增加"},{"phrase":"substantially reduce","zh":"大幅减少"},{"phrase":"substantially different","zh":"大不相同"},{"phrase":"substantially the same","zh":"基本相同"},{"phrase":"substantially complete","zh":"基本完成"},{"phrase":"substantially all","zh":"实质全部（法律、会计用语）"}],"forms":[{"label":"形容词形式","form":"substantial（大量的；实质的；坚固的）"},{"label":"名词（本体）","form":"substance（物质；实质）"},{"label":"动词（证实）","form":"substantiate（证实；证明有根据）"},{"label":"名词（实质性）","form":"substantiality（实质性；实在性）"},{"label":"比较级","form":"more substantially（更大程度地）"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most substantially（最大程度地）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"substantial","pos":"adj.","zh":"大量的；实质的；坚固的"},{"word":"substance","pos":"n.","zh":"物质；实质；主旨"},{"word":"substantive","pos":"adj.","zh":"实质性的；独立的"},{"word":"substantiate","pos":"v.","zh":"证实；使有根据"},{"word":"substantively","pos":"adv.","zh":"实质上；在内容上"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"To a large degree","titleCN":"在很大程度上：程度很大地","definition":"to a large degree, or by a large amount","definitionCN":"在很大程度上，或达到很大的量","example":"The new tax changed the market substantially.","exampleCN":"新税在很大程度上改变了市场。","why":"Substantial first meant 'having substance', and a thing with substance has weight and size; the adverb therefore measures degree as if it were mass.","whyCN":"substantial 最初意为「有实体的」，有实体之物有重量与体积；因此副词像称量质量一样衡量程度。"},{"no":"02","title":"In essence, not merely in name","titleCN":"本质上：不在名目而在实质","definition":"in essential character, even if the form or the name is different","definitionCN":"指本质特征上如此，即使形式或名称不同","example":"Substantially, the proposal is the old policy in new words.","exampleCN":"实质上，这项提案只是旧政策换了个说法。","why":"Latin substantia was the underlying being of a thing, what stands beneath appearances; this sense keeps that literal idea and asks what remains when the wording changes.","whyCN":"拉丁 substantia 指事物表面之下的根本存在；这一义项保留该字面思路，追问换掉措辞后还剩下什么。"},{"no":"03","title":"By a large amount, up or down","titleCN":"大幅增减：数量或价格明显变化","definition":"by a large amount, used of increases, decreases or differences in number, price or level","definitionCN":"指数量、价格或水平上升、下降或差异的幅度很大","example":"The cost of the project rose substantially after the design was revised.","exampleCN":"设计修改后，项目成本大幅上升。","why":"This is the most frequent modern use: the adverb quantifies a change, and the direction comes from the verb, so rose substantially and fell substantially are equally natural.","whyCN":"这是现代最常见的用法：副词量化变化的幅度，方向由动词给出，因此 rose substantially 与 fell substantially 同样自然。"},{"no":"04","title":"Almost complete","titleCN":"基本完成：几乎全部收尾","definition":"used with complete or completed, meaning that nearly all the required work has been done but not every detail is finished","definitionCN":"与 complete 或 completed 连用，表示所需工作已几乎全部完成，但并非每个细节都已收尾","example":"The building was substantially complete by December.","exampleCN":"这座建筑到十二月已基本完工。","why":"In construction and contracts, substantially sets a threshold: the thing is usable for its purpose, though a punch list of small defects remains.","whyCN":"在建筑与合同中，substantially 设定一个门槛：标的已能按用途使用，尽管还剩一份小的缺陷清单。"},{"no":"05","title":"Broadly the same","titleCN":"基本一致：差异无关紧要","definition":"used with the same or similar, meaning that the differences are not important enough to change the conclusion","definitionCN":"与 the same 或 similar 连用，表示差异不足以改变结论","example":"The two versions are substantially the same.","exampleCN":"两个版本基本相同。","why":"Here the word admits small differences while denying that they matter, a hedge that is common in comparison and translation.","whyCN":"这里该词承认存在小差异，同时否认这些差异重要，是比较与翻译中常见的留有余地的说法。"},{"no":"06","title":"Substantially all in law","titleCN":"法律上的「实质全部」","definition":"in law and accounting, used of substantially all the assets or shares, meaning nearly the whole of them","definitionCN":"在法律与会计中用于 substantially all 的资产或股份，意为几乎全部","example":"The sale covered substantially all of the company's assets.","exampleCN":"这笔出售涉及公司实质全部资产。","why":"Courts and auditors need a phrase for almost everything but not literally every item, so substantially all became a fixed term with a threshold of its own.","whyCN":"法院与审计师需要一种说法表示「几乎全部但并非字面每一项」，于是 substantially all 成为有自身门槛的固定术语。"},{"no":"07","title":"Contributing in a significant way","titleCN":"显著贡献：对结果有实质分量","definition":"used of a contribution, meaning that it made a large and real difference to a result","definitionCN":"用于贡献，表示对结果产生了很大而真实的差别","example":"Tourism contributes substantially to the island's income.","exampleCN":"旅游业对该岛收入有显著贡献。","why":"This sense attributes weight to an actor: the contribution is not merely present but carries substance, which is why it collocates with contribute and account for.","whyCN":"这一义项把分量归给某个行为者：贡献不仅存在，而且有实质，因此常与 contribute、account for 搭配。"},{"no":"08","title":"On the whole","titleCN":"大体上：整体来看，不计细节","definition":"when considered as a whole, leaving details aside","definitionCN":"指整体来看，暂不计较细节","example":"Substantially, the report supports the earlier findings.","exampleCN":"大体上，这份报告支持此前的结论。","why":"The adverb can close a summary: it signals a judgement about the whole rather than a measurement of any single part.","whyCN":"这个副词可以用来收束总结：它标记对整体的判断，而不是对任何单一部位的测量。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Substantially is an English adverb built on substantial, from Latin substantia 'being, essence', from substare 'to stand under, be the basis', itself sub- 'under' plus stare 'to stand'. The dates below are approximate.","cn":"substantially 是英语副词，建立在 substantial 之上；substantial 出自拉丁 substantia「本质、实体」，而 substantia 出自 substare「在下面支撑、作为基础存在」，后者由 sub-「在下」与 stare「站立」构成。以下年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN STARE","en":"Latin stare 'to stand' is the base of the family, seen also in status, station, constant and instance.","cn":"拉丁 stare「站立」是整个词族的基础，也见于 status、station、constant、instance。"},{"era":"LATIN SUBSTARE","en":"substare, from sub- 'under' plus stare, meant 'to stand under, to be present as a support or basis'; its participle is substans.","cn":"substare 由 sub-「在下」与 stare 构成，意为「在下面站立、作为支撑或基础而存在」；其分词为 substans。"},{"era":"LATIN SUBSTANTIA","en":"substantia 'being, essence, substance' was formed on substans and named what stands beneath appearances.","cn":"substantia「存在、本质、实体」由 substans 构成，命名位于表象之下、支撑表象的东西。"},{"era":"SUBSTANCE AND SUBSTANTIAL","en":"Substance came through Old French; substantial followed, meaning 'having substance, real, considerable'. Substantive was kept for the separate sense 'essential, having independent standing'.","cn":"substance 经古法语进入英语；随后出现 substantial，意为「有实体的、真实的、可观的」。substantive 则保留另一义「本质的、有独立地位的」，与 substantial 分工。"},{"era":"ADVERB -LY","en":"The native ending -ly, from Old English -lice, turns substantial into an adverb of degree and essence.","cn":"本族词尾 -ly 出自古英语 -lice，把 substantial 变成表示程度与本质的副词。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"The first English citation of substantially is uncertain. The Indo-European root of stare is reconstructed as *steh₂- 'to stand', a reconstruction rather than a recorded form.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：substantially 的英语最早书证年代不明。stare 的印欧词根被重构为 *steh₂-「站立」，属重构形式，而非有记录的真实词形。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the substance family, above all substantial from substantive; the second gives near-synonyms for degree and essence.","cn":"第一组区分 substance 词族，尤其是 substantial 与 substantive；第二组给出表示程度与本质的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"substantial","ipa":"/səbˈstænʃəl/","tag":"adjective","definition":"The adjective: a substantial meal has weight and size; substantially says to what degree.","definitionCN":"形容词：a substantial meal 指一顿分量足的饭；substantially 则说明达到什么程度。"},{"word":"substantive","ipa":"/səbˈstæntɪv/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Means essential or having independent standing, especially in law and politics; it is not a degree word, so substantively different asks about content, not size.","definitionCN":"意为本质的、有独立地位的，尤用于法律与政治；它不是程度词，因此 substantively different 问的是内容，而不是大小。"},{"word":"substance","ipa":"/ˈsʌbstəns/","tag":"noun","definition":"The noun for matter or essence; it cannot stand where the adverb stands.","definitionCN":"指物质或实质的名词，不能出现在副词的位置上。"},{"word":"substantiate","ipa":"/səbˈstænʃieɪt/","tag":"verb","definition":"To prove with evidence; it concerns support for a claim, not degree.","definitionCN":"指用证据证实；它关心对主张的支持，而不是程度。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"considerably","ipa":"/kənˈsɪdərəbli/","tag":"large degree","definition":"By a large amount; close to sense 3, but it cannot mean 'in essence'.","definitionCN":"指程度很大；接近第 3 个义项，但不能表示「实质上」。"},{"word":"significantly","ipa":"/sɪɡˈnɪfɪkəntli/","tag":"important degree","definition":"By an important amount, and in research also 'with statistical significance'; substantially is about size, not tested probability.","definitionCN":"指达到重要程度，在研究语境还表示「统计显著」；substantially 说的是幅度，而不是检验出的概率。"},{"word":"largely","ipa":"/ˈlɑːdʒli/","tag":"for the most part","definition":"For the most part; it leans toward sense 8 and does not quantify a change.","definitionCN":"指大部分、主要地；它偏向第 8 个义项，并不量化变化幅度。"},{"word":"essentially","ipa":"/ɪˈsenʃəli/","tag":"in essence","definition":"In essence; it matches sense 2, but it cannot report a large increase.","definitionCN":"指本质上；它对应第 2 个义项，但不能用来报告大幅增加。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"sub- (under) + stant (standing) + -ial + -ly: what stands under the surface gives the thing its weight.","cn":"sub-（在下）+ stant（站立）+ -ial + -ly：站在表面之下者，赋予事物分量。"},{"en":"The family runs substance, substantial, substantive, substantiate, substantially.","cn":"同族词包括 substance、substantial、substantive、substantiate、substantially。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases sort the senses: rise substantially, substantially the same, substantially complete, substantially all.","cn":"固定搭配区分义项：大幅上升、基本相同、基本完成、实质全部。"},{"en":"Substantial is about weight; substantive is about content; substantially can follow either, depending on the verb.","cn":"substantial 关乎分量，substantive 关乎内容，substantially 依动词不同可承接两者。"},{"en":"Ask 'how much?' for sense 3, 'what remains?' for sense 2, and 'how whole?' for sense 8.","cn":"第 3 个义项问「多少」，第 2 个义项问「剩下什么」，第 8 个义项问「整体到什么程度」。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a solid weight sinking slowly into a scale.","cn":"想象一块实心砝码慢慢压进秤盘。"},{"en":"Picture a thick foundation under a thin wall.","cn":"想象一堵薄墙下面垫着厚厚的基础。"},{"en":"Picture a nearly full jar, with a spoonful left at the bottom.","cn":"想象一个几乎装满的罐子，底部只余一勺。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The rules changed substantially after the review.","cn":"复核之后，规则大幅改变。"},{"en":"The two paintings are substantially the same, apart from the signature.","cn":"除签名外，两幅画基本相同。"},{"en":"The work is substantially complete, though the wiring still needs a check.","cn":"工程已基本完成，只是布线仍需检查。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「substance（实质）+ ial + ly」——有实质地 → substantially 在很大程度上；实质上","word":"substantially"},"root":"拉丁 stare「站立」→ 拉丁 substare「在下面支撑、作为基础存在」→ 拉丁 substantia「本质、实体」→ 古法语 substance → 英语 substantial + -ly。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses move from degree to essence: a large amount, what remains beneath the wording, a sharp rise or fall, almost finished work, broadly the same, substantially all in law, a real contribution, and a judgement on the whole.","cn":"八个义项从程度走向本质：很大的程度、措辞之下剩下的实质、明显的涨跌、几乎完工、基本一致、法律上的实质全部、真实的贡献，以及对整体的判断。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a heavy weight rests on a scale and the beam barely moves.","cn":"核心意象：沉重的砝码压在秤上，横梁几乎不动。"},"chain":["STAND UNDER","GIVE IT WEIGHT","MEASURE THE CHANGE","NEARLY WHOLE","ALL BUT A FEW","JUDGE THE WHOLE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S3","en":"DEGREE: the amount is large, whether it rises or falls.","cn":"程度：无论上升还是下降，幅度都很大。"},{"senses":"S2 · S5","en":"ESSENCE: what stands beneath the wording, and differences too small to matter.","cn":"本质：措辞之下真正存在的东西，以及小到无关紧要的差异。"},{"senses":"S4 · S6","en":"THRESHOLDS: nearly complete work, and substantially all in law.","cn":"门槛：几乎完成的工作，以及法律上的实质全部。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"CONTRIBUTION: the actor's share carries real weight.","cn":"贡献：行为者所占的份额具有真实分量。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"THE WHOLE: a summary judgement that leaves details aside.","cn":"整体：撇开细节作出的总结性判断。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Substantially is a Latin core with two English layers: substantia 'essence', the adjective ending -al, and the native adverb ending -ly.","cn":"substantially 以拉丁成分为核心，外加两层英语构词：substantia「本质」，形容词词尾 -al，以及本族副词词尾 -ly。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin sub- 'under' and stare 'to stand' combine in substare 'stand under, be the basis', whose participle substans gives substantia; -al is Latin -alis, while -ly is native.","cn":"拉丁 sub-「在下」与 stare「站立」合成 substare「在下面站立、作为基础」，其分词 substans 构成 substantia；-al 出自拉丁 -alis，而 -ly 为本族词尾。"},"items":[{"word":"substantially","structure":"substantial + -ly (manner adverb)","meaning":"to a large degree; in essence","meaningCN":"在很大程度上；实质上","example":"Prices rose substantially in the first quarter.","exampleCN":"第一季度价格大幅上涨。"},{"word":"substantial","structure":"substance + -ial (relating to)","meaning":"large, solid or essential","meaningCN":"大量的；坚实的；实质的","example":"A substantial deposit is required.","exampleCN":"需要一笔可观的定金。"},{"word":"substance","structure":"Latin substantia (essence)","meaning":"matter or essential nature","meaningCN":"物质；本质","example":"The substance of the argument is simple.","exampleCN":"这场论证的实质很简单。"},{"word":"substantive","structure":"Latin substantivus, from substantia","meaning":"essential, independent","meaningCN":"实质性的；独立的","example":"The talks produced no substantive agreement.","exampleCN":"会谈没有产生实质性的协议。"},{"word":"substantiate","structure":"substance + -iate (to give substance)","meaning":"to support with evidence","meaningCN":"用证据证实","example":"He could not substantiate the claim.","exampleCN":"他无法证实这一说法。"},{"word":"substantiality","structure":"substantial + -ity (quality noun)","meaning":"the quality of having substance","meaningCN":"有实体的性质；实质性","example":"The substantiality of the evidence was questioned.","exampleCN":"证据的实质性受到质疑。"},{"word":"insubstantial","structure":"in- (not) + substantial","meaning":"thin, slight or unreal","meaningCN":"单薄的；微不足道的；不实在的","example":"The meal was tasty but insubstantial.","exampleCN":"这顿饭味道不错，但分量不足。"},{"word":"substantial evidence","structure":"fixed phrase: substantial + evidence","meaning":"a legal standard of adequate proof","meaningCN":"法律上「充分证据」的标准","example":"The court found substantial evidence for the ruling.","exampleCN":"法院认为该裁决有充分证据支持。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"substare","structure":"sub- (under) + stare (to stand)","meaning":"to stand under, be the basis","meaningCN":"在下面站立；作为基础存在"},{"word":"substantia","structure":"substans, substantis (present participle) + -ia","meaning":"being, essence, substance","meaningCN":"存在；本质；实体"},{"word":"-alis","structure":"-alis, -ale (adjective suffix)","meaning":"belonging to, relating to","meaningCN":"属于……的；与……有关的"}]}},{"word":"substitution","ipa_uk":"/ˌsʌbstɪˈtjuːʃən/","ipa_us":"/ˌsʌbstɪˈtuːʃən/","definition_zh":"替换；代替；代换；（数学）代入；（化学）取代；（体育）换人","definition_en":"the act of putting one person or thing in the place of another","core_image":"棋盘上一枚棋子被另一枚同色棋子换下，方格上的位置标记保持不变","scene":"The coach made a substitution at halftime to strengthen the midfield.","sceneCN":"这里 substitution 是「体育换人」（第 4 个义项：比赛中用替补球员换下场上球员）；句意：教练在半场换人，以加强中场。图中可辨识物件：边线旁的换人牌、第四官员、被换下的球员、替补球员，以及保持不动的中场站位标记。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"替换；代替；代换；（数学）代入；（化学）取代；（体育）换人（指行为时可数，指过程或概念时多不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"substitution effect","zh":"替代效应"},{"phrase":"substitution cipher","zh":"替换密码"},{"phrase":"nucleophilic substitution","zh":"亲核取代"},{"phrase":"substitution rate","zh":"替换率；替代速率"},{"phrase":"make a substitution","zh":"进行换人"},{"phrase":"substitution drill","zh":"替换练习"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多次替换）","form":"substitutions（替换；换人次数）"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"substitute（用……代替；代替）"},{"label":"名词（替代者）","form":"substitute（替代者；替补）"},{"label":"形容词（可替代的）","form":"substitutable（可被替代的）"},{"label":"形容词（替换的）","form":"substitutional（替换的；替代的）"},{"label":"形容词（取代的）","form":"substitutive（取代的；替代性的）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"substitute","pos":"v./n.","zh":"用……代替；替代者；替补"},{"word":"substitutable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可替代的"},{"word":"substitutional","pos":"adj.","zh":"替换的；替代的"},{"word":"substitutive","pos":"adj.","zh":"取代的；替代性的"},{"word":"substitutability","pos":"n.","zh":"可替代性"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Putting one thing in another's place","titleCN":"替换行为：以他物占据其位","definition":"the act of using one person or thing in place of another","definitionCN":"用一个人或物代替另一个的行为","example":"The substitution of fresh herbs for dried ones changed the dish.","exampleCN":"用新鲜香草代替干香草改变了这道菜。","why":"Latin substituere meant 'to set one thing under or in place of another'; the noun names that placing, not the thing placed.","whyCN":"拉丁 substituere 意为「把一物置于另一物之下或其位」，名词命名这一放置动作，而不是被放置之物。"},{"no":"02","title":"Substitution into an equation","titleCN":"数学代入：把值放进变量的位置","definition":"in algebra, the replacement of a variable by a number or expression","definitionCN":"在代数中用数值或表达式替换变量","example":"Substitution of x = 3 gives the value of the expression.","exampleCN":"代入 x = 3 即可得到该表达式的值。","why":"Mathematics adopted the word for the mechanical act of putting a value where a symbol stood, which is the literal Latin image of placing one thing in another's position.","whyCN":"数学采用该词表示把数值放到符号原先所在位置的机械动作，这正是拉丁语「置一物于其位」的字面意象。"},{"no":"03","title":"A chemical substitution reaction","titleCN":"化学取代：基团被另一基团换下","definition":"a reaction in which one atom or group in a molecule is replaced by another","definitionCN":"分子中一个原子或基团被另一个所替换的反应","example":"Nucleophilic substitution replaces the bromide with a hydroxyl group.","exampleCN":"亲核取代用羟基替换溴离子。","why":"Chemists keep the word because a group literally leaves and another takes its site on the carbon skeleton, so the Latin idea of placing in position fits the mechanism.","whyCN":"化学家沿用该词，是因为一个基团确实离开，另一个占据它在碳骨架上的位置，拉丁语「置于其位」的思路正好契合这一机理。"},{"no":"04","title":"A player sent on for another","titleCN":"体育换人：替补球员换下场上球员","definition":"in team sports, the replacement of one player by another during a match","definitionCN":"团队运动中在比赛进行时用一名球员换下另一名","example":"The coach made a substitution at halftime to strengthen the midfield.","exampleCN":"教练在半场换人，以加强中场。","why":"Sport borrows the general act and makes it a counted event: a team has a limited number of substitutions, so the noun names both the act and the slot used.","whyCN":"体育借用了这一一般动作，并把它变成可计数的赛事事件：球队的换人次数有限，因此名词既指动作，也指用掉的那个名额。"},{"no":"05","title":"The substitution effect in economics","titleCN":"经济学替代效应：转向更便宜的替代品","definition":"the change in demand caused by a consumer switching to a cheaper alternative when a price rises","definitionCN":"价格上涨时消费者转向更便宜替代品所引起的需求变化","example":"The substitution effect explains why sales of the cheaper brand rose.","exampleCN":"替代效应解释了为什么较便宜品牌的销量上升。","why":"Economics turns the act into a named force: one good takes the place of another in the buyer's basket, and the effect is measured separately from income.","whyCN":"经济学把这一动作变成有名称的力量：一种商品在买家的篮子里取代另一种，这一效应与收入效应分开计量。"},{"no":"06","title":"Substitution in language teaching","titleCN":"语言学替换：同一位置上换形式","definition":"in linguistics and language teaching, the replacement of one form by another in the same slot, as in a substitution drill","definitionCN":"语言学与语言教学中，用另一形式替换同一位置上的形式，如替换练习","example":"The substitution drill swaps one noun for another in the same frame.","exampleCN":"替换练习在同一句型框架内用一个名词换掉另一个。","why":"A substitution class is a set of forms that can occupy the same position; the term names the test that identifies the slot.","whyCN":"替换类指能占据同一位置的一组形式；这个术语命名识别该位置的测试。"},{"no":"07","title":"A substitution cipher","titleCN":"密码替换：按规则逐符号替换","definition":"a cipher in which each symbol or letter is replaced by another according to a fixed rule","definitionCN":"按固定规则把每个符号或字母替换成另一个的密码","example":"A simple substitution cipher is easy to break by counting letter frequencies.","exampleCN":"简单的替换密码很容易通过统计字母频率破解。","why":"The cipher is named for the operation, not the key: every unit is systematically replaced, which is the plain sense of substitutio applied to symbols.","whyCN":"这种密码因操作而得名，而非因密钥：每个单元被系统性地替换，这正是 substitutio 用于符号时的字面义。"},{"no":"08","title":"Replacing a party to a contract","titleCN":"合同主体替换：换人而不换义务","definition":"in law, the replacement of one party, debtor or obligation by another, often with the consent of the remaining party","definitionCN":"法律中用另一方替换合同一方、债务人或者义务，通常需剩余一方同意","example":"The lender agreed to the substitution of a new guarantor.","exampleCN":"贷款方同意更换新的担保人。","why":"Contract law needs a precise word for a change of person rather than of terms; substitution marks that the obligation continues while the party occupying it changes.","whyCN":"合同法需要一个精确的词来表示「换人而非换条款」；substitution 标记义务延续、占据该义务的主体发生变更。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Substitution comes from Latin substitutio, the action noun of substituere 'to set in place of another', from sub- 'under, instead of' plus statuere 'to set, make stand', which itself comes from stare 'to stand'. The dates below are approximate.","cn":"substitution 出自拉丁 substitutio，即 substituere「使替代、置于其位」的动作名词；substituere 由 sub-「在下、代替」与 statuere「安置、使站立」构成，而 statuere 又出自 stare「站立」。以下年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN STATUERE","en":"Latin statuere 'to set up, place, establish' comes from stare 'to stand' and supplies the idea of setting something in a position.","cn":"拉丁 statuere「竖立、安置、确立」出自 stare「站立」，提供「把某物放到某个位置」的思路。"},{"era":"LATIN SUBSTITUERE","en":"substituere, from sub- 'under, in place of' plus statuere, meant 'to set in place of another, put under'.","cn":"substituere 由 sub-「在下、代替」与 statuere 构成，意为「把一物置于另一物之位、置于其下」。"},{"era":"LATIN SUBSTITUTIO","en":"substitutio is the action noun of substituere, formed with -io; it names the act of setting one thing in another's place.","cn":"substitutio 是 substituere 的动作名词，以 -io 构成，命名「把一物置于另一物之位」的动作。"},{"era":"FRENCH AND ENGLISH","en":"Old French substitution and Latin substitutio supply the English noun in the fifteenth century; substitute appears first as a person and later as a verb.","cn":"古法语 substitution 与拉丁 substitutio 于十五世纪提供英语名词；substitute 先指人，后作动词。"},{"era":"SCIENTIFIC AND SPORTING SENSES","en":"Algebra, chemistry and team sport each took the word between the eighteenth and twentieth centuries because each turns a symbol, a group or a player into a replaceable slot.","cn":"代数、化学与团队运动在十八至二十世纪各自采用该词，因为它们都把符号、基团或球员变成可替换的位置。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"The first English citation of substitution is uncertain. Latin sub- has several shades, 'under' and 'instead of' among them, and which shade is primary in substituere is a matter of interpretation rather than record; the Indo-European root of stare is reconstructed as *steh₂-.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：substitution 的英语最早书证年代不明。拉丁 sub- 有数种含义，「在下」与「代替」都在其中，substituere 中哪一义为主属解释问题而非文献记录；stare 的印欧词根被重构为 *steh₂-。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the substitute family by part of speech; the second gives near-synonyms, with register and direction of change as the main differences.","cn":"第一组按词性区分 substitute 词族；第二组给出近义词，主要差别在语域与替换的方向性。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"substitute","ipa":"/ˈsʌbstɪtjuːt/","tag":"noun or verb","definition":"The stand-in or the act of standing in; substitution is the abstract noun for that act.","definitionCN":"指替代者，或指代替的动作；substitution 是表示该动作的抽象名词。"},{"word":"substitutional","ipa":"/ˌsʌbstɪˈtjuːʃənəl/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Relating to substitution, common in legal and religious language; it modifies a noun rather than naming the act.","definitionCN":"意为与替换有关的，常见于法律与宗教语言；它修饰名词，而不是命名动作。"},{"word":"substitutable","ipa":"/səbˈstɪtjuːtəbl/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Capable of being replaced; it describes a property of the thing, not the event.","definitionCN":"意为可被替代的；它描述事物的属性，而不是事件。"},{"word":"substitutive","ipa":"/ˈsʌbstɪtjuːtɪv/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Serving as a substitute; it describes the role something plays, not the act of change.","definitionCN":"意为起替代作用的；它描述某物所扮演的角色，而不是替换动作。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"replacement","ipa":"/rɪˈpleɪsmənt/","tag":"plain, often permanent","definition":"The everyday word for putting a new thing in place, often permanently; substitution is more formal and technical, and is the usual term in maths, chemistry and sport.","definitionCN":"指把新物放到原位的日常说法，常含永久替换之意；substitution 更正式、更技术化，是数学、化学与体育中的常用术语。"},{"word":"swap","ipa":"/swɒp/","tag":"casual and mutual","definition":"A casual exchange, often of two things traded for each other; substitution is one-directional and neutral in register.","definitionCN":"指随意的交换，常为两物互换；substitution 是单向的，语域中性偏正式。"},{"word":"exchange","ipa":"/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/","tag":"give and receive","definition":"Giving one thing and receiving another; substitution need not involve anything coming back.","definitionCN":"指给出一物并收到另一物；substitution 不一定涉及回返之物。"},{"word":"surrogate","ipa":"/ˈsʌrəɡət/","tag":"the stand-in","definition":"A person or thing acting in another's role, especially in medicine or law; it names the stand-in, not the act.","definitionCN":"指代替他人角色的对象，尤用于医学或法律；它命名替代者，而不是替换行为。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"sub- (in place of) + stitut (set, from statuere) + -ion: setting one thing in another's place.","cn":"sub-（代替）+ stitut（安置，出自 statuere）+ -ion：把一物置于另一物之位。"},{"en":"The family runs substitute, substitution, substitutable, substitutional, substitutive.","cn":"同族词包括 substitute、substitution、substitutable、substitutional、substitutive。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the fields: substitution effect, substitution cipher, nucleophilic substitution, make a substitution.","cn":"固定搭配标出各领域：替代效应、替换密码、亲核取代、进行换人。"},{"en":"A substitute is the stand-in; substitution is the change; substitutable is the property.","cn":"substitute 是替代者，substitution 是替换，substitutable 是可替代的性质。"},{"en":"Replacement is plain and often permanent; substitution is formal, technical and slot-based.","cn":"replacement 平实且常指永久替换；substitution 正式、技术化，并以「位置」为核心。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a chess piece lifted and another set on the same square.","cn":"想象一枚棋子被拿起，另一枚被放到同一个方格上。"},{"en":"Picture a form with a blank where a name can be written again.","cn":"想象一张表格，留有一处可以重新写名字的空白。"},{"en":"Picture a tactics board with a numbered magnet carried from the bench to the pitch.","cn":"想象战术板上，一枚编号磁子从替补席被移到球场位置。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The substitution of machine parts for manual checks speeded up production.","cn":"用机器部件替代人工检查加快了生产。"},{"en":"A substitution cipher hides the message by replacing each letter.","cn":"替换密码通过替换每个字母来隐藏信息。"},{"en":"The referee allowed the substitution after the injury.","cn":"裁判在受伤后允许换人。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「sub（下面／代替）+ stitution」——把另一个放到它的位置 → substitution 替换","word":"substitution"},"root":"拉丁 stare「站立」→ 拉丁 statuere「安置、使站立」→ 拉丁 substituere「使替代、置于其位」→ 拉丁 substitutio → 英语 substitution。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses share one act, putting one thing in another's place: plain replacement, substitution into an equation, a group taking a site in a molecule, a player coming on, the substitution effect, a language slot, a cipher alphabet and a change of contract party.","cn":"八个义项共享同一动作「把一物置于另一物之位」：一般替换、数学代入、化学基团顶替、球员上场、替代效应、语言位置、密码字母表，以及合同主体变更。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one piece is lifted and another set down on the same square.","cn":"核心意象：一枚棋子被拿起，另一枚被放到同一个方格上。"},"chain":["LIFT THE OLD","SET ANOTHER DOWN","OCCUPY THE SLOT","KEEP THE RULE","MEASURE THE SWITCH","CHANGE THE PARTY"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S7","en":"PLAIN AND CODED: one object or symbol takes another's place.","cn":"一般与编码：一个物体或符号占据另一个的位置。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"FORMAL SYSTEMS: a value enters an equation, and a group takes a site on a molecule.","cn":"形式系统：数值进入方程，基团占据分子上的位点。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"COUNTED SLOTS: a player and a basket position are swapped, with effects measured.","cn":"可计数的位置：球员与篮子中的位置被替换，并计量其效应。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"THE LANGUAGE SLOT: a form is tested by what can stand in its position.","cn":"语言位置：用一个形式能否占据该位置来检验它。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"THE LEGAL PARTY: the obligation stays, the person under it changes.","cn":"法律主体：义务保留，承担义务的人发生变更。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Substitution layers Latin sub- 'in place of', statuere 'to set', the action ending -io, and an English noun built on the Latin participle stem substitut-.","cn":"substitution 分层构成：拉丁 sub-「代替」、statuere「安置」、动作名词词尾 -io，以及建立在拉丁分词词干 substitut- 之上的英语名词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"statuere comes from stare 'to stand'; sub- adds the idea of placing under or instead, and -io forms the action noun substitutio, which reaches English as -tion.","cn":"statuere 出自 stare「站立」；sub- 附加「置于其下或代替」之意，-io 构成动作名词 substitutio，经法语进入英语作 -tion。"},"items":[{"word":"substitution","structure":"substitute + -ion (action noun)","meaning":"the act of putting one thing in another's place","meaningCN":"把一物置于另一物之位的动作","example":"No substitution of ingredients is allowed.","exampleCN":"不允许替换原料。"},{"word":"substitute","structure":"Latin substitutus (past participle)","meaning":"a stand-in, or to stand in","meaningCN":"替代者；代替","example":"Honey can substitute for sugar in this recipe.","exampleCN":"在这个食谱里，蜂蜜可以代替糖。"},{"word":"substitutable","structure":"substitute + -able (capable of)","meaning":"able to be replaced","meaningCN":"可被替代的","example":"The two parts are substitutable.","exampleCN":"这两个零件可以互换替代。"},{"word":"substitutional","structure":"substitution + -al (relating to)","meaning":"relating to substitution","meaningCN":"与替换有关的","example":"The doctrine is substitutional rather than penal.","exampleCN":"这一学说是替代性的，而非惩罚性的。"},{"word":"substitutive","structure":"substitute + -ive (serving as)","meaning":"serving as a substitute","meaningCN":"起替代作用的","example":"Substitutive therapy helps the body replace what it lacks.","exampleCN":"替代疗法帮助身体补足所缺之物。"},{"word":"substitutability","structure":"substitutable + -ity (quality noun)","meaning":"the degree to which one thing can replace another","meaningCN":"一物可替代另一物的程度","example":"Elasticity depends on the substitutability of the goods.","exampleCN":"弹性取决于商品之间的可替代性。"},{"word":"substituted","structure":"substitute + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"having been replaced by another","meaningCN":"已被另一物替代的","example":"The substituted compound behaves differently.","exampleCN":"被取代的化合物表现出不同性质。"},{"word":"substituting","structure":"substitute + -ing (present participle)","meaning":"the ongoing act of replacing","meaningCN":"正在进行的替换","example":"Substituting a symbol for a value is the first step.","exampleCN":"用符号代替数值是第一步。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"statuere","structure":"statuere, statui, statutum (third conjugation)","meaning":"to set up, place, establish","meaningCN":"竖立；安置；确立"},{"word":"substituere","structure":"sub- (under, instead of) + statuere (to set)","meaning":"to set one thing in place of another","meaningCN":"使替代；把一物置于另一物之位"},{"word":"-io","structure":"-io, -ionis (f., action noun)","meaning":"suffix naming an action","meaningCN":"命名动作的名词词尾"}]}},{"word":"successive","ipa_uk":"/səkˈsesɪv/","ipa_us":"/səkˈsesɪv/","definition_zh":"接连的；连续的；相继的；一个接一个的（强调前后相承、中间不断）","definition_en":"following one another in an unbroken order, each item coming after the one before it","core_image":"雨后的泥路上，一串脚印前一枚尚未干透，后一枚已踩上去，沿着同一条线依次伸向远处","scene":"Successive governments have promised to simplify the tax code.","sceneCN":"这里 successive 是「历届的、一届接一届的」（第 6 个义项：指前后相承的多届政府）；句意：历届政府都承诺简化税法。图中可辨识物件：一串前后相接的脚印、同一条泥路、尚未干透的鞋印、向远处延伸的路线。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"接连的；连续的；相继的；一个接一个的（通常作定语，无比较级）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"successive generations","zh":"连续几代人"},{"phrase":"successive victories","zh":"一连串胜利"},{"phrase":"successive governments","zh":"历届政府"},{"phrase":"successive layers","zh":"连续地层"},{"phrase":"successive attempts","zh":"反复的尝试"},{"phrase":"successive approximation","zh":"逐次逼近"}],"forms":[{"label":"副词形式","form":"successively（接连地；依次地）"},{"label":"名词形式","form":"succession（相继；继承）"},{"label":"名词（性质）","form":"successiveness（连续性；相继性）"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"succeed（接着；继任；成功）"},{"label":"同族形容词（勿混）","form":"successful（成功的）"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"succeeding（随后的；接着的）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"successively","pos":"adv.","zh":"接连地；依次地"},{"word":"succession","pos":"n.","zh":"相继；连续；继承"},{"word":"succeed","pos":"v.","zh":"接着；继任；成功"},{"word":"successor","pos":"n.","zh":"继任者；继承人"},{"word":"successiveness","pos":"n.","zh":"连续性；相继性"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Following with no gap","titleCN":"接连不断：中间没有间断","definition":"coming immediately after another in a series, so that each item is followed by the next without a break","definitionCN":"在一系列中紧接另一项而来，每一项后面都跟着下一项，中间没有间断","example":"The village suffered floods on three successive nights.","exampleCN":"这个村庄连续三个夜晚遭遇洪水。","why":"Latin succedere was sub- 'next to, close after' plus cedere 'to go', and its participle successivus named what comes after another. The adjective therefore begins as pure order in time, with no hint of success.","whyCN":"拉丁 succedere 由 sub-「紧接、靠近」加 cedere「走」构成，其分词形式 successivus 命名「跟在另一者之后的」，因此这个形容词的起点只是时间上的顺序，与「成功」毫无关系。"},{"no":"02","title":"Each generation in turn","titleCN":"代代相承：连续几代人","definition":"of people in a family or line, following one another generation after generation in an unbroken chain","definitionCN":"指家族或世系中的人一代接一代相随，形成未曾中断的链条","example":"Successive generations repaired the same stone walls.","exampleCN":"连续几代人都修缮着同一批石墙。","why":"When the counted units are lifetimes rather than events, the same 'coming after' stretches across decades; the word measures the chain of people, not any one person's achievement.","whyCN":"当被计数的单位是一生而不是事件时，同样的「跟在后面」便跨越数十年；这个词衡量的是人的链条，而不是某一个人的成就。"},{"no":"03","title":"A run of results or attempts","titleCN":"一连串的胜负或尝试","definition":"of repeated outcomes or efforts, occurring one after another so that they form a continuous run","definitionCN":"指反复出现的结果或努力一个接一个发生，形成连续的一串","example":"Successive defeats forced the coach to change the formation.","exampleCN":"一连串失利迫使教练改变阵型。","why":"A run is a series read as a whole; each result follows the previous one, and the adjective marks the repetition rather than the merit of any single result.","whyCN":"一连串是把系列当作整体来看；每个结果都紧跟上一个，形容词标记的是重复本身，而不是任何单个结果的好坏。"},{"no":"04","title":"Step-by-step approximation","titleCN":"逐次逼近：一步步接近答案","definition":"of a numerical method, reaching an answer through a series of estimates, each calculated from the one before, rather than by one exact operation","definitionCN":"指数值方法通过一系列估计值得到答案，每个估计值都由前一个算出，而不是一次精确运算完成","example":"Successive approximation refined the estimate until the error was negligible.","exampleCN":"逐次逼近不断修正估计值，直到误差可以忽略。","why":"In computation each estimate is fed into the next, so the method is literally a chain of followers: the second value exists because the first came before it.","whyCN":"在计算中，每个估计值都被送入下一个，这个方法字面上就是一条相随之链：第二个值之所以存在，是因为第一个先出现。"},{"no":"05","title":"Beds laid one above another","titleCN":"连续地层：一层压着一层","definition":"of rock layers, deposited one after another in an unbroken sequence, so that each bed rests on the one below","definitionCN":"指岩层一层接一层沉积，形成未中断的序列，每层都覆盖在下一层之上","example":"The cliff exposes successive beds of sandstone and shale.","exampleCN":"这处崖壁露出连续的石砂岩与页岩层。","why":"Geology reads time downward: an unbroken stack means no erosion or gap intervened, so successive layers are the physical record of events that followed one another.","whyCN":"地质学自上而下读时间：未被中断的层堆意味着中间没有侵蚀或缺失，因此连续地层就是事件相随的物理记录。"},{"no":"06","title":"Office-holders in turn","titleCN":"历届：同一职位上的前后任","definition":"of governments, presidents or other office-holders, following one another in time, each replacing the previous one in the same post","definitionCN":"指政府、总统或其他任职者按时间先后相随，每一位都在同一职位上接替前一位","example":"Successive governments have promised to simplify the tax code.","exampleCN":"历届政府都承诺简化税法。","why":"Here the series is institutional: the office outlasts its holders, and each holder follows the last in the same post; the word stresses continuity of the office, not agreement between its occupants.","whyCN":"这里的系列是制度性的：职位比任职者更长久，每一位都在同一职位上接替上一位；这个词强调职位的连续性，而不是历任者之间的意见一致。"},{"no":"07","title":"Neighbouring terms in a sequence","titleCN":"数列中的相继项","definition":"of terms in a mathematical sequence, next to each other in the ordered list, so that one position is immediately followed by the next","definitionCN":"指数列中的项在有序列表中彼此相邻，一个位置后面紧接着下一个位置","example":"The ratio of successive terms approaches a constant.","exampleCN":"相继两项的比值趋近于一个常数。","why":"Mathematics strips the word to bare adjacency: the term numbered n plus one comes after the term numbered n, and successive means exactly neighbouring positions in the list.","whyCN":"数学把这个词削减为纯粹的相邻关系：后一项紧接前一项，successive 正是指列表中相邻的位置。"},{"no":"08","title":"Small steps that add up","titleCN":"逐步累积：小变化叠加成大变化","definition":"of gradual change, accumulating through repeated small steps so that the combined effect becomes large","definitionCN":"指逐渐的变化通过反复的小步骤累积，使合起来的效果变得显著","example":"Successive cuts reduced the budget by a third over five years.","exampleCN":"连续几年的削减使预算在五年内减少了三分之一。","why":"Each step is small, but because the steps follow without interruption their effects add; this sense names cumulative change rather than mere repetition.","whyCN":"每一步都很小，但因为这些步骤不间断地相随，效果便叠加起来；这一义项命名的是累积变化，而不只是重复。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Successive is the English adjective of a Latin line running from cedere 'to go' through succedere 'to come after' to late Latin successivus. English took it through French, and its meaning has stayed close to 'following'.","cn":"successive 是拉丁词线在英语中的形容词：从 cedere「走」到 succedere「跟在后面」，再到晚期拉丁 successivus。英语经法语借入，词义始终贴近「相随」。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN CEDERE","en":"Latin cedere meant 'to go, withdraw, yield'. It supplies the -cess- element in cede, proceed, recess and succession. Its deeper origin is disputed.","cn":"拉丁 cedere 意为「走、退、让」，为 cede、proceed、recess、succession 提供 -cess- 这一成分；其更深来源有争议。"},{"era":"LATIN SUCCEDERE","en":"The compound succedere joins sub- 'next to, close after' with cedere 'to go', giving 'to come or go after, follow, take the place of'. The verb is well attested in classical Latin.","cn":"复合词 succedere 把 sub-「紧接、靠近」与 cedere「走」结合，得到「跟在后面、随之而来、接替」之义；该动词在古典拉丁语中有充分记录。"},{"era":"LATIN SUCCESSIVUS","en":"Successus, the past participle of succedere, also served as a noun meaning 'a following, an outcome'. Late Latin formed successivus 'following in order' on that stem; this is the direct source of the English adjective.","cn":"successus 既是 succedere 的过去分词，也作名词表示「相随、结果」。晚期拉丁语在该词干上构成 successivus「依次相随的」，它正是英语形容词的直接来源。"},{"era":"FRENCH AND ENGLISH","en":"Old French successif, successive carried the adjective into English in the late Middle Ages. The earliest English citation is not securely dated.","cn":"古法语 successif、successive 在中世纪晚期把这个形容词带入英语；英语最早书证年代不确切。"},{"era":"SPLIT FROM SUCCESSFUL","en":"English later gave success the sense 'a favourable outcome' and built successful 'having success'. Successive never took that sense: it still means only 'following one after another'. The two words share a Latin parent but have divided meanings.","cn":"英语后来让 success 获得「有利结果」之义，并构成 successful「获得成功的」。successive 从未取得这一义项，仍只表示「一个接一个」。两个词共享拉丁语来源，语义却已分叉。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"First citation uncertain: the earliest English use of successive has no secure date. Root uncertain: the deeper origin of Latin cedere is disputed, and no confirmed Indo-European reconstruction can be given.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：successive 的英语最早书证年代不确定。来源不确定（词根）：拉丁 cedere 的更深词源有争议，无法给出已确证的原印欧语形式。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the Latin family by part of speech and guards against the false friend successful; the second gives near-synonyms for ordered repetition.","cn":"第一组按词性区分这个拉丁词族，并防止把 successful 当作同义词；第二组给出表示「有序重复」的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"succession","ipa":"/səkˈseʃən/","tag":"noun","definition":"The process or series of things following one another, or the right to take over an office. Successive is the adjective describing that order.","definitionCN":"指事物相随的过程或系列，也指接任职位的权利；successive 是描述这一顺序的形容词。"},{"word":"succeed","ipa":"/səkˈsiːd/","tag":"verb","definition":"To come after another in time or rank, and also, by a later English development, to achieve a goal. Successive carries only the first sense.","definitionCN":"指在时间或位次上接续另一者，后来又经英语自身发展出「达到目标」之义；successive 只保留前一义。"},{"word":"successful","ipa":"/səkˈsesfəl/","tag":"false friend","definition":"Achieving what was wanted. It shares the Latin parent but not the meaning: successive means 'one after another', never 'having succeeded'.","definitionCN":"指达成所愿；它与 successive 共享拉丁语来源，但词义不同：successive 意为「一个接一个」，绝不是「成功的」。"},{"word":"successively","ipa":"/səkˈsesɪvli/","tag":"adverb","definition":"The adverb of manner meaning 'one after another'. It modifies a verb, while successive modifies a noun.","definitionCN":"方式副词，意为「一个接一个地」；它修饰动词，而 successive 修饰名词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"consecutive","ipa":"/kənˈsekjətɪv/","tag":"no interval between","definition":"Following in an unbroken sequence, especially of days, numbers or games. It stresses that no interval intervenes, close to the core of successive.","definitionCN":"指以未中断的顺序相随，尤用于天数、数字或比赛；它强调中间没有间隔，与 successive 的核心义接近。"},{"word":"sequential","ipa":"/sɪˈkwenʃəl/","tag":"in a set order","definition":"Arranged in a fixed order, one after another. It emphasises the order of steps rather than the absence of gaps.","definitionCN":"指按固定次序一个接一个排列；它强调步骤的次序，而不是有没有间隔。"},{"word":"serial","ipa":"/ˈsɪəriəl/","tag":"a repeated series","definition":"Occurring in a series, often with the idea of repetition or instalments. It can suggest monotony that successive does not.","definitionCN":"指成系列发生，常带重复或分期的意味；它可能暗示单调，而 successive 没有这层含义。"},{"word":"repeated","ipa":"/rɪˈpiːtɪd/","tag":"done again","definition":"Done or occurring again, without necessarily forming an ordered chain. Successive implies order; repeated only implies recurrence.","definitionCN":"指再次发生，但不一定构成有序链条；successive 含顺序，repeated 只含再次发生。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"sub- plus cedere: to go right behind someone, so one comes after another.","cn":"sub- 加 cedere：紧跟在别人后面走，于是一个接着一个。"},{"en":"The family runs succeed, succession, successive, successively, successor.","cn":"同族词包括 succeed、succession、successive、successively、successor。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the range: successive generations, successive governments, successive layers, successive approximation.","cn":"固定搭配标出范围：连续几代人、历届政府、连续地层、逐次逼近。"},{"en":"Successive and successful share a Latin parent but never share a meaning: one is order, the other is victory.","cn":"successive 与 successful 共享拉丁语来源却从不共享词义：一个讲顺序，一个讲胜利。"},{"en":"In mathematics it means neighbouring terms; in geology it means neighbouring beds; in politics it means neighbouring administrations.","cn":"在数学里指相邻的项，在地质里指相邻的层，在政治里指相邻的届。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture footprints pressed one into the next along a wet path.","cn":"想象湿泥路上脚印一枚压着一枚向前延伸。"},{"en":"Picture stair treads rising one above another with no landing between them.","cn":"想象楼梯的踏板一级高过一级，中间没有平台。"},{"en":"Picture dominoes falling in a line, each pushed by the one before.","cn":"想象多米诺骨牌沿一条线倒下，每一张都被前一张推倒。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The plant flowered on three successive mornings, each bloom lasting a single day.","cn":"这株植物连续三个早晨开花，每朵花只开一天。"},{"en":"Successive approximations brought the calculated orbit closer to the observed one.","cn":"逐次逼近使计算出的轨道越来越接近观测轨道。"},{"en":"Successive administrations left the bridge unrepaired.","cn":"历届政府都没有修这座桥。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「success（成功）+ ive」是假朋友：successive 只表示「接连的、相继的」，与「成功」无关","word":"successive"},"root":"拉丁 sub-「接近、接着」+ cedere「走、让」→ succedere「跟在后面、接替」→ 拉丁 successus（过去分词）→ 晚期拉丁 successivus「依次相随的」→ 英语 successive；首见年代存疑。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one idea at different scales: a plain run in time, a chain of generations, a run of outcomes, a stepwise calculation, a stack of rock beds, a line of office-holders, neighbouring terms in a sequence, and change that accumulates.","cn":"八个义项是同一思路在不同尺度上的展开：时间上的连续、世代链条、结果的连串、逐步计算、岩层叠加、历任职位、数列相邻项，以及逐步累积的变化。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one item follows another with no gap, like footprints on one path.","cn":"核心意象：一物紧接一物、中间无间隙，如同一条路上的脚印。"},"chain":["ONE AFTER ANOTHER","NO GAP","ACROSS GENERATIONS","A RUN OF RESULTS","STEP INTO STEP","EFFECTS ACCUMULATE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S7","en":"PURE ADJACENCY: items sit next to each other in time or in an ordered list.","cn":"纯粹相邻：各项在时间上或在有序列表中彼此紧挨。"},{"senses":"S2","en":"THE FAMILY CHAIN: each generation follows the previous one without a break.","cn":"家族链条：每一代都紧接上一代，未曾中断。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"A RUN READ AS A WHOLE: victories, defeats or attempts form one continuous series.","cn":"作为整体的一串：胜利、失利或尝试构成一个连续的系列。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"STEPWISE ORDER: a calculation feeds each estimate into the next, and rock beds stack in depositional order.","cn":"逐步次序：计算把每个估计值送入下一个，岩层则按沉积顺序层层叠加。"},{"senses":"S6 · S8","en":"INSTITUTIONS AND ACCUMULATION: offices pass from holder to holder, and small steps add into a large effect.","cn":"制度与累积：职位在历任者之间传递，小步骤则叠加成大效果。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Successive is a Latin adjective rebuilt in English: sub- 'next to' plus cedere 'to go' plus the adjective ending -ivus, which reached English as -ive.","cn":"successive 是在英语中重建的拉丁形容词：sub-「紧接」加 cedere「走」，再加形容词词尾 -ivus，后者进入英语作 -ive。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin core is cedere 'to go, yield', with the prefix sub- 'next to, close after' and the adjective ending -ivus. The deeper origin of cedere is disputed, so only the attested Latin forms are listed.","cn":"拉丁核心是 cedere「走、让」，前缀 sub- 表示「紧接、靠近」，形容词词尾为 -ivus。cedere 的更深词源有争议，因此这里只列有记录的拉丁形式。"},"items":[{"word":"successive","structure":"success(us) + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"following one after another","meaningCN":"一个接一个的；相继的","example":"The team lost on three successive weekends.","exampleCN":"这支队伍连续三个周末失利。"},{"word":"succession","structure":"success(us) + -ion (action noun)","meaning":"a following; the right to take over","meaningCN":"相随；接任的权利","example":"The succession of seasons governs the harvest.","exampleCN":"季节的相继决定着收成。"},{"word":"succeed","structure":"sub- (next to) + cedere (to go)","meaning":"to come after; to take the place of","meaningCN":"接着；接替","example":"A new director succeeded the founder.","exampleCN":"一位新主管接替了创始人。"},{"word":"successor","structure":"succeed + -or (agent noun)","meaning":"one who follows in an office","meaningCN":"继任者；接班人","example":"Her successor took office in January.","exampleCN":"她的继任者在一月上任。"},{"word":"success","structure":"successus (past participle used as a noun)","meaning":"a favourable outcome","meaningCN":"成功；有利结果","example":"The experiment was a success.","exampleCN":"这次实验成功了。"},{"word":"successful","structure":"success + -ful (having)","meaning":"having achieved what was wanted","meaningCN":"获得成功的","example":"The campaign was successful in raising funds.","exampleCN":"这场活动成功筹到了资金。"},{"word":"successively","structure":"successive + -ly (manner adverb)","meaning":"one after another","meaningCN":"接连地；依次地","example":"The three gates open successively.","exampleCN":"三道闸门依次打开。"},{"word":"concession","structure":"con- (together) + cedere (yield) + -ion","meaning":"something granted or yielded","meaningCN":"让步；让与物","example":"The treaty included a territorial concession.","exampleCN":"条约包含一项领土让与。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"cedere","structure":"cedere, cessi, cessum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to go, withdraw, yield","meaningCN":"走；退；让"},{"word":"succedere","structure":"sub- + cedere (compound verb)","meaning":"to follow after, take the place of","meaningCN":"跟在后面；接替"},{"word":"successivus","structure":"success- + -ivus (adjective)","meaning":"following in order","meaningCN":"依次相随的"}]}},{"word":"succession","ipa_uk":"/səkˈseʃən/","ipa_us":"/səkˈseʃən/","definition_zh":"相继；连续；一连串（事件）；继承；继承顺序；生态演替","definition_en":"the fact or process of one thing following another, or the right and order by which a person takes over an office, title or property","core_image":"接力赛中，一根接力棒从一只手中递到下一只手中，跑者依次接替，编号沿着赛道向前排开","scene":"The line of succession was unclear after the president resigned.","sceneCN":"这里 succession 是「继承顺序」（第 2 个义项：规定继任者先后次序的规则）；句意：总统辞职后，继承顺序并不明确。图中可辨识物件：接力棒、交握又松开的两只手、依次起跑的跑者、画着编号的赛道。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"相继；连续；一连串（事件）；继承；继承顺序；生态演替（指过程时多不可数，指一连串事件时可用「a succession of」）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"line of succession","zh":"继承顺序"},{"phrase":"a succession of","zh":"一连串的"},{"phrase":"ecological succession","zh":"生态演替"},{"phrase":"succession planning","zh":"继任规划"},{"phrase":"order of succession","zh":"继位次序"},{"phrase":"succession crisis","zh":"继承危机"}],"forms":[{"label":"形容词形式","form":"successive（连续的；相继的）"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"succeed（接着；继任；成功）"},{"label":"名词（继任者）","form":"successor（继任者；继承人）"},{"label":"形容词（成功的）","form":"successful（成功的）"},{"label":"复数","form":"successions（多次相继；多个继承系列）"},{"label":"副词形式","form":"successively（接连地；依次地）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"successive","pos":"adj.","zh":"连续的；相继的"},{"word":"succeed","pos":"v.","zh":"接着；继任；成功"},{"word":"successor","pos":"n.","zh":"继任者；继承人"},{"word":"successful","pos":"adj.","zh":"成功的"},{"word":"success","pos":"n.","zh":"成功；有利结果"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"One thing after another","titleCN":"相继发生：一物接着一物","definition":"the process by which one thing follows another in time, without a break","definitionCN":"指一物在时间上接着另一物发生、中间没有中断的过程","example":"The succession of seasons sets the rhythm of farm work.","exampleCN":"季节的相继决定了农活的节奏。","why":"Latin successio was the abstract noun of succedere 'to come after'; it named the act of following before it named any particular institution.","whyCN":"拉丁 successio 是 succedere「跟在后面」的抽象名词，先命名「相随」这一动作，后来才用于各种具体制度。"},{"no":"02","title":"The ranked order of heirs","titleCN":"继承顺序：谁依次接任","definition":"the fixed order in which people are entitled to take over a throne, title or office as each holder dies or leaves","definitionCN":"指在位者去世或离任时，人们按固定次序接掌王位、头衔或职位的规则","example":"The duke was third in the line of succession.","exampleCN":"这位公爵在继承顺序中排在第三。","why":"An office outlives its holder, so the order of followers becomes a rule; the noun shifts from the event of following to the ranked list of who follows.","whyCN":"职位比任职者长久，于是相随的次序变成规则；名词从「相随事件」转为「谁接谁的排序名单」。"},{"no":"03","title":"A series of events","titleCN":"一连串事件","definition":"a series of similar events or things, one following another, especially in the pattern 'a succession of'","definitionCN":"指同类事件或事物一个接一个形成的一串，尤见于「a succession of」这一结构","example":"A succession of storms battered the coast for a week.","exampleCN":"一连串风暴袭击海岸达一周之久。","why":"English uses the countable pattern 'a succession of X' for a run of events; the same noun that names the process now names the series produced by it.","whyCN":"英语用可数的「a succession of」结构指一连串事件；原本命名过程的名词，此时命名由过程产生的那一串。"},{"no":"04","title":"Communities replacing communities","titleCN":"生态演替：群落依次更替","definition":"the gradual replacement of one community of plants and animals by another on the same site until a stable community forms","definitionCN":"指同一地点上一种动植物群落逐渐被另一种取代，直到形成稳定群落","example":"Ecological succession turns bare rock into forest over centuries.","exampleCN":"生态演替历经数百年，把裸岩变成森林。","why":"Botanists borrowed the word because each plant community literally follows the previous one; the sequence is a succession of occupants of one place.","whyCN":"植物学家借用这个词，是因为每一个植物群落都字面意义上接替前一个；这一序列就是同一地点的占据者相继更替。"},{"no":"05","title":"Planning who comes next","titleCN":"继任规划：预先安排接班人","definition":"the deliberate preparation of people to take over key posts, and the plan that sets out who will follow whom","definitionCN":"指有意识地培养人员接掌关键职位，以及规定谁接替谁的方案","example":"The board began succession planning long before the chief executive retired.","exampleCN":"董事会早在首席执行官退休之前就开始了继任规划。","why":"Businesses turned the legal idea of orderly inheritance into planning for posts: who will follow, and how they are prepared.","whyCN":"商界把法律上有序继承的观念转化为职位规划：谁来接替，以及如何培养。"},{"no":"06","title":"Chords following chords","titleCN":"音乐中的连续进行","definition":"an ordered progression of chords or notes in which each follows the previous one in time","definitionCN":"指和弦或音符按时间顺序依次相接形成的有序进行","example":"The fugue is built on a succession of chords rather than a single tune.","exampleCN":"这首赋格建立在连续的和弦进行上，而不是单一旋律上。","why":"Theory speaks of chords following one another in time; the term names an ordered progression, not a story or a legal right.","whyCN":"乐理研究和弦在时间上一个接一个地出现；这个词命名的是有序进行，而不是故事或法律权利。"},{"no":"07","title":"Inheritance fixed by law","titleCN":"法定继承：依法转移财产或头衔","definition":"the transfer of property or a title to heirs according to law, especially when there is no will","definitionCN":"指财产或头衔依法转移给继承人，尤指没有遗嘱的情形","example":"Succession to the estate passed to the eldest daughter by law.","exampleCN":"依照法律，遗产的继承权归长女所有。","why":"Law fixes what happens when someone dies without a will; property passes by statutory succession, which is the oldest institutional sense of the word.","whyCN":"法律规定了无遗嘱死亡时如何处理；财产依法定继承转移，这是这个词最古老的制度义项。"},{"no":"08","title":"When the order breaks down","titleCN":"权力交接危机：继承秩序失灵","definition":"a dispute or breakdown over who should take over a position of power, especially when the expected order fails","definitionCN":"指围绕谁应接掌权力职位产生的争执或秩序崩溃，尤指预期顺序失效之时","example":"The party plunged into a succession crisis when the leader died without naming an heir.","exampleCN":"领导人去世却没有指定继承人，该党随即陷入继承危机。","why":"When the expected order of following breaks down, the process becomes a crisis; the noun then names the disputed transfer itself.","whyCN":"当预期的相随次序崩溃时，这一过程就变成危机；名词此时命名的正是那场有争议的交接本身。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Succession is the Latin action noun of succedere, built with -io on the same sub- plus cedere compound that gave successive. It reached English through Old French and kept both the temporal and the legal senses.","cn":"succession 是 succedere 的拉丁动作名词，与 successive 同出 sub- 加 cedere 的复合词，以 -io 构成。它经古法语进入英语，同时保留时间与法律两类义项。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN CEDERE","en":"Latin cedere meant 'to go, withdraw, yield' and supplies the -cess- element of succession, cede, proceed and recess. Its deeper origin is disputed.","cn":"拉丁 cedere 意为「走、退、让」，为 succession、cede、proceed、recess 提供 -cess- 成分；其更深来源有争议。"},{"era":"LATIN SUCCEDERE","en":"Succedere joins sub- 'next to, close after' with cedere 'to go', giving 'to come after, follow, take the place of'. It is well attested in classical Latin.","cn":"succedere 把 sub-「紧接、靠近」与 cedere「走」结合，得到「跟在后面、随之而来、接替」之义，在古典拉丁语中有充分记录。"},{"era":"LATIN SUCCESSIO","en":"Successio, successionis (f.) was the abstract noun of succedere: 'a following, a succession, an inheritance'. The ending -io names the act or its result, which is why the word can mean both the process and the thing handed over.","cn":"successio（属格 successionis，阴性）是 succedere 的抽象名词，意为「相随、相继、继承」。词尾 -io 命名动作或其结果，因此这个词既能指过程，也能指被移交之物。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH AND ENGLISH","en":"Old French succession carried the word into English, where it is generally dated to the thirteenth century. It named both following in time and the right to inherit an office.","cn":"古法语 succession 把这个词带入英语，一般定为十三世纪。它既指时间上的相随，也指接任职位的权利。"},{"era":"LAW, ECOLOGY AND BUSINESS","en":"Canon and civil law fixed successio for the transfer of an office or benefice, and the phrase line of succession comes from that usage. Botany applied the word to the replacement of plant communities in the late nineteenth and early twentieth centuries, and business later coined succession planning.","cn":"教会法与民法把 successio 固定用于职位或教职的转移，line of succession 即出自这一用法。植物学在十九世纪末、二十世纪初用该词指植物群落的更替，商界后来造出 succession planning。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"First citation uncertain: the earliest English use of succession has no secure date. Root uncertain: the deeper origin of Latin cedere is disputed, and no confirmed Indo-European reconstruction can be given.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：succession 的英语最早书证年代不确定。来源不确定（词根）：拉丁 cedere 的更深词源有争议，无法给出已确证的原印欧语形式。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the Latin family and keeps the legal noun apart from its adjective and verb; the second gives near-synonyms for a series and for inheritance.","cn":"第一组区分这个拉丁词族，并把法律名词与它的形容词、动词分开；第二组给出表示「系列」与「继承」的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"successive","ipa":"/səkˈsesɪv/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Describes things following one another, as in successive layers. Succession is the noun for the process or the right to take over.","definitionCN":"形容词，描述一个接一个的事物，如连续地层；succession 是表示过程或接任权利的名词。"},{"word":"succeed","ipa":"/səkˈsiːd/","tag":"verb","definition":"To follow in an office, and later also to achieve a goal. The noun succession keeps only the first branch.","definitionCN":"动词，指接任职位，后来又指达成目标；名词 succession 只保留前一分支。"},{"word":"successor","ipa":"/səkˈsesə/","tag":"person","definition":"The person who takes over. Succession is the process or right; a successor is the individual who exercises it.","definitionCN":"指接任的人；succession 是过程或权利，successor 是行使这一权利的具体个人。"},{"word":"success","ipa":"/səkˈses/","tag":"outcome noun","definition":"A favourable outcome, a later English sense. It is not a synonym of succession, which is about order and transfer.","definitionCN":"指有利结果，是英语后起的义项；它不是 succession 的同义词，后者讲的是次序与转移。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"sequence","ipa":"/ˈsiːkwəns/","tag":"ordered set","definition":"A set of things arranged in a particular order. It names the arrangement, while succession often implies that each item replaces the previous one.","definitionCN":"指按特定次序排列的一组事物；它命名排列方式，而 succession 常含「后者取代前者」之意。"},{"word":"series","ipa":"/ˈsɪəriːz/","tag":"connected run","definition":"A number of similar things coming one after another. It is broader and does not carry the legal or ecological senses.","definitionCN":"指若干同类事物一个接一个出现；它更宽泛，不带法律或生态义项。"},{"word":"inheritance","ipa":"/ɪnˈherɪtəns/","tag":"what is received","definition":"Property, money or qualities received from a predecessor. It focuses on what is received, while succession focuses on the right and order of receiving.","definitionCN":"指从前人那里得到的财产、金钱或特质；它侧重所得之物，而 succession 侧重取得的法律权利与次序。"},{"word":"handover","ipa":"/ˈhændəʊvə/","tag":"the act of transfer","definition":"The practical act of giving power or responsibility to someone else. Succession can be a right or a plan; a handover is the event itself.","definitionCN":"指把权力或职责实际交给他人；succession 可以是权利或方案，handover 则是交接事件本身。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"sub- plus cedere plus -ion: the act of going right after someone.","cn":"sub- 加 cedere 再加 -ion：紧跟在某人之后走的那一动作。"},{"en":"The family runs succeed, successor, successive, successively, success.","cn":"同族词包括 succeed、successor、successive、successively、success。"},{"en":"Three fixed phrases mark three worlds: line of succession in law, ecological succession in biology, succession planning in business.","cn":"三个固定搭配标出三个领域：法律中的继承顺序、生物学中的生态演替、商业中的继任规划。"},{"en":"A relay race is the clearest picture: the baton is handed on, and the order of runners is fixed in advance.","cn":"接力赛是最清楚的画面：接力棒被交下去，跑者次序事先排定。"},{"en":"Succession is the noun of order and transfer; success is the noun of a favourable result. Keep them apart.","cn":"succession 是次序与转移的名词，success 是结果有利的名词；要把它们分开。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a baton passing from hand to hand along a numbered track.","cn":"想象一根接力棒沿编号赛道从一只手传到另一只手。"},{"en":"Picture a throne room where the names of heirs are written in a fixed column.","cn":"想象王座厅里，继承人的名字被写进一列固定的名单。"},{"en":"Picture a bare field passing through grass, shrubs and finally forest.","cn":"想象一片裸地依次经过草地、灌木，最后变成森林。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The empire survived a long succession of weak rulers.","cn":"这个帝国熬过了一长串软弱的统治者。"},{"en":"Ecological succession on the lava flow has been studied for a century.","cn":"熔岩流上的生态演替已被研究了一个世纪。"},{"en":"Good succession planning keeps an organization steady when a leader leaves.","cn":"良好的继任规划能在领导者离任时让组织保持稳定。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「success（成功）+ ion」是假朋友：succession 主要表示「相继、继承」，不是「成功」","word":"succession"},"root":"拉丁 sub-「接近、接着」+ cedere「走、让」→ succedere「跟在后面、接替」→ 拉丁 successio「相继、继承」→ 古法语 succession → 英语 succession；首见年代存疑。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses run from plain following, through the ranked line of heirs and a run of events, to plant communities, corporate planning, chord progressions, statutory inheritance and the breakdown of orderly transfer.","cn":"八个义项从单纯的相随出发，经过继承人排序与事件连串，延伸到植物群落、企业规划、和弦进行、法定继承，以及有序交接的崩溃。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a baton is handed on, and the order of runners is fixed beforehand.","cn":"核心意象：接力棒被交下去，跑者次序事先排定。"},"chain":["ONE FOLLOWS ANOTHER","THE ORDER IS FIXED","A RUN OF EVENTS","COMMUNITIES REPLACE COMMUNITIES","PLAN WHO COMES NEXT","THE ORDER BREAKS"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S3","en":"PROCESS AND SERIES: following in time, and the countable run that the process produces.","cn":"过程与系列：时间上的相随，以及由此产生的可数一连串。"},{"senses":"S2 · S7","en":"THE LEGAL ORDER: a ranked line of heirs and the statutory transfer of property.","cn":"法律次序：继承人排序，以及财产的法定转移。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"ECOLOGICAL REPLACEMENT: one community of organisms follows another on the same ground.","cn":"生态更替：同一片土地上的生物群落依次取代。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"PLANNED AND MUSICAL ORDER: posts are prepared for successors, and chords follow chords.","cn":"规划中的与音乐中的次序：为接班人预备职位，和弦则依次相接。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"BROKEN ORDER: the expected transfer fails and becomes a crisis.","cn":"断裂的次序：预期的交接失效，变成危机。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Succession is a Latin action noun: the verb succedere plus the noun ending -io, which reached English as -ion through French.","cn":"succession 是拉丁动作名词：动词 succedere 加名词词尾 -io，后者经法语进入英语作 -ion。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin elements are sub- 'next to', cedere 'to go, yield' and the action-noun ending -io. Cedere also supplies cede, concession and procession; its deeper origin is disputed.","cn":"拉丁成分是 sub-「紧接」、cedere「走、让」与动作名词词尾 -io。cedere 还提供 cede、concession、procession；其更深来源有争议。"},"items":[{"word":"succession","structure":"success(us) + -ion (action noun)","meaning":"a following; the right to take over","meaningCN":"相随；接任的权利","example":"The succession of dry years ruined the harvest.","exampleCN":"连续几年的干旱毁了收成。"},{"word":"succeed","structure":"sub- (next to) + cedere (to go)","meaning":"to come after; to take the place of","meaningCN":"接着；接替","example":"One generation succeeds another.","exampleCN":"一代接替一代。"},{"word":"successive","structure":"success(us) + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"following one after another","meaningCN":"接连的；相继的","example":"They met on three successive days.","exampleCN":"他们连续三天见面。"},{"word":"successor","structure":"succeed + -or (agent noun)","meaning":"one who follows in an office","meaningCN":"继任者；接班人","example":"The successor inherited a difficult budget.","exampleCN":"继任者接手了一份困难的预算。"},{"word":"success","structure":"successus (past participle used as a noun)","meaning":"a favourable outcome","meaningCN":"成功；有利结果","example":"The negotiation ended in success.","exampleCN":"谈判以成功告终。"},{"word":"successful","structure":"success + -ful (having)","meaning":"having achieved what was wanted","meaningCN":"获得成功的","example":"She made a successful appeal.","exampleCN":"她的申诉获得了成功。"},{"word":"successively","structure":"successive + -ly (manner adverb)","meaning":"one after another","meaningCN":"接连地；依次地","example":"The lights came on successively.","exampleCN":"灯光依次亮起。"},{"word":"concession","structure":"con- (together) + cedere (yield) + -ion","meaning":"something granted or yielded","meaningCN":"让步；让与物","example":"The union won a small concession on hours.","exampleCN":"工会在一项工时问题上赢得了小幅让步。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"cedere","structure":"cedere, cessi, cessum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to go, withdraw, yield","meaningCN":"走；退；让"},{"word":"succedere","structure":"sub- + cedere (compound verb)","meaning":"to follow after, take the place of","meaningCN":"跟在后面；接替"},{"word":"successio","structure":"success- + -io (action noun)","meaning":"a following; an inheritance","meaningCN":"相继；继承"}]}},{"word":"sufficiently","ipa_uk":"/səˈfɪʃəntli/","ipa_us":"/səˈfɪʃəntli/","definition_zh":"足够地；充分地；达到所需程度地；（与形容词连用）足以……地","definition_en":"to the degree that is needed for a particular purpose or result","core_image":"灶台上，一只手把水壶倾到杯口上方，最后一滴水将落未落，杯里的水恰好升到杯沿","scene":"The evidence was sufficiently strong to support the conclusion.","sceneCN":"这里 sufficiently 是「证据充分地」（第 4 个义项：证据达到足以支撑结论的程度）；句意：证据足够有力，足以支持这一结论。图中可辨识物件：水壶、杯沿、将落未落的最后一滴水、恰好齐沿的水面。","pos":[{"tag":"adv.","zh":"足够地；充分地；达到所需程度地；（与形容词连用）足以……地"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"sufficiently large","zh":"足够大"},{"phrase":"sufficiently clear","zh":"足够清楚"},{"phrase":"sufficiently advanced","zh":"足够先进"},{"phrase":"sufficiently strong","zh":"足够有力"},{"phrase":"sufficiently documented","zh":"有充分记录的"},{"phrase":"sufficiently close","zh":"足够接近"}],"forms":[{"label":"形容词形式","form":"sufficient（足够的；充分的）"},{"label":"名词形式","form":"sufficiency（充足；足够）"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"suffice（足够；满足需要）"},{"label":"否定形容词","form":"insufficient（不足的；不够的）"},{"label":"否定副词","form":"insufficiently（不够地；不足以……地）"},{"label":"比较级","form":"more sufficiently（更充分地）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"sufficient","pos":"adj.","zh":"足够的；充分的"},{"word":"sufficiency","pos":"n.","zh":"充足；足够"},{"word":"suffice","pos":"v.","zh":"足够；满足需要"},{"word":"insufficient","pos":"adj.","zh":"不足的；不够的"},{"word":"insufficiently","pos":"adv.","zh":"不够地；不足以……地"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Enough to meet a need","titleCN":"足够：数量或程度满足需要","definition":"in an amount or degree that meets a requirement, so that no more is needed","definitionCN":"以足以满足某一需要的数量或程度，因而不需要更多","example":"He prepared sufficiently for the interview and answered every question.","exampleCN":"他为面试做了足够准备，回答了每一个问题。","why":"Latin sufficere meant 'to supply, be enough', built from sub- and facere 'to make or do'. The adverb says the supply has reached the line the need drew.","whyCN":"拉丁 sufficere 意为「供给、够用」，由 sub- 与 facere「做、制造」构成。副词表示供给已经达到需求所画出的那条线。"},{"no":"02","title":"Before an adjective: up to the level","titleCN":"与形容词连用：达到所需程度","definition":"used before an adjective or another adverb to say that a quality reaches the level required for a stated result","definitionCN":"放在形容词或另一副词之前，表示某一性质达到后文所述结果所需的水平","example":"The gap was sufficiently wide for a car to pass.","exampleCN":"缝隙足够宽，能让一辆车通过。","why":"In this pattern the adverb does not stand alone; it turns an adjective into a threshold, so 'sufficiently wide' means wide enough for the purpose named next.","whyCN":"在这一结构中，副词并不单独成立；它把形容词变成一个门槛，于是「sufficiently wide」意为「宽到足以……」后文所说的目的。"},{"no":"03","title":"Above a measurement threshold","titleCN":"数值阈值上足够：量值越过技术门槛","definition":"of a quantity in an experiment or calculation, large or small enough to satisfy a stated technical condition","definitionCN":"指实验或计算中的量值，大或小到足以满足某一既定技术条件","example":"The sample was sufficiently large for the test to detect a small effect.","exampleCN":"样本足够大，使该检验能发现微小效应。","why":"Statistics and metrology turn adequacy into a number: a sample, a dose or an error must cross a threshold before a procedure is valid.","whyCN":"统计学与计量学把「足够」变成数字：样本、剂量或误差必须越过某个门槛，程序才有效。"},{"no":"04","title":"Evidence strong enough to support a claim","titleCN":"证据充分：足以支撑结论","definition":"of evidence or proof, having enough weight that a conclusion can reasonably be drawn from it","definitionCN":"指证据或证明具有足够分量，可以合理地从中得出结论","example":"The evidence was sufficiently strong to support the conclusion.","exampleCN":"证据足够有力，足以支持这一结论。","why":"Here sufficiency is a standard of proof rather than a quantity; the word asks whether what is offered can carry the weight of the claim.","whyCN":"这里的「充分」是证明标准而不是数量；这个词问的是所提供的材料能否承载该主张的分量。"},{"no":"05","title":"Technology advanced enough to do the job","titleCN":"技术足够先进：达到完成任务的水平","definition":"of a method, instrument or technology, developed far enough to perform a stated task","definitionCN":"指方法、仪器或技术发展到足以完成某一任务的水平","example":"Sufficiently advanced sensors can detect a single photon.","exampleCN":"足够先进的传感器能探测到单个光子。","why":"Capability is treated as a level that a tool must reach; below it the task is impossible, above it the task becomes routine.","whyCN":"能力被看作工具必须达到的一个水平；低于它任务无法完成，高于它任务便成为常规。"},{"no":"06","title":"Wording clear enough to be understood","titleCN":"表述足够清楚：读者能据此行动","definition":"of language or instructions, expressed clearly enough that the intended reader can act without further explanation","definitionCN":"指语言或指示表达得足够清楚，使目标读者无需进一步解释便能行动","example":"The instructions were sufficiently clear that no one asked for help.","exampleCN":"说明足够清楚，没有人再请求帮助。","why":"Communication has its own threshold: a message is sufficient when the reader can act on it, even if it is not elegant or complete.","whyCN":"沟通有自己的门槛：只要读者能据此行动，信息就算充分，即便它并不优雅或并不完整。"},{"no":"07","title":"Legally notified in adequate form","titleCN":"法律上已充分告知：形式与时间均适当","definition":"in law, of notice or disclosure, given in a form and with enough time that the recipient is properly informed","definitionCN":"在法律上指通知或披露的形式适当、时间充足，使接收者得到恰当告知","example":"The tenant was sufficiently notified before the hearing.","exampleCN":"租户在听证之前已得到充分通知。","why":"Courts ask whether notice was adequate in form and timing; sufficiently marks that legal test rather than the amount of information.","whyCN":"法院关心通知在形式与时间上是否适当；sufficiently 标记的是这一法律检验，而不是信息的数量。"},{"no":"08","title":"Close enough for an approximation","titleCN":"近似计算中足够接近：误差在容许范围内","definition":"of a numerical approximation, near enough to the true value that the remaining error can be tolerated","definitionCN":"指数值近似与真值接近到其余误差可以被容许的程度","example":"The approximation was sufficiently close for the engineering tolerance.","exampleCN":"这一近似足够接近，落在工程公差之内。","why":"In numerical work no approximation is exact, so adequacy means staying inside an allowed error; the adverb names that margin.","whyCN":"在数值工作中没有近似是精确的，因此「充分」意味着留在允许误差之内；副词命名的正是这一余量。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Sufficiently is the adjective sufficient plus the native adverb ending -ly. Sufficient rests on Latin sufficiens, the present participle of sufficere, a compound of sub- and facere 'to make, do' meaning 'to supply, be enough'.","cn":"sufficiently 是形容词 sufficient 加本族副词词尾 -ly。sufficient 建立于拉丁 sufficiens，即 sufficere 的现在分词；sufficere 由 sub- 与 facere「做、制造」构成，意为「供给、够用」。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN FACERE","en":"Latin facere 'to make, do' is one of the most productive verbs in the language and underlies fact, effect, manufacture and sufficere.","cn":"拉丁 facere「做、制造」是这门语言中最具构词能力的动词之一，fact、effect、manufacture 与 sufficere 都建立在它之上。"},{"era":"LATIN SUFFICERE","en":"Sufficere is generally analysed as sub- plus facere, with the sense 'to supply, make up, be enough'. The precise force of sub- here, whether 'up' or 'in addition', is debated.","cn":"sufficere 一般认为由 sub- 加 facere 构成，意为「供给、补足、够用」。sub- 在此究竟是「向上」还是「补充」，学界有讨论。"},{"era":"LATIN SUFFICIENS","en":"Sufficiens is the present participle of sufficere, 'supplying, being enough'. English sufficient comes from this participle stem rather than from the infinitive.","cn":"sufficiens 是 sufficere 的现在分词，意为「供给的、够用的」。英语 sufficient 来自这一分词词干，而不是不定式。"},{"era":"FRENCH AND ENGLISH","en":"Old French suffisant and the Latin stem sufficient- supplied the English adjective sufficient in the late Middle Ages. The date of its first English use is not secure.","cn":"古法语 suffisant 与拉丁词干 sufficient- 在中世纪晚期为英语提供了形容词 sufficient；其英语首见年代不确切。"},{"era":"ADVERB -LY","en":"English added the native ending -ly, from Old English -lice, to sufficient, making sufficiently 'in a sufficient manner'. The adverb is the form used before adjectives to mark a threshold.","cn":"英语给 sufficient 加上本族词尾 -ly（源自古英语 -lice），构成 sufficiently「以充分的方式」。副词正是放在形容词前标记门槛的形式。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"First citation uncertain: the earliest English use of sufficiently has no secure date. Root note: facere is generally traced to Indo-European *dhe- 'to put, make', a reconstructed form; the Latin root is not in doubt, only the force of sub- in sufficere.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：sufficiently 的英语最早书证年代不确定。词根说明：facere 一般被追溯到印欧语 *dhe-「放置、制造」，这是重构形式；拉丁词根本身并无疑问，有争议的只是 sufficere 中 sub- 的作用。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the sufficient family by part of speech and polarity; the second gives near-synonyms for adequacy, with their different shades.","cn":"第一组按词性与肯定否定区分 sufficient 词族；第二组给出表示「足够」的近义词，并说明各自细微差别。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"sufficient","ipa":"/səˈfɪʃənt/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Enough for a purpose, describing a noun such as evidence or time. Sufficiently describes how a verb is done or how far an adjective goes.","definitionCN":"形容词，指足以满足目的，修饰证据、时间等名词；sufficiently 描述动作如何完成或形容词达到什么程度。"},{"word":"sufficiency","ipa":"/səˈfɪʃənsi/","tag":"quality noun","definition":"The state of being enough. It names the quality, while sufficiently names the degree.","definitionCN":"指「足够」的状态，命名性质；sufficiently 命名程度。"},{"word":"suffice","ipa":"/səˈfaɪs/","tag":"verb","definition":"To be enough, often in formal or fixed phrases. It states the fact of adequacy; sufficiently measures the degree.","definitionCN":"动词，指足够，常用于正式或固定说法；它陈述足够这一事实，sufficiently 则衡量程度。"},{"word":"insufficient","ipa":"/ˌɪnsəˈfɪʃənt/","tag":"opposite adjective","definition":"Not enough for the purpose. It is the negative counterpart of sufficient, not a form of sufficiently.","definitionCN":"指不足以满足目的，是 sufficient 的否定对应词，而不是 sufficiently 的一种形式。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"enough","ipa":"/ɪˈnʌf/","tag":"everyday adequacy","definition":"The plain word for adequacy, usable after an adjective as well as before a noun. It is more informal and less tied to a stated standard than sufficiently.","definitionCN":"表示「足够」的日常词，既可放在形容词后，也可放在名词前；它更口语化，也不如 sufficiently 那样紧扣某一既定标准。"},{"word":"adequately","ipa":"/ˈædɪkwətli/","tag":"meeting the requirement","definition":"In a way that meets the requirement, often with the idea of a minimum standard. It is close to sufficiently but carries less sense of a measured threshold.","definitionCN":"指达到要求，常含「最低标准」之意；它接近 sufficiently，但较少「可测量的门槛」意味。"},{"word":"amply","ipa":"/ˈæmpli/","tag":"with room to spare","definition":"More than enough, with a margin. Sufficiently stops at the line; amply goes beyond it.","definitionCN":"指充足有余、留有裕量；sufficiently 停在那条线上，amply 则越过它。"},{"word":"satisfactorily","ipa":"/ˌsætɪsˈfæktərəli/","tag":"to an acceptable standard","definition":"In a way that is judged acceptable, often by another person. It adds evaluation, while sufficiently states a measured degree.","definitionCN":"指达到可被接受的标准，常含他人评判；它增加评价意味，而 sufficiently 只陈述测得的程度。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"sub- plus facere: to add enough until the supply meets the need.","cn":"sub- 加 facere：不断补上，直到供给满足需要。"},{"en":"The family runs sufficient, sufficiency, suffice, insufficient, insufficiently.","cn":"同族词包括 sufficient、sufficiency、suffice、insufficient、insufficiently。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the threshold: sufficiently large, sufficiently clear, sufficiently close, sufficiently documented.","cn":"固定搭配标出门槛：足够大、足够清楚、足够接近、有充分记录。"},{"en":"Sufficiently usually sits before an adjective, turning it into a pass-fail test.","cn":"sufficiently 通常放在形容词前，把该形容词变成一个及格与否的检验。"},{"en":"Sufficient means enough; efficient means doing it with less waste. The prefixes differ.","cn":"sufficient 意为足够，efficient 意为高效、少浪费；两个词的前缀不同。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a jug tilted until the water just reaches the rim of a cup.","cn":"想象水壶倾斜，水面恰好升到杯沿。"},{"en":"Picture a gate that opens only when the water level touches a marked line.","cn":"想象一道闸门只在水位触到标记线时打开。"},{"en":"Picture a tolerance band on a drawing, with the part falling just inside it.","cn":"想象图纸上的公差带，零件恰好落在带内。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The room was sufficiently warm for the seedlings to survive the night.","cn":"房间足够温暖，幼苗得以熬过夜晚。"},{"en":"Her explanation was sufficiently detailed for the committee to act.","cn":"她的解释足够详细，委员会得以采取行动。"},{"en":"The second estimate was sufficiently close to the measured value.","cn":"第二个估计值足够接近实测值。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「sufficient（足够）+ ly」——刚好够用，不再多添 → sufficiently 足够地","word":"sufficiently"},"root":"拉丁 sub-「向上、补充」+ facere「做、制造」→ sufficere「补足、供得上」→ 拉丁 sufficiens（现在分词）→ 英语 sufficient + -ly → sufficiently；首见年代存疑。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses move from plain adequacy to the adjective pattern, a measured threshold, evidence, technology, clear wording, legal notice and a tolerated approximation.","cn":"八个义项从一般的「足够」，推进到形容词前的程度结构、可测量的门槛、证据、技术、清楚的表述、法律告知，以及可容许的近似误差。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: the supply rises exactly to the line that the need has drawn.","cn":"核心意象：供给恰好升到需求画出的那条线。"},"chain":["A NEED APPEARS","DRAW THE LINE","SUPPLY REACHES IT","PROVE THE CLAIM","MEET THE TOLERANCE","THE TASK BECOMES POSSIBLE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"PLAIN ADEQUACY AND DEGREE: enough for a need, and enough of a quality for a named result.","cn":"一般足够与程度：满足需要，或某种性质达到指定结果所需。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"THE MEASURED THRESHOLD: a sample, dose or error crosses a technical line.","cn":"可测量的门槛：样本、剂量或误差越过技术界线。"},{"senses":"S4 · S7","en":"STANDARDS OF PROOF: evidence carries a conclusion, and notice satisfies a legal test.","cn":"证明标准：证据足以承载结论，通知满足法律检验。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"CAPABILITY AND CLARITY: a tool can do the job, and wording lets the reader act.","cn":"能力与清晰：工具足以完成任务，表述足以让读者行动。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"THE APPROXIMATION MARGIN: the remaining error stays inside what is allowed.","cn":"近似余量：剩余误差留在允许范围之内。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Sufficiently is Latin sufficere plus an English adverb ending: sufficiens gave sufficient, and -ly made it an adverb of degree.","cn":"sufficiently 是拉丁 sufficere 加英语副词词尾：sufficiens 给出 sufficient，-ly 再把它变成程度副词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin core is sub- plus facere 'to make, do', giving sufficere 'to supply, be enough'. The participle sufficiens supplies the adjective stem, and -ly is the native English adverb ending.","cn":"拉丁核心是 sub- 加 facere「做、制造」，构成 sufficere「供给、够用」。分词 sufficiens 提供形容词词干，-ly 则是本族英语副词词尾。"},"items":[{"word":"sufficiently","structure":"sufficient + -ly (manner adverb)","meaning":"to an adequate degree","meaningCN":"达到足够程度地","example":"The lamp was sufficiently bright to read by.","exampleCN":"灯光足够亮，可以看书。"},{"word":"sufficient","structure":"sufficiens (present participle stem) + -ent","meaning":"enough for a purpose","meaningCN":"足够满足目的的","example":"There is sufficient evidence to proceed.","exampleCN":"有足够证据可以继续。"},{"word":"sufficiency","structure":"sufficient + -cy (quality noun)","meaning":"the state of being enough","meaningCN":"充足的状态","example":"They questioned the sufficiency of the food supply.","exampleCN":"他们质疑食物供给是否充足。"},{"word":"suffice","structure":"sufficere (verb)","meaning":"to be enough","meaningCN":"足够；满足需要","example":"A brief note will suffice.","exampleCN":"一则简短说明就够了。"},{"word":"insufficient","structure":"in- (not) + sufficient","meaning":"not enough","meaningCN":"不足的；不够的","example":"The evidence was insufficient to convict.","exampleCN":"证据不足以定罪。"},{"word":"insufficiently","structure":"insufficient + -ly","meaning":"to a degree that is not enough","meaningCN":"不够地；不足以……地","example":"The notice was insufficiently clear.","exampleCN":"通知不够清楚。"},{"word":"self-sufficient","structure":"self + sufficient","meaning":"able to provide for oneself","meaningCN":"自给自足的","example":"The village became self-sufficient in vegetables.","exampleCN":"这个村庄在蔬菜上实现了自给自足。"},{"word":"manufacture","structure":"manu (hand) + facere (make)","meaning":"to make by hand or machine","meaningCN":"手工或机器制造","example":"The factory manufactures parts for bicycles.","exampleCN":"这家工厂生产自行车零件。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"facere","structure":"facere, feci, factum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to make, do","meaningCN":"做；制造"},{"word":"sufficere","structure":"sub- + facere (compound verb)","meaning":"to supply, be enough","meaningCN":"供给；够用"},{"word":"sufficiens","structure":"sufficere + -ns (present participle)","meaning":"supplying, being enough","meaningCN":"供给的；够用的"}]}},{"word":"sustainability","ipa_uk":"/səˌsteɪnəˈbɪləti/","ipa_us":"/səˌsteɪnəˈbɪləti/","definition_zh":"可持续性；可持续；（组织、财政等）长期可维持性；可持续发展理念","definition_en":"the quality of being able to continue over the long term without exhausting the resources or conditions it depends on","core_image":"一根幼苗被下方的木桩托住，旁边一只天平两端分别放着今天的收成与留给来年的种子","scene":"The city's sustainability program cut energy use by a fifth within three years.","sceneCN":"这里 sustainability 是「机构层面的可持续战略」（第 5 个义项：城市作为治理主体对长期环境目标的管理）；句意：这座城市的可持续计划在三年内把能耗降低了五分之一。图中可辨识物件：被木桩托住的幼苗、天平、收成堆、种子袋、下降的能耗曲线。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"可持续性；可持续；（生态系统、组织、财政等的）长期可维持性；（指理念或事业时多不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"sustainable development","zh":"可持续发展"},{"phrase":"fiscal sustainability","zh":"财政可持续性"},{"phrase":"environmental sustainability","zh":"环境可持续性"},{"phrase":"corporate sustainability","zh":"企业可持续性"},{"phrase":"sustainability report","zh":"可持续发展报告"},{"phrase":"sustainability goals","zh":"可持续发展目标"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（指多种可持续性指标或做法）","form":"sustainabilities"},{"label":"形容词形式","form":"sustainable（可持续的）"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"sustain（维持；支撑）"},{"label":"形容词（持续不断的）","form":"sustained（持续的）"},{"label":"副词形式","form":"sustainably（可持续地）"},{"label":"反义名词","form":"unsustainability（不可持续性）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"sustain","pos":"v.","zh":"维持；支撑（sustain 源自古法语 sustenir，再上溯拉丁 sustinere = sub-「自下」+ tenere「握住」）"},{"word":"sustainable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可持续的（sustain + -able「可……的」，义项由「可被支撑」偏移为「可长期维持」）"},{"word":"sustainably","pos":"adv.","zh":"可持续地（sustainable + -ly，方式副词）"},{"word":"sustenance","pos":"n.","zh":"食物；生计（sustain + -ance「……之物」，由「支撑」偏移为「维持生命之物」）"},{"word":"unsustainable","pos":"adj.","zh":"不可持续的（un-「不」+ sustainable，语义偏移为「继续下去会崩溃的」）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The ability of an ecosystem to endure","titleCN":"生态可持续性：生态系统长期存续的能力","definition":"the capacity of an ecosystem to keep producing and renewing itself over time without collapsing","definitionCN":"生态系统在长期内持续产出、自我更新而不崩溃的能力","example":"The reef's sustainability depends on water temperature and the balance of species.","exampleCN":"珊瑚礁的可持续性取决于水温与物种平衡。","why":"Here the word answers a question about nature: can this system keep going on its own? The sense of holding up from below becomes the ecosystem holding itself up across generations.","whyCN":"这里该词回答一个关于自然的问题：这个系统能否自行持续运转？「从下方托住」的本义转化为生态系统跨世代自我支撑的能力。"},{"no":"02","title":"A system or enterprise that can keep functioning","titleCN":"系统或组织的可维持性：长期运转而不瓦解","definition":"the ability of an organization, project or technical system to continue operating within its resources over the long term","definitionCN":"组织、项目或技术系统在其资源范围内长期持续运转的能力","example":"Without new funding, the program's sustainability is in doubt.","exampleCN":"没有新的资金，该项目的可持续性堪忧。","why":"The same question is asked of human institutions: a project is sustainable if it can renew its resources, staff and purpose instead of living on one grant. The image is a machine that fuels itself.","whyCN":"同样的问题被问到人类组织上：一个项目若能不断补充资源、人手与目标，而不是靠一笔拨款过活，就是可持续的。意象是一台能自我供能的机器。"},{"no":"03","title":"Public finances that can be serviced indefinitely","titleCN":"财政可持续性：债务能被长期偿付","definition":"the condition of government debt and spending that can be maintained without defaulting or forcing intolerable future burdens","definitionCN":"政府债务与支出能够长期维持、不致违约或给未来造成难以承受负担的状态","example":"Fiscal sustainability requires debt to grow no faster than the economy.","exampleCN":"财政可持续性要求债务增长不快于经济增长。","why":"Economists transferred the word to public accounts: a fiscal path is sustainable if it can be serviced year after year. The holding up becomes the state holding up its own obligations.","whyCN":"经济学家把这个词转用到公共账目：一条财政路径若能年复一年地偿付，就是可持续的。「托住」变成了国家托住自己的债务义务。"},{"no":"04","title":"Development that does not spend the future","titleCN":"可持续发展：不透支未来的发展","definition":"economic and social progress that meets present needs without preventing future generations from meeting theirs","definitionCN":"满足当代需求、又不损害后代满足其需求能力的经济社会发展","example":"The master plan links housing, transport and industry under the banner of sustainability.","exampleCN":"总体规划把住房、交通与工业统一在可持续性的旗帜下。","why":"The 1987 Brundtland report made sustainable development a global slogan; sustainability became the noun that names the whole project of balancing growth with the planet's limits.","whyCN":"1987 年的《布伦特兰报告》使可持续发展成为全球口号；sustainability 成为命名「在增长与地球极限之间求平衡」这一整套事业的抽象名词。"},{"no":"05","title":"A company's long-term environmental and social strategy","titleCN":"企业可持续战略：企业层面的长期环境与社会管理","definition":"the policies and reporting through which a business manages its environmental and social impact over the long term","definitionCN":"企业用以长期管理其环境与社会影响的政策与信息披露","example":"The bank made sustainability a board-level responsibility.","exampleCN":"这家银行把可持续性列为董事会层面的职责。","why":"From the 1990s companies turned the movement's demand into a management practice, with sustainability reports, officers and targets. The word now names an organizational discipline.","whyCN":"自二十世纪九十年代起，企业把运动的诉求变成管理实践，出现了可持续发展报告、负责人与目标。该词如今命名一种组织化的专业领域。"},{"no":"06","title":"Farming and food that last","titleCN":"农业与粮食体系的可持续性","definition":"the quality of agricultural practices and food supply chains that preserve soil, water and livelihoods for the long term","definitionCN":"能够长期保住土壤、水源与生计的农业做法与粮食供应链的性质","example":"Soil erosion is the biggest threat to the farm's sustainability.","exampleCN":"水土流失是对该农场可持续性的最大威胁。","why":"Applied to agriculture, the word measures a system's ability to keep producing without mining its own soil. It is sustainability with the ground under it made literal.","whyCN":"用在农业上，这个词衡量一个体系能否在不耗尽自己土地的前提下持续产出。这是把「脚下有支撑」变成字面意义的可持续性。"},{"no":"07","title":"A research field that studies endurance","titleCN":"可持续性科学：研究长期存续的交叉学科","definition":"the interdisciplinary study of how natural and social systems can meet human needs over the long term","definitionCN":"研究自然系统与社会系统如何长期满足人类需求的交叉学科","example":"Sustainability science draws on ecology, economics and engineering together.","exampleCN":"可持续性科学同时借用生态学、经济学与工程学。","why":"Around the year 2000 the word became the name of a discipline that treats endurance as a technical problem; the noun shifted from a quality to a field of study.","whyCN":"大约在 2000 年前后，该词成为一个学科的名称，把「长期存续」当作技术问题来研究；名词从一种性质变成一门学问。"},{"no":"08","title":"A lifestyle a person can actually keep up","titleCN":"生活方式的可持续性：个人能否长期坚持","definition":"the quality of a habit, budget or way of living that a person can maintain without burning out or giving up","definitionCN":"一个人能够长期坚持、不致耗尽精力或放弃的习惯、预算或生活方式的性质","example":"Running every day sounds admirable, but sustainability matters more than intensity.","exampleCN":"每天跑步听起来值得敬佩，但能否长期坚持比强度更重要。","why":"Health writers borrowed the word: a plan is sustainable if the person can repeat it next month. The scale has shrunk from the planet to one daily routine.","whyCN":"健康类作者借用这个词：一个人下个月还能照做的计划才是可持续的。尺度从整个地球缩小到一项日常作息。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Sustainability is the noun sustainable plus the quality ending -ity; sustainable is built on sustain, taken through Old French sustenir from Latin sustinere, made of sub- 'from below' and tenere 'to hold, keep'. The dates below are approximate.","cn":"sustainability 是形容词 sustainable 加性质词尾 -ity 构成；sustainable 建立在 sustain 之上，后者经古法语 sustenir 源自拉丁 sustinere，由 sub-「自下」与 tenere「握住、保持」组成。以下年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN SUSTINERE","en":"Latin sustinere 'to hold up from below, support, endure' was built on sub- 'from below' and tenere 'to hold, keep'. Its original picture is of taking weight from underneath and keeping it in place.","cn":"拉丁 sustinere「自下托住、支撑、承受」由 sub-「自下」与 tenere「握住、保持」构成。其原始画面是从下方接住重量并让它保持原位。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH SUSTENIR","en":"English took sustain through Old French sustenir in the medieval period, with the meanings 'to keep in being, maintain, provide for'.","cn":"英语在中世纪经古法语 sustenir 借入 sustain，义为「使存续、维持、供养」。"},{"era":"SUSTAINABLE IN THE SEVENTEENTH CENTURY","en":"The adjective sustainable, formed on sustain with -able, meant in the seventeenth century 'able to be supported or maintained', used of arguments, weights and provisions. Its first citation is uncertain.","cn":"形容词 sustainable 由 sustain 加 -able 构成，十七世纪时义为「可被支撑或维持的」，用于论证、重物与给养。其最早书证年代存疑。"},{"era":"ENVIRONMENTAL MEANING, 1970s–80s","en":"In the 1970s and 1980s sustainable was applied to development, energy and agriculture that do not exhaust resources, and the phrase sustainable development became a global policy term after the 1987 Brundtland report.","cn":"二十世纪七八十年代，sustainable 被用于不耗尽资源的开发、能源与农业；sustainable development 一词在 1987 年《布伦特兰报告》后成为全球政策用语。"},{"era":"THE NOUN SUSTAINABILITY","en":"Sustainability adds -ity, the ending of quality. The noun existed earlier in the general sense 'capability of being maintained' (first citation uncertain) and spread as a movement term in the late twentieth century.","cn":"sustainability 加上了性质词尾 -ity。该名词更早便以「可被维持的能力」这一一般义存在（最早书证年代存疑），二十世纪后期作为运动用语普及。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"The exact first English citations of both sustainable and sustainability are uncertain. The deeper root of tenere is generally taken to be reconstructed Indo-European *ten- 'to stretch, hold', a reconstruction rather than a recorded form.","cn":"首见年代存疑：sustainable 与 sustainability 的英语最早书证年代均不确定。tenere 的更深词根一般认为是重构的印欧语 *ten-「伸展、保持」，属重构形式，而非有记录的真实词形。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the sustain family by part of speech; the second gives near-synonyms for lasting without exhausting what keeps something going.","cn":"第一组按词性区分 sustain 词族；第二组给出表示「不耗尽支撑物而长久延续」的近义词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"sustainable","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnəbəl/","tag":"adjective","definition":"The adjective: able to be kept going. Sustainability is the noun that names the quality.","definitionCN":"形容词，指可长期维持的；sustainability 是命名这一性质的名词。"},{"word":"sustain","ipa":"/səˈsteɪn/","tag":"verb","definition":"The verb of keeping something going or holding it up. Sustainable describes the thing; sustain is the action.","definitionCN":"动词，指维持或托住某物；sustainable 描述事物，sustain 是动作。"},{"word":"sustained","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnd/","tag":"adjective of duration","definition":"Continuous over time. Sustained describes an effort that did keep going; sustainable asks whether it can keep going without damage.","definitionCN":"指持续的；sustained 描述确实一直持续的努力，sustainable 追问它能否无损害地持续下去。"},{"word":"sustenance","ipa":"/ˈsʌstənəns/","tag":"concrete noun","definition":"The food or means that keeps a life going. It is the concrete thing; sustainability is the abstract quality.","definitionCN":"指维持生命的食物或手段，是具体之物；sustainability 是抽象性质。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"durability","ipa":"/ˌdjʊərəˈbɪləti/","tag":"resistance to wear","definition":"Resistance to wear over time. Durability is about lasting physically; sustainability is about not exhausting what keeps something going.","definitionCN":"指对磨损的抵抗力：durability 强调物理上耐用，sustainability 强调不耗尽维持其运转的东西。"},{"word":"viability","ipa":"/ˌvaɪəˈbɪləti/","tag":"ability to work","definition":"The ability to work or succeed. A plan can be viable now yet unsustainable over decades.","definitionCN":"指行得通、能成功的能力；一个方案眼下可行（viable），却可能在数十年内不可持续。"},{"word":"resilience","ipa":"/rɪˈzɪliəns/","tag":"ability to recover","definition":"The ability to recover from shocks. Resilience is about bouncing back; sustainability is about not being driven to the point of collapse.","definitionCN":"指从冲击中恢复的能力：resilience 强调反弹回来，sustainability 强调不被逼到崩溃边缘。"},{"word":"renewability","ipa":"/rɪˌnjuːəˈbɪləti/","tag":"regenerating source","definition":"The quality of a resource that regenerates. Renewability feeds sustainability, but a system can be renewable yet still mismanaged.","definitionCN":"指资源再生的性质：renewability 为 sustainability 提供基础，但系统可再生（renewable）仍可能被管理失当。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"sustain + -able + -ity: hold it up from below, say it can be kept up, then name the quality.","cn":"sustain + -able + -ity：先从下方托住，再说「撑得住」，最后为这一性质命名。"},{"en":"The family runs sustain, sustainable, sustainability, sustained, sustenance, unsustainable.","cn":"同族词包括 sustain、sustainable、sustainability、sustained、sustenance、unsustainable。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases mark the movement: sustainable development, corporate sustainability, fiscal sustainability, sustainability report.","cn":"固定搭配标出这一运动领域：可持续发展、企业可持续性、财政可持续性、可持续发展报告。"},{"en":"A fishing quota is sustainable only if the catch does not exceed what regrows.","cn":"只有当渔获不超过再生长量时，捕捞配额才是可持续的。"},{"en":"Sustain is the verb, sustainable the adjective, sustainability the noun: the same act at three distances.","cn":"sustain 是动词，sustainable 是形容词，sustainability 是名词：同一个动作的三种距离。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a sapling held upright by a stake, still growing season after season.","cn":"想象一棵被木桩扶正的幼苗，一季又一季地生长。"},{"en":"Picture a ledger that stays balanced year after year, never dipping into the red.","cn":"想象一本年复一年保持平衡、从不出现赤字的账本。"},{"en":"Picture a forest that gives timber every decade without shrinking.","cn":"想象一片每十年都能产出木材却不见缩小的森林。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The company's sustainability report lists emissions for each factory.","cn":"这家公司的可持续发展报告列出了每家工厂的排放量。"},{"en":"Fiscal sustainability forces governments to think beyond the next election.","cn":"财政可持续性迫使政府把眼光放到下一次选举之后。"},{"en":"Scientists warn that groundwater use is far beyond sustainability.","cn":"科学家警告，地下水开采已远远超出可持续的范围。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「sustain（维持）+ able + ity」——托得住、撑得久 → sustainability 可持续性","word":"sustainability"},"root":"拉丁 sustinere = sub-「自下」+ tenere「握住、保持」→ 古法语 sustenir → 英语 sustain + -able + -ity。更深词根一般认为是印欧语 *ten-「伸展、保持」（重构形式）。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses ask the same question at different scales: can an ecosystem, an organization, a budget, a development path, a company, a farm, a discipline or a daily habit keep going?","cn":"八个义项在不同尺度上提出同一个问题：生态系统、组织、预算、发展路径、企业、农场、学科或日常习惯，能否一直运转下去？"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a load is held up from below so it can keep going without breaking.","cn":"核心意象：重物被从下方托住，得以持续运转而不垮。"},"chain":["HOLD FROM BELOW","KEEP IT GOING","DO NOT EXHAUST","MEASURE THE BALANCE","PLAN FOR THE LONG TERM","NAME THE MOVEMENT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"NATURAL AND ORGANIZATIONAL CAPACITY: ecosystems and institutions keep functioning over time.","cn":"自然与组织能力：生态系统与机构长期保持运转。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"PUBLIC FINANCE AND DEVELOPMENT: debt stays serviceable and growth does not spend its own base.","cn":"公共财政与发展：债务可偿付，增长不消耗自身根基。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"INSTITUTIONAL STRATEGY: companies and cities manage resources for the long term.","cn":"机构战略：企业与城市为长期而管理资源。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"AGRICULTURE AND SCIENCE: food systems and research disciplines treat endurance as a measurable object.","cn":"农业与科学：粮食体系与研究学科把「存续」当作可测量的对象。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"PERSONAL ENDURANCE: a habit or lifestyle can be repeated without burning out.","cn":"个人耐力：习惯或生活方式可反复执行而不致耗尽。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Sustainability is layered: the Latin verb sustinere 'hold up from below', the adjective suffix -able, and the quality-noun ending -ity.","cn":"sustainability 是分层的：拉丁动词 sustinere「自下托住」、形容词词尾 -able、性质名词词尾 -ity。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin element is tenere 'to hold, keep' with the prefix sub- 'from below'; -able came through French from Latin -abilis, and -ity from Latin -itas.","cn":"其中的拉丁成分是 tenere「握住、保持」加前缀 sub-「自下」；-able 经法语源自拉丁 -abilis，-ity 源自拉丁 -itas。"},"items":[{"word":"sustainability","structure":"sustain + -able + -ity (quality noun)","meaning":"the quality of being maintainable over the long term","meaningCN":"长期可维持的性质","example":"Urban planners debated the sustainability of the new district.","exampleCN":"城市规划者讨论了新区的可持续性。"},{"word":"sustain","structure":"sub- (from below) + tenere (to hold)","meaning":"to hold up, keep in being, maintain","meaningCN":"托住；使维持；保持","example":"The land can sustain only a few thousand people.","exampleCN":"这片土地只能养活几千人。"},{"word":"sustainable","structure":"sustain + -able (able to be)","meaning":"able to be continued without exhausting the base","meaningCN":"可持续的；不耗尽根基而能继续的","example":"They looked for a sustainable source of water.","exampleCN":"他们寻找可持续的水源。"},{"word":"sustenance","structure":"sustain + -ance (that which)","meaning":"the food or means that keeps life going","meaningCN":"维持生命的食物或手段","example":"The migrants lived on scant sustenance.","exampleCN":"这些迁徙者靠微薄的食物维生。"},{"word":"unsustainable","structure":"un- (not) + sustainable","meaning":"unable to be continued without collapse","meaningCN":"不可持续的；继续下去会崩溃的","example":"The debt level proved unsustainable.","exampleCN":"债务水平被证明不可持续。"},{"word":"tenable","structure":"tenere + -able (able to be)","meaning":"able to be held or defended","meaningCN":"站得住脚的；可辩护的","example":"His argument is no longer tenable.","exampleCN":"他的论点已站不住脚。"},{"word":"retain","structure":"re- (back) + tenere (to hold)","meaning":"to keep hold of","meaningCN":"保留；保持","example":"The treaty lets members retain control of their waters.","exampleCN":"条约允许成员国保留对其水域的控制。"},{"word":"maintain","structure":"Latin manu tenere (to hold in hand) via Old French","meaning":"to keep in good condition or working order","meaningCN":"维持；保养","example":"Regular checks maintain the bridge in safe condition.","exampleCN":"定期检查让桥梁保持安全状态。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"sustinere","structure":"sustinere, sustineo, sustinui, sustentum (second conjugation)","meaning":"to hold up, support, endure","meaningCN":"托住；支撑；承受"},{"word":"tenere","structure":"tenere, teneo, tenui, tentum (second conjugation)","meaning":"to hold, keep, grasp","meaningCN":"握住；保持；抓牢"},{"word":"-itas","structure":"-itas, -itatis (f., quality suffix)","meaning":"suffix forming nouns of quality","meaningCN":"构成性质名词的词尾"}]}},{"word":"sustainable","ipa_uk":"/səˈsteɪnəbəl/","ipa_us":"/səˈsteɪnəbəl/","definition_zh":"可持续的；可长期维持的；（不耗尽资源而）能长期继续的；长期可行的","definition_en":"able to be continued over the long term without destroying or exhausting the resources or conditions it depends on","core_image":"一只渔篓只取走水面一层鱼，留下大部分鱼群继续繁殖，旁边的日历翻过一年又一年","scene":"The project aims for sustainable growth rather than a short-term boom.","sceneCN":"这里 sustainable 是「可持续增长」（第 3 个义项：增长不以透支未来为代价）；句意：该项目追求可持续增长，而不是短期繁荣。图中可辨识物件：渔篓、鱼群、逐年翻过的日历、缓缓上升的曲线、没有断裂的阶梯。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"可持续的；可长期维持的；（环境）不耗尽资源的；长期可行的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"sustainable development","zh":"可持续发展"},{"phrase":"sustainable growth","zh":"可持续增长"},{"phrase":"sustainable agriculture","zh":"可持续农业"},{"phrase":"sustainable energy","zh":"可持续能源"},{"phrase":"sustainable yield","zh":"可持续产量"},{"phrase":"sustainable business model","zh":"可持续商业模式"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more sustainable（更可持续的）"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most sustainable（最可持续的）"},{"label":"副词形式","form":"sustainably（可持续地）"},{"label":"名词（性质）","form":"sustainability（可持续性）"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"sustain（维持；支撑）"},{"label":"反义形容词","form":"unsustainable（不可持续的）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"sustainability","pos":"n.","zh":"可持续性（sustainable + -ity「性质」，语义由形容词偏移为抽象名词）"},{"word":"sustainably","pos":"adv.","zh":"可持续地（sustainable + -ly，方式副词）"},{"word":"sustain","pos":"v.","zh":"维持；支撑（源自古法语 sustenir = 拉丁 sustinere「自下托住」）"},{"word":"sustenance","pos":"n.","zh":"食物；生计（sustain + -ance「……之物」，由「支撑」偏移为「维持生命之物」）"},{"word":"unsustainable","pos":"adj.","zh":"不可持续的（un-「不」+ sustainable）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Kind to the environment","titleCN":"环境上可持续的：不破坏、不耗尽自然","definition":"describing an activity or product that can continue without destroying or exhausting the natural environment it depends on","definitionCN":"描述一种能够持续进行、而不破坏或耗尽所依赖的自然环境的活动或产品","example":"The factory switched to sustainable energy sources.","exampleCN":"这家工厂改用可持续的能源。","why":"This is the modern headline sense: the word promises that a practice will not consume its own base. The Latin picture of holding up from below becomes the environment holding up the activity.","whyCN":"这是现代最显眼的义项：该词承诺一种做法不会消耗自身根基。拉丁语「自下托住」的画面变成环境托住这项活动。"},{"no":"02","title":"A rate or level that can be kept up","titleCN":"可长期维持的速率或水平","definition":"describing a speed, level or pace that can be continued over time without falling or collapsing","definitionCN":"描述一种可以长期保持、不致下滑或崩溃的速度、水平或节奏","example":"The team set a sustainable pace for the long climb.","exampleCN":"团队为漫长的攀登设定了一个可持续的节奏。","why":"Here the word is applied to quantities: a pace is sustainable if the body or the budget can repeat it. The test is whether the rate outlasts the effort.","whyCN":"这里该词用于数量：只要身体或预算能重复执行，节奏就是可持续的。检验标准是速率能否比努力更长久。"},{"no":"03","title":"Growth that does not overheat","titleCN":"可持续增长：不过热、不透支的增长","definition":"describing economic or organizational growth that can continue without overheating, crashing or consuming its own future","definitionCN":"描述能够持续进行、而不致过热、崩溃或消耗自身未来的经济或组织增长","example":"Analysts welcomed the shift toward sustainable growth.","exampleCN":"分析师欢迎向可持续增长的转变。","why":"Economists use the word for expansion that stays within real limits of credit, labor and demand. A boom is fast; sustainable growth is fast enough to last.","whyCN":"经济学家用该词指停留在信贷、劳动力与需求真实限度内的扩张。繁荣是快的；可持续增长则是快得能持久。"},{"no":"04","title":"Farming that protects the soil","titleCN":"可持续农业：保护土壤与水源的耕作","definition":"describing agricultural methods that preserve soil, water and biodiversity while producing food over the long term","definitionCN":"描述在长期产粮的同时保住土壤、水源与生物多样性的农业方法","example":"Sustainable agriculture rotates crops to protect the soil.","exampleCN":"可持续农业通过轮作来保护土壤。","why":"In farming the word measures the ground itself: a method is sustainable if the field still produces in fifty years. The image of holding up from below becomes literal topsoil.","whyCN":"在农业中，该词以土地本身为尺度：一片田地五十年后仍能产出，方法才算可持续。「自下托住」的意象变成了字面上的表土。"},{"no":"05","title":"Materials and buildings with a light footprint","titleCN":"可持续材料与建筑：低环境代价的建造","definition":"describing materials, products or buildings that can be produced, used and maintained with low environmental cost over their life cycle","definitionCN":"描述在整个生命周期内能以较低环境代价被生产、使用与维护的材料、产品或建筑","example":"The architects chose sustainable timber for the frame.","exampleCN":"建筑师为框架选择了可持续木材。","why":"In construction and design the adjective certifies a whole life cycle, from harvest to disposal. It is the environmental sense applied to things rather than activities.","whyCN":"在建筑与设计中，该形容词为从采伐到废弃的整个生命周期作担保。这是环境义项从活动延伸到物品。"},{"no":"06","title":"A business model that survives","titleCN":"长期可行的商业模式","definition":"describing a business model or income source that can continue earning enough to operate over the long term","definitionCN":"描述能够长期持续赚到足够运营收入的商业模式或收入来源","example":"A subscription model proved more sustainable than one-off sales.","exampleCN":"订阅模式被证明比一次性销售更可持续。","why":"In business English the word is about survival without constant rescue: revenue must cover costs year after year. The system keeps itself going.","whyCN":"在商业英语中，该词指无需不断救援而能生存：收入必须年复一年地覆盖成本。系统自己维持自己。"},{"no":"07","title":"A lifestyle a person can maintain","titleCN":"可坚持的生活方式","definition":"describing a habit, diet or way of living that a person can continue without burning out or giving up","definitionCN":"描述一个人能够长期坚持、不致耗尽精力或放弃的习惯、饮食或生活方式","example":"The diet is sustainable because it allows occasional treats.","exampleCN":"这种饮食法允许偶尔犒劳自己，所以能够坚持。","why":"Health and productivity writers apply the word to willpower: a plan is sustainable if the person can repeat it next month. The scale is one life, not the planet.","whyCN":"健康与效率类作者把该词用在意志力上：一个人下个月还能照做的计划才是可持续的。尺度是一个人的生活，而不是整个地球。"},{"no":"08","title":"A harvest that does not deplete the stock","titleCN":"可持续产量：不耗尽资源的采收","definition":"describing a harvest, catch or extraction level that removes no more than the resource can replace","definitionCN":"描述移除量不超过资源再生量的采收、捕捞或开采水平","example":"The quota was set at a sustainable yield.","exampleCN":"配额被定在可持续产量的水平上。","why":"Fisheries and forestry use the word for the maximum that can be taken forever: take the interest, keep the capital. It is the oldest precise sense of the modern environmental meaning.","whyCN":"渔业与林业用该词指可永远采走的最大量：只取利息，保住本金。这是现代环境义项中最古老而精确的用法。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Sustainable is sustain plus the adjective ending -able; sustain came through Old French sustenir from Latin sustinere, made of sub- 'from below' and tenere 'to hold, keep'. The dates below are approximate.","cn":"sustainable 是 sustain 加形容词词尾 -able；sustain 经古法语 sustenir 源自拉丁 sustinere，由 sub-「自下」与 tenere「握住、保持」组成。以下年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN SUSTINERE","en":"Latin sustinere 'to hold up from below, support, endure' was built on sub- 'from below' and tenere 'to hold, keep'. It already covered both physical support and enduring hardship.","cn":"拉丁 sustinere「自下托住、支撑、承受」由 sub-「自下」与 tenere「握住、保持」构成；它既有物理支撑义，也有忍受苦难义。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH SUSTENIR","en":"English took sustain through Old French sustenir in the medieval period, with the meanings 'to keep in being, maintain, provide for'.","cn":"英语在中世纪经古法语 sustenir 借入 sustain，义为「使存续、维持、供养」。"},{"era":"SEVENTEENTH-CENTURY ADJECTIVE","en":"Sustainable was formed on sustain with -able; in the seventeenth century it meant 'able to be supported or maintained', used of arguments, weights and provisions. Its first citation is uncertain.","cn":"sustainable 由 sustain 加 -able 构成；十七世纪时义为「可被支撑或维持的」，用于论证、重物与给养。其最早书证年代存疑。"},{"era":"ENVIRONMENTAL MEANING, 1970s–80s","en":"The environmental sense arose in the 1970s and 1980s, and the phrase sustainable development became a global policy term after the 1987 Brundtland report.","cn":"环境义项在二十世纪七八十年代兴起；sustainable development 一词在 1987 年《布伦特兰报告》后成为全球政策用语。"},{"era":"MODERN RANGE","en":"Economics and engineering fixed the modern range of the adjective: sustainable growth, sustainable yield, sustainable energy, sustainable materials.","cn":"经济学与工程学固定了该形容词的现代义域：可持续增长、可持续产量、可持续能源、可持续材料。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"The exact first English citation of sustainable is uncertain. The deeper root of tenere is generally taken to be reconstructed Indo-European *ten- 'to stretch, hold', a reconstruction rather than a recorded form.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：sustainable 的英语最早书证年代不确定。tenere 的更深词根一般认为是重构的印欧语 *ten-「伸展、保持」，属重构形式，而非有记录的真实词形。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the sustain family by part of speech; the second contrasts sustainable with near-synonyms, since sustainable stresses not exhausting resources and lasting over the long term.","cn":"第一组按词性区分 sustain 词族；第二组将 sustainable 与近义词对照，因为 sustainable 强调不耗尽资源、可长期维持。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"sustained","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnd/","tag":"adjective of duration","definition":"Continuous over a period. Sustained describes effort that went on; sustainable asks whether it can go on without damage.","definitionCN":"指持续的；sustained 描述确实持续下去的努力，sustainable 追问它能否无损害地继续。"},{"word":"sustain","ipa":"/səˈsteɪn/","tag":"verb","definition":"The verb of keeping something going. Sustainable is the adjective formed on it with -able.","definitionCN":"动词，指维持某物；sustainable 是它加 -able 构成的形容词。"},{"word":"sustenance","ipa":"/ˈsʌstənəns/","tag":"concrete noun","definition":"The concrete means of staying alive. Sustainable describes the quality of a practice, not the food itself.","definitionCN":"指维持生命的具体手段；sustainable 描述做法的性质，而非食物本身。"},{"word":"sustainability","ipa":"/səˌsteɪnəˈbɪləti/","tag":"abstract noun","definition":"The abstract noun. Sustainable is the quality; sustainability is the name of the quality and of the movement.","definitionCN":"抽象名词；sustainable 是性质，sustainability 是这一性质及其运动的名称。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"maintainable","ipa":"/meɪnˈteɪnəbəl/","tag":"kept in working order","definition":"Able to be kept in working order. Maintained implies constant input and care; sustainable implies the system can go on without exhausting itself.","definitionCN":"指可保持良好运转；maintained 隐含需要不断投入与维护，sustainable 隐含系统能不耗尽自身而继续。"},{"word":"viable","ipa":"/ˈvaɪəbəl/","tag":"able to work","definition":"Able to work or succeed. Viable is about feasibility now; sustainable adds the demand that it last without damage.","definitionCN":"指能行得通、能成功；viable 关乎眼下可行，sustainable 还要求无损害地长久延续。"},{"word":"renewable","ipa":"/rɪˈnjuːəbəl/","tag":"regenerating source","definition":"Able to be replenished by natural processes. Renewable describes the source; sustainable describes the whole practice that respects the source.","definitionCN":"指可被自然过程补充；renewable 描述资源本身，sustainable 描述尊重该资源的整个做法。"},{"word":"durable","ipa":"/ˈdjʊərəbəl/","tag":"resistant to wear","definition":"Resistant to wear. Durable is about physical toughness; sustainable is about not consuming what keeps the system alive.","definitionCN":"指耐磨、结实；durable 关乎物理强度，sustainable 关乎不消耗维持系统存活的东西。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"sustain + -able: able to be held up, hence able to keep going.","cn":"sustain + -able：托得住，因而撑得久。"},{"en":"The family runs sustain, sustainable, sustainability, sustained, sustenance, unsustainable.","cn":"同族词包括 sustain、sustainable、sustainability、sustained、sustenance、unsustainable。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases fix the range: sustainable development, sustainable growth, sustainable yield, sustainable energy.","cn":"固定搭配标定义域：可持续发展、可持续增长、可持续产量、可持续能源。"},{"en":"Sustainable fishing takes no more than what regrows.","cn":"可持续捕捞只取再生长的那部分。"},{"en":"A sustainable pace is one you can repeat tomorrow.","cn":"可持续的节奏是明天还能照做的节奏。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a tree that yields fruit every year because the picker never strips it bare.","cn":"想象一棵每年都结果的树，因为采摘者从不把它摘光。"},{"en":"Picture a runner keeping a pace slow enough to finish the whole race.","cn":"想象一位跑者把节奏放慢到足以跑完全程。"},{"en":"Picture a well that stays full because no one pumps more than the rain returns.","cn":"想象一口总也不见底的井，因为没人抽得比雨水回补更多。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The farm switched to sustainable practices that protect the topsoil.","cn":"这家农场改用保护表土的可持续做法。"},{"en":"Analysts doubted the project was financially sustainable without subsidies.","cn":"分析师怀疑没有补贴，这个项目在财务上是否可持续。"},{"en":"A sustainable workload keeps the whole team healthy year-round.","cn":"可持续的工作量让整个团队全年保持健康。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「sustain（维持）+ able（可……的）」——撑得住、耗不尽 → sustainable 可持续的","word":"sustainable"},"root":"拉丁 sustinere = sub-「自下」+ tenere「握住、保持」→ 古法语 sustenir → 英语 sustain + -able「可……的」。更深词根一般认为是印欧语 *ten-「伸展、保持」（重构形式）。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses share one test — can it keep going? — applied to nature, rates, growth, farming, materials, business, habits and harvests.","cn":"八个义项共用同一道考题——能否一直运转？——分别施于自然、速率、增长、农业、材料、商业、习惯与收成。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: something is held up from below so it can keep going without breaking.","cn":"核心意象：某物被从下方托住，得以持续运转而不垮。"},"chain":["HOLD FROM BELOW","KEEP THE RATE","DO NOT EXHAUST","REPLENISH THE SOURCE","PLAN FOR THE LONG TERM","OUTLAST THE SHORT TERM"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S4 · S8","en":"NATURAL RESOURCES: energy, farming and harvests do not deplete the base they draw on.","cn":"自然资源：能源、农业与收成不耗尽其所依托的根基。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"RATES AND GROWTH: paces, levels and expansions can be kept up without collapse.","cn":"速率与增长：节奏、水平与扩张可持续而不崩溃。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"MATERIALS AND BUILDINGS: products and structures are made and maintained at low environmental cost.","cn":"材料与建筑：产品与结构以低环境代价制造与维护。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"BUSINESS SURVIVAL: a model earns enough to keep operating over the long term.","cn":"商业生存：模式长期能赚到足以运营的收入。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"PERSONAL HABITS: a practice can be repeated without burning out.","cn":"个人习惯：做法可反复执行而不致枯竭。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Sustainable is sustain plus the adjective suffix -able: the Latin verb sustinere 'hold up from below' and the ending that says 'able to be'.","cn":"sustainable 是 sustain 加形容词词尾 -able：即拉丁动词 sustinere「自下托住」加「可……」的词尾。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin element is tenere 'to hold, keep' with sub- 'from below'; -able reached English through French from Latin -abilis. The same family includes tenable, retain and maintain.","cn":"拉丁成分是 tenere「握住、保持」加 sub-「自下」；-able 经法语源自拉丁 -abilis。同一词族还有 tenable、retain、maintain。"},"items":[{"word":"sustainable","structure":"sustain + -able (able to be)","meaning":"able to be continued without exhausting the base","meaningCN":"可持续的；不耗尽根基而能继续的","example":"They chose sustainable materials for the floors.","exampleCN":"他们为地板选择了可持续材料。"},{"word":"sustain","structure":"sub- (from below) + tenere (to hold)","meaning":"to hold up, keep in being","meaningCN":"托住；使维持","example":"The region cannot sustain its growing population.","exampleCN":"该地区无法养活不断增长的人口。"},{"word":"sustainability","structure":"sustain + -able + -ity (quality noun)","meaning":"the quality of being sustainable","meaningCN":"可持续性","example":"Sustainability shaped the company's product line.","exampleCN":"可持续性影响了公司的产品线。"},{"word":"sustained","structure":"sustain + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"kept going over time","meaningCN":"持续的；不间断的","example":"The team showed sustained effort all season.","exampleCN":"全队整个赛季都表现出持续的努力。"},{"word":"sustenance","structure":"sustain + -ance (that which)","meaning":"that which keeps life going","meaningCN":"食物；生计","example":"The refugees found sustenance in the mountain villages.","exampleCN":"难民在山村找到了食物与生计。"},{"word":"unsustainable","structure":"un- (not) + sustainable","meaning":"not able to be continued","meaningCN":"不可持续的","example":"The boom proved unsustainable.","exampleCN":"这场繁荣被证明不可持续。"},{"word":"tenable","structure":"tenere + -able (able to be)","meaning":"able to be held or defended","meaningCN":"站得住脚的；可辩护的","example":"The theory is tenable only with new evidence.","exampleCN":"只有在新的证据下，这个理论才站得住脚。"},{"word":"maintain","structure":"Latin manu tenere (to hold in hand) via Old French","meaning":"to keep in working order","meaningCN":"维持；保养","example":"Farmers maintain the terraces every spring.","exampleCN":"农民每年春天维护梯田。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"sustinere","structure":"sustinere, sustineo, sustinui, sustentum (second conjugation)","meaning":"to hold up, support, endure","meaningCN":"托住；支撑；承受"},{"word":"tenere","structure":"tenere, teneo, tenui, tentum (second conjugation)","meaning":"to hold, keep","meaningCN":"握住；保持"},{"word":"-abilis","structure":"-abilis, -abile (adjective suffix)","meaning":"able to be ...","meaningCN":"可……的"}]}},{"word":"systematic","ipa_uk":"/ˌsɪstəˈmætɪk/","ipa_us":"/ˌsɪstəˈmætɪk/","definition_zh":"系统的；有条理的；按固定方法进行的；（误差、风险等）系统性的；成体系的","definition_en":"done according to a fixed, orderly method that covers all parts, or relating to a system as a whole","core_image":"一张网格被一支笔从左上角起一格一格打勾，旁边一台机器内部每个齿轮都咬合着下一个齿轮","scene":"The library was arranged in a systematic order by subject.","sceneCN":"这里 systematic 是「有条理、按方法的」（第 1 个义项：按固定顺序而非随手摆放）；句意：图书馆按主题被整理成系统的顺序。图中可辨识物件：网格、逐格打勾的笔、齿轮组、互相咬合的轮齿、分类指示牌。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"系统的；有条理的；按固定方法进行的；（误差、风险等）系统性的；成体系的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"systematic approach","zh":"系统化的方法"},{"phrase":"systematic review","zh":"系统综述"},{"phrase":"systematic error","zh":"系统性误差"},{"phrase":"systematic search","zh":"系统搜查"},{"phrase":"systematic risk","zh":"系统性风险"},{"phrase":"systematic study","zh":"系统研究"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more systematic（更有条理的）"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most systematic（最有条理的）"},{"label":"副词形式","form":"systematically（系统地；有条理地）"},{"label":"动词形式","form":"systematize（使系统化）"},{"label":"名词（分类学）","form":"systematics（分类学）"},{"label":"名词（过程）","form":"systematization（系统化）"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"systematically","pos":"adv.","zh":"系统地（systematic + -ly「以……方式」，语义由「按系统的」偏移为「按系统方式地」）"},{"word":"system","pos":"n.","zh":"系统；体系（systematic 的词基，希腊 systēma「组合成整体」）"},{"word":"systemic","pos":"adj.","zh":"影响整个系统的（system + -ic，与 systematic 拼写相近但语义不同）"},{"word":"systematize","pos":"v.","zh":"使系统化（system + -ize「使成为」）"},{"word":"systematics","pos":"n.","zh":"分类学（system + -ics「……之学」）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Done by a fixed, orderly method","titleCN":"有条理的：按固定方法一步步进行","definition":"done according to a fixed plan or method rather than by chance or impulse","definitionCN":"按固定计划或方法进行，而非凭偶然或冲动","example":"She catalogued the samples in a systematic order.","exampleCN":"她按系统的顺序给样品编目。","why":"The Greek base systēma names an organized whole, so the adjective describes an action arranged into steps; the image is a sequence where every step has its place.","whyCN":"希腊词基 systēma 指「组织起来的整体」，因此该形容词描述被编排成步骤的动作；意象是一串每步都有位置的序列。"},{"no":"02","title":"Research methods that cover all studies","titleCN":"系统综述与研究：覆盖全部证据的研究方法","definition":"relating to a review or research method that collects and appraises all relevant studies on a question according to a preset protocol","definitionCN":"指按照预设方案收集并评价某个问题上全部相关研究的综述或研究方法","example":"A systematic review of forty trials found no clear benefit.","exampleCN":"一项涵盖四十项试验的系统综述没有发现明确益处。","why":"Evidence-based medicine made systematic review a named method in the late twentieth century: the word promises completeness and reproducibility rather than mere order.","whyCN":"循证医学在二十世纪后期把系统综述变成一种有名称的方法：该词承诺的是完整性与可复现性，而不只是有条理。"},{"no":"03","title":"Error built into the method itself","titleCN":"系统性误差与偏差：内建于方法本身的错误","definition":"describing an error or bias that recurs in every measurement because it is part of the method or instrument, not random","definitionCN":"指因为属于方法或仪器的一部分而在每次测量中重复出现、并非随机的误差或偏差","example":"The scale's zero drift caused systematic error in every reading.","exampleCN":"天平的零点漂移使每次读数都产生系统性误差。","why":"In statistics a systematic error points in the same direction every time, unlike random error; the adjective keeps its root meaning of built into the system.","whyCN":"在统计学中，系统性误差每次都偏向同一方向，不同于随机误差；该形容词保留「内建于系统」这一词根本义。"},{"no":"04","title":"Organized as a procedure or system","titleCN":"系统化的流程：被组织成程序","definition":"set up as a regular procedure, protocol or program rather than left to improvisation","definitionCN":"被设定为固定程序、规程或计划，而不是靠临时发挥","example":"The clinic introduced a systematic screening program for diabetes.","exampleCN":"这家诊所引入了系统化的糖尿病筛查计划。","why":"When institutions formalize a routine, the adjective describes the result: steps fixed in writing, repeated the same way each time. The system has been built on purpose.","whyCN":"机构把日常做法正式化时，该形容词描述其结果：步骤被写定，每次都按同一方式重复。系统是被有意建立起来的。"},{"no":"05","title":"An investigation that leaves nothing out","titleCN":"系统调查：不放过任何角落的彻底排查","definition":"thorough and organized, covering every part of a field or question in an orderly way","definitionCN":"彻底而有条理，按顺序覆盖某个领域或问题的每一个部分","example":"Detectives carried out a systematic search of the warehouse.","exampleCN":"侦探对仓库进行了系统搜查。","why":"Here the sense approaches thorough: a systematic search follows a grid so no area is missed. The method guarantees completeness.","whyCN":"此处义项接近「彻底」：系统搜查按网格推进，任何区域都不会漏掉。方法保证了完整性。"},{"no":"06","title":"The science of classifying life","titleCN":"分类学的：按亲缘关系归类生物","definition":"relating to the scientific classification and naming of organisms by their evolutionary relationships","definitionCN":"指按演化亲缘关系对生物进行分类与命名的科学","example":"Systematic botany groups plants by shared ancestry.","exampleCN":"系统植物学按共同祖先对植物分组。","why":"In biology the adjective and its noun systematics became the name of classification itself: arranging living things into an ordered whole, the original Greek meaning revived.","whyCN":"在生物学中，该形容词及其名词 systematics 成为分类学本身的名称：把生物编排成一个有秩序的整体，复活了希腊语的本义。"},{"no":"07","title":"Harm built into an institution","titleCN":"系统性侵害：被制度化的伤害","definition":"describing abuse, oppression or discrimination that is organized and repeated as part of an institution's normal practice","definitionCN":"指作为机构日常做法的一部分而被组织化、反复实施的虐待、压迫或歧视","example":"The inquiry documented systematic abuse in the detention centers.","exampleCN":"调查记录了拘留中心存在的系统性虐待。","why":"In law and journalism the word marks harm that is not a few bad individuals but a pattern the institution itself produces; the system here is the organization.","whyCN":"在法律与新闻中，该词标记的不是个别坏人，而是机构本身产生的模式化伤害；这里的「系统」就是该组织。"},{"no":"08","title":"Risk that hits the whole market","titleCN":"金融系统性风险：波及整个市场的风险","definition":"in finance, describing risk that comes from factors affecting the whole market and cannot be removed by diversifying within it","definitionCN":"在金融中指来自影响整个市场的因素、无法通过市场内分散投资消除的风险","example":"Systematic risk is why diversification cannot eliminate all losses.","exampleCN":"系统性风险正是分散投资也无法消除全部损失的原因。","why":"Finance borrowed the word for the risk carried by every asset at once; note that systemic risk, a related but distinct term, means the risk of the whole system collapsing.","whyCN":"金融界借用该词指同时压在每个资产上的风险；注意与之相近但不同的 systemic risk，后者指整个系统崩溃的风险。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Systematic comes from Late Latin systematicus, taken from Greek systēmatikos, an adjective of systēma 'a composite whole', built on syn- 'together' and histanai 'to place, set up'. The deeper root is reconstructed as Indo-European *sta- 'to stand'. The exact first English citation is uncertain.","cn":"systematic 出自晚期拉丁 systematicus，源自希腊 systēmatikos，它是 systēma「组合成的整体」的形容词；systēma 由 syn-「一起」与 histanai「放置、使站立」构成。更深词根被重构为印欧语 *sta-「站立」。其英语最早书证年代存疑。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK SYSTĒMA","en":"Greek systēma 'a composite whole, an organized body' was formed from syn- 'together' and histanai 'to place, set up, cause to stand'.","cn":"希腊语 systēma「组合成的整体、有组织的整体」由 syn-「一起」与 histanai「放置、使站立」构成。"},{"era":"GREEK SYSTĒMATIKOS","en":"The adjective systēmatikos meant 'of or relating to a system, arranged into a whole'.","cn":"形容词 systēmatikos 意为「与系统有关的、被编排成整体的」。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN SYSTEMATICUS","en":"Late Latin adopted the Greek adjective as systematicus, and English took the word through that line, with French systématique also contributing in the early modern period.","cn":"晚期拉丁把这一希腊形容词接纳为 systematicus；英语经由这条线索借入，近代早期的法语 systématique 也起了作用。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ARRIVAL","en":"Systematic entered English in the early modern period in learned prose about method and arrangement; its exact first citation is uncertain.","cn":"systematic 在近代早期进入英语，最初见于讨论方法与编排的学术散文；其最早书证年代存疑。"},{"era":"SCIENTIFIC AND SOCIAL SPREAD","en":"In the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries the word spread through taxonomy, medicine, philosophy and social reform; the twentieth century added systematic review, systematic error and systematic risk.","cn":"十八、十九世纪，该词在分类学、医学、哲学与社会改革中扩散；二十世纪又增加了系统综述、系统性误差与系统性风险。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"The exact first English citation of systematic is uncertain. The deeper root of histanai is reconstructed as Indo-European *sta- 'to stand', a reconstruction rather than a recorded form.","cn":"首见年代存疑：systematic 的英语最早书证年代不确定。重构形式：histanai 的更深词根被重构为印欧语 *sta-「站立」，属重构形式，而非有记录的真实词形。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group separates the system family by part of speech and use; the second contrasts systematic with near-synonyms, since systematic means following a complete, orderly method.","cn":"第一组按词性与用法区分 system 词族；第二组将 systematic 与近义词对照，因为 systematic 指遵循完整、有条理的方法。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"systemic","ipa":"/sɪˈstemɪk/","tag":"affecting the whole","definition":"Affecting the whole system. Systematic is about method and order; systemic is about spread through the entire system, as in systemic disease or systemic risk.","definitionCN":"指影响整个系统的；systematic 关乎方法与条理，systemic 关乎扩散到整个系统，如全身性疾病或系统性风险。"},{"word":"system","ipa":"/ˈsɪstəm/","tag":"noun","definition":"The organized whole itself. Systematic is the adjective describing action arranged by that whole.","definitionCN":"指组织起来的整体本身；systematic 是描述按该整体编排之动作的形容词。"},{"word":"systematize","ipa":"/ˈsɪstəmətaɪz/","tag":"verb","definition":"To arrange into a system. Systematic describes the state or method; systematize is the act of producing it.","definitionCN":"指把……编排成系统；systematic 描述状态或方法，systematize 是产生它的动作。"},{"word":"systematics","ipa":"/ˌsɪstəˈmætɪks/","tag":"noun of classification","definition":"The science of classification. It is a noun, while systematic is the adjective.","definitionCN":"指分类学，是名词；systematic 是相应的形容词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"methodical","ipa":"/məˈθɒdɪkəl/","tag":"orderly and careful","definition":"Orderly and careful. Methodical stresses care and order; systematic stresses a named, complete method that covers everything.","definitionCN":"指有条理而细致；methodical 强调细心与秩序，systematic 强调有名称、覆盖一切的完整方法。"},{"word":"organized","ipa":"/ˈɔːɡənaɪzd/","tag":"arranged into a whole","definition":"Arranged into a working whole. Organized describes the result; systematic describes following an explicit plan to reach it.","definitionCN":"指被编排成能运转的整体；organized 描述结果，systematic 描述为达到结果而遵循明确计划。"},{"word":"thorough","ipa":"/ˈθʌrə/","tag":"complete coverage","definition":"Complete, leaving nothing out. Thorough is about completeness of coverage; systematic adds that the coverage follows a fixed order.","definitionCN":"指完整、无遗漏；thorough 关乎覆盖的完整性，systematic 还要求覆盖遵循固定顺序。"},{"word":"deliberate","ipa":"/dɪˈlɪbərət/","tag":"done on purpose","definition":"Done on purpose. Deliberate marks intention; systematic adds that the intention is built into an organized practice, as in systematic abuse.","definitionCN":"指有意的；deliberate 标记意图，systematic 还表示意图被内建于有组织的做法，如系统性侵害。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real collocations and real relatives, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的构词成分、真实搭配与真实同族词，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"system + -atic: of, or arranged like, a system.","cn":"system + -atic：属于系统的，或被编排得像系统一样。"},{"en":"The family runs system, systematic, systemic, systematize, systematics, systematization, subsystem, unsystematic.","cn":"同族词包括 system、systematic、systemic、systematize、systematics、systematization、subsystem、unsystematic。"},{"en":"Fixed phrases fix the technical uses: systematic review, systematic error, systematic risk, systematic search.","cn":"固定搭配固定了技术义项：系统综述、系统性误差、系统性风险、系统搜查。"},{"en":"Systematic means following the method; systemic means spreading through the whole system.","cn":"systematic 指遵循方法，systemic 指扩散到整个系统。"},{"en":"A systematic worker ticks every box in order; a sloppy one ticks boxes at random.","cn":"有条理的人按顺序逐个打勾，马虎的人随手乱勾。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a grid of boxes being ticked one by one from corner to corner.","cn":"想象一张网格，从一角开始一格一格被勾完。"},{"en":"Picture a net that is dragged across the whole pond so no fish escapes.","cn":"想象一张被拖过整个池塘的网，没有一条鱼能漏掉。"},{"en":"Picture a clockwork where every gear turns the next, with no part left to chance.","cn":"想象一架每个齿轮都带动下一个的钟表机件，没有任何部件靠运气。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The archive was rebuilt in a systematic order by year and by author.","cn":"档案馆按年份与作者被重新整理成系统的顺序。"},{"en":"A systematic review of the evidence changed the treatment guidelines.","cn":"对证据的系统综述改变了治疗指南。"},{"en":"Systematic errors in the sensors skewed every reading in the same direction.","cn":"传感器的系统性误差让每次读数都偏向同一方向。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「system（系统）+ atic」——一切都放进格子、按序打勾 → systematic 系统的、有条理的","word":"systematic"},"root":"希腊 systēma = syn-「一起」+ histanai「放置、使站立」→ systēmatikos → 晚期拉丁 systematicus → 英语 systematic。更深词根为重构的印欧语 *sta-「站立」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses move from ordered method to complete research coverage, built-in error, formalized procedures, thorough searches, classification science, institutional abuse and market-wide risk.","cn":"八个义项从有条理的方法，扩展到完整的研究覆盖、内建误差、正式化程序、彻底搜查、分类科学、机构性侵害与市场级风险。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: parts are set together into one whole, then every step of the plan is followed in order.","cn":"核心意象：各部分被放置成一个整体，随后计划的每一步都被按序执行。"},"chain":["SET PARTS TOGETHER","FIX THE ORDER","FOLLOW EVERY STEP","COVER ALL PARTS","BUILD IT INTO THE MACHINE","SPREAD THROUGH THE WHOLE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S4","en":"METHODICAL ACTION: work and procedures follow a fixed, step-by-step order.","cn":"有条理的行动：工作与程序遵循固定的分步顺序。"},{"senses":"S2 · S6","en":"RESEARCH AND TAXONOMY: reviews and classifications cover all relevant material by design.","cn":"研究与分类学：综述与分类按设计覆盖全部相关材料。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"BUILT-IN FAULT: error recurs because it belongs to the method itself.","cn":"内建缺陷：误差因属于方法本身而反复出现。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"THOROUGH COVERAGE: a search or inquiry leaves no part of the field untouched.","cn":"彻底覆盖：搜查或调查不让领域的任何部分被遗漏。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"INSTITUTIONAL AND MARKET SCALE: abuse and risk are produced by design across the whole system.","cn":"机构与市场尺度：侵害与风险被有意地产生于整个系统。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Systematic is the Greek noun systēma 'composite whole' plus the adjective ending -ikos, which reached English through Late Latin -icus: syn- 'together' + histanai 'to place' + -ikos.","cn":"systematic 是希腊名词 systēma「组合成的整体」加形容词词尾 -ikos，经晚期拉丁 -icus 进入英语：即 syn-「一起」+ histanai「放置」+ -ikos。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin layer is systematicus, a Late Latin adaptation of Greek systēmatikos; Latin only carried the word, so the base is Greek, not Latin. The Greek root histanai goes back to the reconstructed Indo-European *sta- 'to stand'.","cn":"拉丁层是 systematicus，即晚期拉丁对希腊 systēmatikos 的转写；拉丁只是中介，词基属于希腊语而非拉丁语。希腊 histanai 的更深词根是重构的印欧语 *sta-「站立」。"},"items":[{"word":"systematic","structure":"systēma + -ikos (adjective suffix)","meaning":"arranged into a methodical whole","meaningCN":"被编排成有条理整体的","example":"They kept systematic notes during the trial.","exampleCN":"他们在试验期间做了系统笔记。"},{"word":"system","structure":"syn- (together) + histanai (to set up)","meaning":"an organized whole of parts","meaningCN":"组织起来的整体","example":"The immune system defends the body.","exampleCN":"免疫系统保卫身体。"},{"word":"systematize","structure":"system + -ize (to make)","meaning":"to arrange into a system","meaningCN":"使系统化","example":"The librarian systematized the loose files.","exampleCN":"图书管理员把散乱的档案系统化。"},{"word":"systematics","structure":"system + -ics (field of study)","meaning":"the science of classification","meaningCN":"分类学","example":"Molecular systematics rewrote the plant family tree.","exampleCN":"分子分类学重写了植物谱系。"},{"word":"systemic","structure":"system + -ic (adjective)","meaning":"affecting the whole system","meaningCN":"影响整个系统的","example":"The drug has systemic effects on the body.","exampleCN":"这种药对全身有系统性影响。"},{"word":"systematization","structure":"systematize + -ation (action noun)","meaning":"the act of arranging into a system","meaningCN":"系统化的过程","example":"The systematization of the rules took a full year.","exampleCN":"规则的系统化花了一整年。"},{"word":"subsystem","structure":"sub- (under) + system","meaning":"a system within a larger system","meaningCN":"子系统","example":"The cooling subsystem failed first.","exampleCN":"冷却子系统最先失灵。"},{"word":"unsystematic","structure":"un- (not) + systematic","meaning":"not arranged by a method","meaningCN":"不成系统的","example":"Unsystematic notes are hard to reuse.","exampleCN":"不成系统的笔记很难复用。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"systematicus","structure":"Late Latin, from Greek systēmatikos","meaning":"arranged into a system","meaningCN":"被编排成系统的"},{"word":"systema","structure":"systema, systematis (n., from Greek)","meaning":"a composite whole, an organized body","meaningCN":"组合成的整体；有组织的整体"},{"word":"-icus","structure":"-icus, -ica, -icum (adjective suffix)","meaning":"belonging to, pertaining to","meaningCN":"属于……的"}]}}]);
